    {"id":"m-outbox-published-without-local-commit","kind":"temporal","models":"arc-105","statement":"An event committed by another writer, with no commit hook of this runtime, is published by the idle sweep.","evaluate":{"method":"eventually","scenarios":["arc-idle-sweep-publishes-foreign-commit"],"occurs":{"event":"arc-ob-published"},"negatives":[{"scenario":"arc-idle-sweep-publishes-foreign-commit","faults":["arc-idle-sweep-disabled"]}]},"faultModel":"fault-model-launch","assumptions":["a-model-abstraction","a-database-commit"],"faultBasis":"fault"},
    {"id":"ldg-001","kind":"requirement","statement":"An account of the ledger SHALL be identified by one owner, a principal of the tenant or a named pool of the tenant, one unit that the tenant has declared, and one scope that the poster chooses, empty by default.","rationale":"Two owners with one unit, or one owner with two units, are two accounts. An account with no owner or no unit has nothing to count for.","evaluate":{"method":"property"},"ref":"LDG-001","area":"10-product","section":"Accounts and units","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`ledger account`","traces":["g-600","d-5000","d-5001","d-6551"],"milestone":11,"inSection":"sec-ledger-2","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"ldg-002","kind":"requirement","statement":"A posting that names a unit that the tenant has not declared SHALL be refused and change nothing.","rationale":"A misspelt unit would otherwise open an account of its own that nobody counts.","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"LDG-002","area":"10-product","section":"Accounts and units","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`unit`","traces":["g-600","d-5001"],"milestone":11,"inSection":"sec-ledger-2","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"ldg-003","kind":"requirement","statement":"A posting with an amount that is zero, or is not a whole number, SHALL be refused.","rationale":"An entry of zero records nothing, and a fraction cannot be added without the rounding that makes a balance depend on the order of the entries.","evaluate":{"method":"property"},"ref":"LDG-003","area":"10-product","section":"Accounts and units","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`amount`","traces":["g-601","d-5004","d-5013"],"milestone":11,"inSection":"sec-ledger-2","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"ldg-004","kind":"requirement","statement":"A posting that names a principal that the tenant does not have, or a pool that the tenant has not declared, SHALL be refused and change nothing.","rationale":"A misspelt owner would otherwise open an account of its own that nobody counts.","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"LDG-004","area":"10-product","section":"Accounts and units","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`owner`","traces":["g-600","d-5001"],"milestone":11,"inSection":"sec-ledger-2","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"ldg-005","kind":"requirement","statement":"An entry SHALL record its amount, its idempotency key, its reason, the principal that caused it and the time that was given to the decision as an input.","rationale":"The entry alone must explain a balance: how much, why, who and when, with a key that lets a retry be told from a second posting.","evaluate":{"method":"property"},"ref":"LDG-005","area":"10-product","section":"Postings","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`ledger entry`","traces":["g-600","k-11","d-5010"],"milestone":11,"inSection":"sec-ledger-3","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"ldg-006","kind":"requirement","statement":"A posting that repeats an idempotency key of its account with the same amount, reason and correction SHALL answer with the entry that the first posting recorded and change the balance once.","rationale":"A retry, a redelivered message and a double click all repeat a key. Each must change the balance once.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"LDG-006","area":"10-product","section":"Postings","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`idempotency key`","traces":["g-603","d-5007","k-11"],"milestone":11,"inSection":"sec-ledger-3","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"ldg-007","kind":"requirement","statement":"A posting that repeats an idempotency key of its account with another amount, reason or correction SHALL be refused and change nothing.","rationale":"A key that means two things hides a defect in the poster, and applying either meaning would be a guess.","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"LDG-007","area":"10-product","section":"Postings","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`idempotency key`","traces":["g-603","d-5007"],"milestone":11,"inSection":"sec-ledger-3","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"ldg-008","kind":"requirement","statement":"The kernel SHALL decide a posting from the snapshot, the posting, the context and the time it is given, and from nothing else.","rationale":"A decision that reads a clock or a source of randomness cannot be simulated or replayed (K-1, K-11), and a journal that cannot be replayed cannot be checked.","evaluate":{"method":"property"},"ref":"LDG-008","area":"10-product","section":"Postings","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`decide-ledger-posting`","traces":["k-1","k-11","d-5006","d-5010"],"milestone":11,"inSection":"sec-ledger-3","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"ldg-009","kind":"requirement","statement":"A posting SHALL be committed in the same transaction as the change that causes it.","rationale":"A change and the points it earned are one fact. A crash between them would give points for nothing or take points for nothing.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"LDG-009","area":"10-product","section":"Postings","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-2","boundaryDetail":"`commit`","traces":["g-600","k-9","d-5006"],"milestone":11,"inSection":"sec-ledger-3","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"ldg-029","kind":"requirement","statement":"A change that rolls back SHALL leave no entry in the ledger.","rationale":"Points for a change that did not happen cannot be explained to the person who has them.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"LDG-029","area":"10-product","section":"Postings","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-2","boundaryDetail":"`commit`","traces":["g-600","k-9","d-5006"],"milestone":11,"inSection":"sec-ledger-3","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"ldg-010","kind":"requirement","statement":"The commit that records an entry SHALL record exactly one domain event, ledger-entry-posted, for that entry.","rationale":"A trigger subscribed to the posting must see each entry once, and no event may report an entry that was rolled back (SCH-004, RUN-005).","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"LDG-010","area":"10-product","section":"Postings","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-2","boundaryDetail":"`ledger-entry-posted`","traces":["g-604","d-5008"],"milestone":11,"inSection":"sec-ledger-3","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"ldg-011","kind":"requirement","statement":"The tenant SHALL be able to declare for a unit, and for one account of it, a floor, a cap and a cap per period.","rationale":"A floor of zero keeps a balance from going negative, a cap bounds a pool such as a promotion budget, and a cap per period bounds what can be earned in a day.","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"LDG-011","area":"10-product","section":"Limits","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`ledger limit`","traces":["g-602","d-5005"],"milestone":11,"inSection":"sec-ledger-4","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"ldg-012","kind":"requirement","statement":"A limit declared for an account SHALL take the place of the limit declared for its unit, limit by limit.","rationale":"A tenant sets a default for a unit and an exception for one account without restating the other limits of the unit.","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"LDG-012","area":"10-product","section":"Limits","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`ledger limit`","traces":["g-602","d-5005"],"milestone":11,"inSection":"sec-ledger-4","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"ldg-013","kind":"requirement","statement":"A posting that would leave a balance below its floor or above its cap, and does not move a balance that is already outside the limit back toward it, SHALL be refused and change nothing.","rationale":"A limit that a posting can pass is a hint. A refusal that leaves half of its effect behind is a second defect.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"LDG-013","area":"10-product","section":"Limits","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`ledger limit`","traces":["g-602","d-5005","k-11"],"milestone":11,"inSection":"sec-ledger-4","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"ldg-014","kind":"requirement","statement":"A posting that would take the credits posted in one period above the cap per period SHALL be refused and change nothing.","rationale":"The cap per period is what bounds earning in a day or a month, whatever the balance is.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"LDG-014","area":"10-product","section":"Limits","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`cap per period`","traces":["g-602","d-5005"],"milestone":11,"inSection":"sec-ledger-4","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"ldg-015","kind":"requirement","statement":"The period of a cap per period SHALL be the calendar hour, day, week or month, in UTC, that contains the time of the entry.","rationale":"A period computed from the time that is an input gives the same period when the journal is replayed, whenever it is replayed.","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"LDG-015","area":"10-product","section":"Limits","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`period`","traces":["g-602","d-5005","d-5010","k-11"],"milestone":11,"inSection":"sec-ledger-4","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"ldg-016","kind":"requirement","statement":"A change of a limit SHALL apply to the postings committed after it and change no entry and no balance.","rationale":"A limit lowered below a balance must not rewrite the history that the balance was made of.","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"LDG-016","area":"10-product","section":"Limits","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`ledger limit`","traces":["g-601","g-602","d-5005"],"milestone":11,"inSection":"sec-ledger-4","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"ldg-017","kind":"requirement","statement":"Of two concurrent postings to one account that together would pass a cap, exactly one SHALL be refused.","rationale":"Two postings that each fit alone but not together are the case that a check made before the commit gets wrong.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"LDG-017","area":"10-product","section":"Concurrent postings","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-2","boundaryDetail":"`ledger limit`","traces":["g-602","d-5009","k-100"],"milestone":11,"inSection":"sec-ledger-5","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"ldg-018","kind":"requirement","statement":"A posting that lost a commit race to another posting of its account and still passes every limit after the winner SHALL be applied.","rationale":"A refusal of a posting that fits turns every busy moment into lost points.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"LDG-018","area":"10-product","section":"Concurrent postings","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-2","boundaryDetail":"`commit`","traces":["g-602","d-5009"],"milestone":11,"inSection":"sec-ledger-5","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"ldg-019","kind":"requirement","statement":"The entries of an account SHALL be numbered 1, 2, 3 in the order they commit, with no gap and no repeat.","rationale":"A gap is how a replay finds an entry that was lost, and a repeat is how it finds one that was written twice.","evaluate":{"method":"property"},"ref":"LDG-019","area":"10-product","section":"Concurrent postings","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-2","boundaryDetail":"`ledger entry`","traces":["g-601","d-5002","d-5009"],"milestone":11,"inSection":"sec-ledger-5","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"ldg-020","kind":"requirement","statement":"The balance of an account SHALL equal the sum of the amounts of its entries after the journal of the tenant is replayed.","rationale":"A stored sum that differs from the entries is a defect, and the replay is the way to find it.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"LDG-020","area":"10-product","section":"Balance and journal","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-2","boundaryDetail":"`ledger balance`","traces":["g-601","d-5003","k-11"],"milestone":11,"inSection":"sec-ledger-6","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"ldg-021","kind":"requirement","statement":"No operation of the platform or of a tenant SHALL set the balance of an account.","rationale":"A balance that someone can write is a balance that nobody can explain.","evaluate":{"method":"property"},"ref":"LDG-021","area":"10-product","section":"Balance and journal","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`ledger balance`","traces":["g-601","d-5003"],"milestone":11,"inSection":"sec-ledger-6","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"ldg-022","kind":"requirement","statement":"No operation of the platform or of a tenant SHALL change or remove an entry.","rationale":"An append-only journal is what lets a person who disputes a balance be shown every step of it.","evaluate":{"method":"property"},"ref":"LDG-022","area":"10-product","section":"Balance and journal","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-2","boundaryDetail":"`ledger entry`","traces":["g-601","d-5002"],"milestone":11,"inSection":"sec-ledger-6","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"ldg-023","kind":"requirement","statement":"A correction of an entry SHALL be a new entry that names the entry it corrects.","rationale":"The error and its correction both stay in the journal, and the correction can be found from the error.","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"LDG-023","area":"10-product","section":"Balance and journal","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`corrects`","traces":["g-601","d-5002"],"milestone":11,"inSection":"sec-ledger-6","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"ldg-024","kind":"requirement","statement":"A read of the entries of an account SHALL return only the entries that the policies of the reader permit.","rationale":"A ledger is read like any other record, and an entry that a reader may not see must not reach them (KRN-004).","evaluate":{"method":"property"},"ref":"LDG-024","area":"10-product","section":"Reads","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`list-ledger-entries`","traces":["g-604","g-20","d-5011"],"milestone":11,"inSection":"sec-ledger-7","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"ldg-025","kind":"requirement","statement":"A read of the balance of an account SHALL count only the entries that the policies of the reader permit.","rationale":"A total that includes an entry the reader may not see discloses that entry to anyone who can subtract.","evaluate":{"method":"property"},"ref":"LDG-025","area":"10-product","section":"Reads","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`read-ledger-balance`","traces":["g-604","g-20","d-5011"],"milestone":11,"inSection":"sec-ledger-7","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"ldg-026","kind":"requirement","statement":"A read of a ledger by a principal that does not hold the capability to read the ledger SHALL be refused.","rationale":"The capability is what a tenant grants to a role, as it grants the right to read records.","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"LDG-026","area":"10-product","section":"Reads","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`ledger-read`","traces":["g-604","d-5011"],"milestone":11,"inSection":"sec-ledger-7","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"ldg-027","kind":"requirement","statement":"The erasure of a principal SHALL clear that principal from the accounts it owns and from the entries it caused, as the retention rules of those records say.","rationale":"The identity of a person is personal data; the number of points counted for nobody is not (K-350).","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"LDG-027","area":"10-product","section":"Erasure","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-350","boundaryDetail":"`erasure request`","traces":["g-604","g-350","k-350","d-5012"],"milestone":11,"inSection":"sec-ledger-8","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"ldg-028","kind":"requirement","statement":"The erasure of a principal SHALL leave every entry, every amount and every balance of the tenant unchanged apart from the fields that name that principal.","rationale":"The totals of pools, and the explanation of every balance, must survive the erasure of one person.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"LDG-028","area":"10-product","section":"Erasure","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-350","boundaryDetail":"`erasure request`","traces":["g-604","g-601","d-5012"],"milestone":11,"inSection":"sec-ledger-8","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"m-ledger-posting-once-per-key","kind":"invariant","models":"ldg-006","statement":"However often a posting with one key arrives, the entries of the account are as many as the keys that were applied.","evaluate":{"method":"state-invariant","scenarios":["ledger-posting-retried","ledger-posting-delivered-twice"],"expr":"ledger-posting-flow.entries == ledger-posting-flow.keysApplied","negatives":[{"scenario":"ledger-posting-retried","faults":["defect-ledger-dup-applies-again"]},{"scenario":"ledger-posting-delivered-twice","faults":["defect-ledger-dup-applies-again"]}]},"faultModel":"fault-model-launch","assumptions":["a-model-abstraction"],"faultBasis":"fault"},
    {"id":"m-ledger-answers-repeated-key","kind":"temporal","models":"ldg-006","statement":"A posting that repeats a recorded key is answered from the entry of that key.","evaluate":{"method":"eventually","scenarios":["ledger-posting-retried"],"occurs":{"event":"ldg-post-replayed"},"negatives":[{"scenario":"ledger-posting-retried","faults":["defect-ledger-dup-applies-again"]}]},"faultModel":"fault-model-launch","assumptions":["a-model-abstraction"],"faultBasis":"fault"},
    {"id":"m-ledger-balance-within-limits","kind":"invariant","models":"ldg-013","statement":"The balance of the account is never below its floor and never above its cap, whatever is posted.","evaluate":{"method":"state-invariant","scenarios":["ledger-posting-past-limits"],"expr":"ledger-posting-flow.floor <= ledger-posting-flow.balance && ledger-posting-flow.balance <= ledger-posting-flow.cap","negatives":[{"scenario":"ledger-posting-past-limits","faults":["defect-ledger-cap-ignored"]},{"scenario":"ledger-posting-past-limits","faults":["defect-ledger-floor-ignored"]}]},"faultModel":"fault-model-launch","assumptions":["a-model-abstraction"],"faultBasis":"fault"},
    {"id":"m-ledger-over-cap-refused","kind":"temporal","models":"ldg-013","statement":"A posting that would pass the cap is refused naming the cap.","evaluate":{"method":"eventually","scenarios":["ledger-posting-past-limits"],"occurs":{"event":"ldg-refused-cap"},"negatives":[{"scenario":"ledger-posting-past-limits","faults":["ledger-cap-refusal-disabled"]}]},"faultModel":"fault-model-launch","assumptions":["a-model-abstraction"],"faultBasis":"fault"},
    {"id":"m-ledger-below-floor-refused","kind":"temporal","models":"ldg-013","statement":"A posting that would pass the floor is refused naming the floor.","evaluate":{"method":"eventually","scenarios":["ledger-posting-past-limits"],"occurs":{"event":"ldg-refused-floor"},"negatives":[{"scenario":"ledger-posting-past-limits","faults":["ledger-floor-refusal-disabled"]}]},"faultModel":"fault-model-launch","assumptions":["a-model-abstraction"],"faultBasis":"fault"},
    {"id":"m-ledger-balance-not-writable","kind":"invariant","models":"ldg-021","statement":"The balance of the account equals what its entries add up to, even when a request arrives to set it.","evaluate":{"method":"state-invariant","scenarios":["ledger-posting-retried"],"expr":"ledger-posting-flow.balance == ledger-posting-flow.journal","negatives":[{"scenario":"ledger-posting-retried","faults":["defect-ledger-balance-set"]}]},"faultModel":"fault-model-launch","assumptions":["a-model-abstraction"],"faultBasis":"fault"},
    {"id":"m-ledger-replay-equals-balance","kind":"invariant","models":"ldg-020","statement":"The balance that a replay of the journal gives equals the balance of the account.","evaluate":{"method":"state-invariant","scenarios":["ledger-posting-retried"],"expr":"ledger-posting-flow.replayed == -1 || ledger-posting-flow.replayed == ledger-posting-flow.balance","negatives":[{"scenario":"ledger-posting-retried","faults":["defect-ledger-replay-drops-last"]}]},"faultModel":"fault-model-launch","assumptions":["a-model-abstraction"],"faultBasis":"fault"},
    {"id":"m-ledger-race-never-passes-cap","kind":"invariant","models":"ldg-017","statement":"The balance never passes the cap, however two posters race.","evaluate":{"method":"state-invariant","scenarios":["ledger-two-postings-race-a-cap","ledger-two-postings-race-and-fit"],"expr":"ledger-concurrent-flow.balance <= ledger-concurrent-flow.cap","negatives":[{"scenario":"ledger-two-postings-race-a-cap","faults":["defect-ledger-commit-unguarded"]}]},"faultModel":"fault-model-launch","assumptions":["a-model-abstraction"],"faultBasis":"fault"},
    {"id":"m-ledger-race-one-is-refused","kind":"temporal","models":"ldg-017","statement":"Of two postings that together pass the cap, one is refused.","evaluate":{"method":"eventually","scenarios":["ledger-two-postings-race-a-cap"],"occurs":{"event":"ldg-race-refused"},"negatives":[{"scenario":"ledger-two-postings-race-a-cap","faults":["ledger-race-refusal-disabled"]}]},"faultModel":"fault-model-launch","assumptions":["a-model-abstraction"],"faultBasis":"fault"},
    {"id":"m-ledger-race-exactly-one-posted","kind":"invariant","models":"ldg-017","statement":"Of two postings that together pass the cap, at most one is committed and at most one is refused.","evaluate":{"method":"state-invariant","scenarios":["ledger-two-postings-race-a-cap"],"expr":"ledger-concurrent-flow.posted <= 1 && ledger-concurrent-flow.refused <= 1","negatives":[{"scenario":"ledger-two-postings-race-a-cap","faults":["defect-ledger-commit-unguarded"]}]},"faultModel":"fault-model-launch","assumptions":["a-model-abstraction"],"faultBasis":"fault"},
    {"id":"m-ledger-race-loser-that-fits-is-applied","kind":"invariant","models":"ldg-018","statement":"A posting that loses a race and still fits after the winner is not refused.","evaluate":{"method":"state-invariant","scenarios":["ledger-two-postings-race-and-fit"],"expr":"ledger-concurrent-flow.refused == 0","negatives":[{"scenario":"ledger-two-postings-race-and-fit","faults":["defect-ledger-conflict-refuses"]}]},"faultModel":"fault-model-launch","assumptions":["a-model-abstraction"],"faultBasis":"fault"},
    {"id":"m-ledger-posting-with-its-change","kind":"invariant","models":"ldg-009","statement":"The entries exist for the changes that committed: a commit records its entry in the same step.","evaluate":{"method":"state-invariant","scenarios":["ledger-change-commits"],"expr":"ledger-commit-flow.entries == ledger-commit-flow.changes","negatives":[{"scenario":"ledger-change-commits","faults":["defect-ledger-posting-after-commit"]}]},"faultModel":"fault-model-launch","assumptions":["a-model-abstraction"],"faultBasis":"fault"},
    {"id":"m-ledger-rolled-back-change-leaves-no-entry","kind":"invariant","models":"ldg-029","statement":"A change that rolls back leaves no entry: the entries are as many as the changes that committed.","evaluate":{"method":"state-invariant","scenarios":["ledger-change-rolls-back"],"expr":"ledger-commit-flow.entries == ledger-commit-flow.changes","negatives":[{"scenario":"ledger-change-rolls-back","faults":["defect-ledger-rollback-posts"]}]},"faultModel":"fault-model-launch","assumptions":["a-model-abstraction"],"faultBasis":"fault"},
    {"id":"m-ledger-committed-change-posts","kind":"temporal","models":"ldg-009","statement":"A committed change records its entry.","evaluate":{"method":"eventually","scenarios":["ledger-change-commits"],"occurs":{"event":"ledger-entry-posted"},"negatives":[{"scenario":"ledger-change-commits","faults":["ledger-commit-disabled"]}]},"faultModel":"fault-model-launch","assumptions":["a-model-abstraction"],"faultBasis":"restatement"},
    {"id":"m-ledger-one-event-per-entry","kind":"invariant","models":"ldg-010","statement":"The domain events published are exactly as many as the entries recorded.","evaluate":{"method":"state-invariant","scenarios":["ledger-change-commits","ledger-change-rolls-back"],"expr":"ledger-commit-flow.published == ledger-commit-flow.entries","negatives":[{"scenario":"ledger-change-rolls-back","faults":["defect-ledger-rollback-publishes"]}]},"faultModel":"fault-model-launch","assumptions":["a-model-abstraction"],"faultBasis":"fault"},
    {"id":"seg-001","kind":"requirement","statement":"A segment SHALL be stored as tenant metadata under the schema version, holding a name, a subject object type, a predicate and a version number.","rationale":"A segment is data, so it is versioned, projected and exported with the tenant, and no tenant code runs (NG-3).","evaluate":{"method":"property"},"ref":"SEG-001","area":"04-automation","section":"Definition","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-7","boundaryDetail":"`segment`","traces":["g-605","d-5020"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-segments-2","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"seg-002","kind":"requirement","statement":"A segment predicate SHALL be written in the tenant rule language and SHALL read only the principal and the roles of the person, the balances of the person's ledger accounts, the fields of the person's record of the subject type, the fields of records reached from it through at most two reference fields, and the time that the decision is given.","rationale":"This is the whole context that the kernel loads for one person, so the cost of one evaluation is known when the segment is defined.","evaluate":{"method":"property"},"ref":"SEG-002","area":"04-automation","section":"Definition","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-7","boundaryDetail":"`segment predicate`","traces":["g-605","g-608","d-5021","d-6544"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-segments-2","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"seg-003","kind":"requirement","statement":"A segment definition whose predicate fails to parse, or uses a construct that the tenant rule language does not declare, SHALL be refused with the position of the error.","rationale":"A tenant writes predicates in the language it already knows, and a mistake is found before any person is evaluated.","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"SEG-003","area":"04-automation","section":"Definition","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-7","boundaryDetail":"`define-segment`","traces":["g-605","d-5020"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-segments-2","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"seg-004","kind":"requirement","statement":"A segment definition whose predicate reads outside the context of SEG-002, reaches further than two reference fields from the subject record, or is longer than two hundred nodes SHALL be refused.","rationale":"A predicate that cannot be planned cannot be bounded, so it is refused when it is defined and never when a person is evaluated.","evaluate":{"method":"property"},"ref":"SEG-004","area":"04-automation","section":"Definition","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-7","boundaryDetail":"`define-segment`","traces":["g-608","k-100","d-5021","d-5025"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-segments-2","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"seg-005","kind":"requirement","statement":"A segment definition whose predicate names a field that the policies of the defining principal do not permit that principal to read SHALL be refused.","rationale":"A predicate over a hidden field with a list of the members would let its definer read the field.","evaluate":{"method":"property"},"ref":"SEG-005","area":"04-automation","section":"Definition","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-7","boundaryDetail":"`define-segment`","traces":["g-607","k-13","d-5028"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-segments-2","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"seg-006","kind":"requirement","statement":"A schema change that removes or retypes a field that a segment names SHALL be refused while the segment names it.","rationale":"A view or a query that names a missing field is refused the same way, and a segment must not fail silently at the next change.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"SEG-006","area":"04-automation","section":"Definition","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-7","boundaryDetail":"`schema change`","traces":["g-605","d-5028"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-segments-2","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"seg-007","kind":"requirement","statement":"A segment SHALL be defined, changed or removed only by a principal whose policies grant the capability segments-define.","rationale":"Defining a segment decides who receives mail and notices, so it is held by the owner.","evaluate":{"method":"property"},"ref":"SEG-007","area":"04-automation","section":"Definition","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-7","boundaryDetail":"`segments-define`","traces":["g-607","d-5029"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-segments-2","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"seg-008","kind":"requirement","statement":"A committed change that makes a person satisfy the predicate of a segment SHALL write one entry event in the transaction that commits the change.","rationale":"A change and the membership it causes are one fact, as an event and its jobs are (SCH-004).","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"SEG-008","area":"04-automation","section":"Membership","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-7","boundaryDetail":"`entry event`","traces":["g-606","d-5022","k-9"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-segments-3","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"seg-009","kind":"requirement","statement":"A committed change that makes a person stop satisfying the predicate of a segment SHALL write one exit event in the transaction that commits the change.","rationale":"Leaving is as much a fact as entering, and a workflow that waits for it must not poll.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"SEG-009","area":"04-automation","section":"Membership","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-7","boundaryDetail":"`exit event`","traces":["g-606","d-5022"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-segments-3","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"seg-010","kind":"requirement","statement":"A committed change that leaves the membership of a person in a segment as it was SHALL write no entry event and no exit event.","rationale":"An event that repeats a state would start a workflow for nothing.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"SEG-010","area":"04-automation","section":"Membership","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-7","boundaryDetail":"`segment membership`","traces":["g-606","d-5022"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-segments-3","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"seg-011","kind":"requirement","statement":"The members of a segment SHALL be the persons for whom its predicate is true when evaluated on the state that replaying the journal gives, at the time of the latest evaluation of the segment.","rationale":"Membership is derived from the journal and the times given to its decisions, so it can be rebuilt and checked at any point (K-11).","evaluate":{"method":"property"},"ref":"SEG-011","area":"04-automation","section":"Membership","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`segment membership`","traces":["g-605","k-11","d-5022"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-segments-3","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"seg-012","kind":"requirement","statement":"A transaction that rolls back SHALL leave every membership as it was and SHALL write no entry event and no exit event.","rationale":"An event for a change that did not happen is a lie that a trigger would act on.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"SEG-012","area":"04-automation","section":"Membership","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-7","boundaryDetail":"`segment membership`","traces":["g-606","d-5022"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-segments-3","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"seg-013","kind":"requirement","statement":"An entry event and an exit event SHALL be domain events that name the segment, the person, the version of the predicate and the revision of the change.","rationale":"Triggers and the journal need to know what happened to whom and under which definition.","evaluate":{"method":"property"},"ref":"SEG-013","area":"04-automation","section":"Membership","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-7","boundaryDetail":"`segment-membership-event`","traces":["g-606","d-5023"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-segments-3","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"seg-014","kind":"requirement","statement":"A trigger subscribed to the entry events or the exit events of a segment SHALL create its job in the transaction that commits the event.","rationale":"The event and its consequences are one fact (SCH-004).","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"SEG-014","area":"04-automation","section":"Membership","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-7","boundaryDetail":"`trigger`","traces":["g-606","d-5023"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-segments-3","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"seg-015","kind":"requirement","statement":"Two evaluations of a segment predicate on equal state, for the same person and with the same context SHALL give equal results.","rationale":"A decision that can be simulated can be replayed (K-11).","evaluate":{"method":"property"},"ref":"SEG-015","area":"04-automation","section":"Membership","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`evaluate-segment-predicate`","traces":["g-605","k-11"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-segments-3","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"seg-016","kind":"requirement","statement":"An evaluation of a segment predicate SHALL take the time only from the context of the decision, and the kernel SHALL read no clock for it.","rationale":"Time enters decisions as an input so that every decision can be simulated and replayed (K-1, K-11).","evaluate":{"method":"property"},"ref":"SEG-016","area":"04-automation","section":"Time","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`evaluate-segment-predicate`","traces":["g-605","k-1","k-11","d-5024"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-segments-4","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"seg-017","kind":"requirement","statement":"A segment whose predicate reads the time SHALL declare a refresh interval of at least one minute and at most one day, and a definition without one SHALL be refused.","rationale":"The interval is the bound on how far membership may lag, and a floor on it bounds the load.","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"SEG-017","area":"04-automation","section":"Time","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-7","boundaryDetail":"`define-segment`","traces":["g-608","d-5024"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-segments-4","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"seg-018","kind":"requirement","statement":"A segment whose predicate reads the time SHALL have a schedule that creates one refresh job in each refresh interval.","rationale":"A change cannot notice that time has passed, so a schedule does.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"SEG-018","area":"04-automation","section":"Time","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-7","boundaryDetail":"`schedule`","traces":["g-605","g-606","d-5024"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-segments-4","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"seg-019","kind":"requirement","statement":"A refresh job SHALL evaluate the predicate for every person of the subject type at the time given to the job and SHALL write the entry and exit events that the evaluation causes.","rationale":"The refresh is the one evaluation that sees the time, so it must see everyone.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"SEG-019","area":"04-automation","section":"Time","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-7","boundaryDetail":"`run-segment-batch`","traces":["g-605","g-606","d-5024"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-segments-4","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"seg-020","kind":"requirement","statement":"A segment whose predicate does not read the time SHALL have no schedule and SHALL create no refresh job.","rationale":"Work that cannot change a result is not done.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"SEG-020","area":"04-automation","section":"Time","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-7","boundaryDetail":"`schedule`","traces":["g-608","d-5024"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-segments-4","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"seg-021","kind":"requirement","statement":"A person whose value of a time-dependent predicate changes because time has passed SHALL enter or leave the segment at the first refresh that starts after the change.","rationale":"This is the bound: membership lags the predicate by at most one refresh interval and the run of one refresh.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"SEG-021","area":"04-automation","section":"Time","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-7","boundaryDetail":"`refresh interval`","traces":["g-605","d-5024"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-segments-4","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"seg-022","kind":"requirement","statement":"A change of the predicate of a segment SHALL evaluate every person of the subject type under the new predicate in batches, and SHALL write the entry and exit events that the change causes in the transactions of the batches.","rationale":"A predicate change can move many people, and no one transaction may evaluate them all (K-100).","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"SEG-022","area":"04-automation","section":"Change of definition","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-7","boundaryDetail":"`define-segment`","traces":["g-605","g-608","d-5027"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-segments-5","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"seg-023","kind":"requirement","statement":"The batches of a predicate change SHALL write all the events that the change causes within as many batches as there are hundreds of persons of the subject type at the time of the change, rounded up.","rationale":"The bound states what a tenant waits for, and what the platform spends.","evaluate":{"method":"property"},"ref":"SEG-023","area":"04-automation","section":"Change of definition","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-7","boundaryDetail":"`define-segment`","traces":["g-608","d-5026","d-5027"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-segments-5","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"seg-024","kind":"requirement","statement":"A record change that commits while the batches of a predicate change run SHALL be evaluated under the new predicate.","rationale":"A person must not be decided under a definition that has already been replaced.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"SEG-024","area":"04-automation","section":"Change of definition","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-7","boundaryDetail":"`segment membership`","traces":["g-605","d-5027"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-segments-5","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"seg-025","kind":"requirement","statement":"A batch that belongs to a superseded version of a predicate SHALL write nothing.","rationale":"The newer version has started its own batches, and a stale one would undo them.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"SEG-025","area":"04-automation","section":"Change of definition","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-7","boundaryDetail":"`run-segment-batch`","traces":["g-605","d-5027"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-segments-5","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"seg-026","kind":"requirement","statement":"Removing a segment SHALL remove its memberships, its pending batches and its schedule, and SHALL write no exit event.","rationale":"The persons did not stop satisfying a predicate: the segment ended.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"SEG-026","area":"04-automation","section":"Change of definition","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-7","boundaryDetail":"`remove-segment`","traces":["g-605","d-5033"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-segments-5","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"seg-027","kind":"requirement","statement":"A decision that evaluates segments SHALL load only the records that its plan names, which are the subject record of each person evaluated and the records that the predicate reaches from it.","rationale":"A decision loads only the records that its plan names (K-100).","evaluate":{"method":"property"},"ref":"SEG-027","area":"04-automation","section":"Bounds","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`plan-segment-needs`","traces":["g-608","k-100","d-5025"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-segments-6","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"seg-028","kind":"requirement","statement":"A transaction SHALL evaluate the predicate of one segment for at most one hundred persons, and SHALL leave the rest of a change that affects more persons to batches that it creates.","rationale":"One change must not hold the tenant database for as long as the tenant has people.","evaluate":{"method":"property"},"ref":"SEG-028","area":"04-automation","section":"Bounds","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`decide-segment-membership`","traces":["g-608","d-5026"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-segments-6","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"seg-029","kind":"requirement","statement":"A tenant SHALL hold at most one hundred segments and at most twenty-five segments whose predicates read any one object type, and a definition past either bound SHALL be refused.","rationale":"One change evaluates every segment of its tenant, so their number is bounded.","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"SEG-029","area":"04-automation","section":"Bounds","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-7","boundaryDetail":"`define-segment`","traces":["g-608","d-5026","d-6555"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-segments-6","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"seg-030","kind":"requirement","statement":"An evaluation of a segment predicate that fails or exhausts the step budget of tenant expressions SHALL leave the membership of the person as it was and SHALL name the person and the segment in its failure.","rationale":"A failure is reported where it happened and does not move anyone (CMS-252).","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"SEG-030","area":"04-automation","section":"Bounds","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`evaluate-segment-predicate`","traces":["g-608","d-5025"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-segments-6","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"seg-031","kind":"requirement","statement":"An entry event and an exit event SHALL carry the hop count of the change that caused them, increased by one.","rationale":"The hop count is what ends a chain, so every link of a chain through a segment must raise it (SCH-300).","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"SEG-031","area":"04-automation","section":"Bounds","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-7","boundaryDetail":"`entry event`","traces":["g-606","d-5032","d-700"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-segments-6","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"seg-032","kind":"requirement","statement":"A change past the hop limit SHALL still update the membership and write its entry or exit event, and the trigger SHALL create no job for it.","rationale":"Membership must stay equal to the evaluation while the loop is cut (SCH-300).","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"SEG-032","area":"04-automation","section":"Bounds","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-7","boundaryDetail":"`trigger`","traces":["g-606","d-5032","d-700"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-segments-6","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"seg-033","kind":"requirement","statement":"Listing the members of a segment SHALL require the capability segments-read and SHALL show only the persons whose subject records the policies of the reader permit the reader to read.","rationale":"Reading members is a read, and a read is filtered by policy (KRN-004).","evaluate":{"method":"property"},"ref":"SEG-033","area":"04-automation","section":"Reads and erasure","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-7","boundaryDetail":"`list-segment-members`","traces":["g-607","k-13","d-5029"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-segments-7","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"seg-034","kind":"requirement","statement":"A membership SHALL hold the segment, the person, the version of the predicate and the time of entry, and no field of the person.","rationale":"No second copy of personal data exists, so erasure and sealing reach one place.","evaluate":{"method":"property"},"ref":"SEG-034","area":"04-automation","section":"Reads and erasure","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`segment membership`","traces":["g-607","g-609","d-5029"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-segments-7","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"seg-035","kind":"requirement","statement":"A test of a predicate against one person SHALL change no state, SHALL return the value and the names of the fields that the predicate read, and SHALL answer only for a person whose subject record the caller may read.","rationale":"A test is a read, so it can neither write nor show what the caller could not see.","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"SEG-035","area":"04-automation","section":"Reads and erasure","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-7","boundaryDetail":"`test-segment-predicate`","traces":["g-607","d-5030"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-segments-7","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"seg-036","kind":"requirement","statement":"The transaction that records the erasure of a person SHALL remove the person from every segment.","rationale":"An erased person must leave no trace that a trigger could still act on (PRV-353).","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"SEG-036","area":"04-automation","section":"Reads and erasure","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-7","boundaryDetail":"`segment membership`","traces":["g-609","d-5031"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-segments-7","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"seg-037","kind":"requirement","statement":"No change SHALL enter an erased person into a segment.","rationale":"Erasure is final, whatever a later change or refresh evaluates.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"SEG-037","area":"04-automation","section":"Reads and erasure","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-7","boundaryDetail":"`segment membership`","traces":["g-609","d-5031"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-segments-7","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"seg-038","kind":"requirement","statement":"The exit event that an erasure writes SHALL name the person in sealed form.","rationale":"The journal keeps the fact and not the identity (PRV-361).","evaluate":{"method":"property"},"ref":"SEG-038","area":"04-automation","section":"Reads and erasure","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`exit event`","traces":["g-609","d-5031","k-13"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-segments-7","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"m-segment-events-match-membership","kind":"invariant","models":"seg-008","statement":"The entry and exit events of a person are exactly the changes of its membership: after every step the person is a member when one more entry than exit was written, and is not when as many were.","evaluate":{"method":"state-invariant","scenarios":["segment-person-enters-and-leaves","segment-membership-flips-twice","segment-change-flips-and-flips-back","segment-change-rolled-back","segment-member-erased","segment-predicate-change-moves-person"],"expr":"(segment-membership-flow.member && segment-membership-flow.entries - segment-membership-flow.exits == 1) || (!segment-membership-flow.member && segment-membership-flow.entries == segment-membership-flow.exits)","negatives":[{"scenario":"segment-person-enters-and-leaves","faults":["defect-segment-entry-without-event"]},{"scenario":"segment-person-enters-and-leaves","faults":["defect-segment-entry-after-commit"]},{"scenario":"segment-change-flips-and-flips-back","faults":["defect-segment-event-every-change"]}]},"faultModel":"fault-model-launch","assumptions":["a-model-abstraction"],"faultBasis":"restatement"},
    {"id":"m-segment-membership-equals-evaluation","kind":"invariant","models":"seg-011","statement":"Membership equals the evaluation of the predicate after every committed change and every batch of a changed predicate.","evaluate":{"method":"state-invariant","scenarios":["segment-person-enters-and-leaves","segment-membership-flips-twice","segment-change-flips-and-flips-back","segment-change-rolled-back","segment-member-erased","segment-predicate-change-moves-person"],"expr":"segment-membership-flow.member == segment-membership-flow.holds","negatives":[{"scenario":"segment-person-enters-and-leaves","faults":["defect-segment-evaluation-skipped"]},{"scenario":"segment-predicate-change-moves-person","faults":["defect-segment-predicate-change-skipped"]}]},"faultModel":"fault-model-launch","assumptions":["a-model-abstraction"],"faultBasis":"restatement"},
    {"id":"m-segment-rolled-back-writes-nothing","kind":"invariant","models":"seg-012","statement":"No more events are written than changes committed: a rolled back change writes none.","evaluate":{"method":"state-invariant","scenarios":["segment-person-enters-and-leaves","segment-membership-flips-twice","segment-change-flips-and-flips-back","segment-change-rolled-back","segment-member-erased","segment-predicate-change-moves-person"],"expr":"segment-membership-flow.entries + segment-membership-flow.exits <= segment-membership-flow.committed","negatives":[{"scenario":"segment-change-rolled-back","faults":["defect-segment-event-before-commit"]}]},"faultModel":"fault-model-launch","assumptions":["a-model-abstraction"],"faultBasis":"restatement"},
    {"id":"m-erased-person-in-no-segment","kind":"invariant","models":"seg-036","statement":"An erased person is never a member.","evaluate":{"method":"state-invariant","scenarios":["segment-member-erased"],"expr":"!segment-membership-flow.erased || !segment-membership-flow.member","negatives":[{"scenario":"segment-member-erased","faults":["defect-segment-erasure-keeps-member"]},{"scenario":"segment-member-erased","faults":["defect-segment-enters-erased"]}]},"faultModel":"fault-model-launch","assumptions":["a-model-abstraction"],"faultBasis":"restatement"},
    {"id":"m-segment-entry-written","kind":"temporal","models":"seg-008","statement":"A change that makes a person satisfy the predicate writes an entry event.","evaluate":{"method":"eventually","scenarios":["segment-person-enters-and-leaves"],"occurs":{"event":"sg-entered"},"negatives":[{"scenario":"segment-person-enters-and-leaves","faults":["segment-entry-disabled"]}]},"faultModel":"fault-model-launch","assumptions":["a-model-abstraction"],"faultBasis":"restatement"},
    {"id":"m-segment-exit-written","kind":"temporal","models":"seg-009","statement":"A change that makes a person stop satisfying the predicate writes an exit event.","evaluate":{"method":"eventually","scenarios":["segment-person-enters-and-leaves"],"occurs":{"event":"sg-exited"},"negatives":[{"scenario":"segment-person-enters-and-leaves","faults":["segment-exit-disabled"]}]},"faultModel":"fault-model-launch","assumptions":["a-model-abstraction"],"faultBasis":"restatement"},
    {"id":"m-segment-rolled-back-no-entry","kind":"temporal","models":"seg-012","statement":"A change that rolls back writes no entry event.","evaluate":{"method":"never","scenarios":["segment-rolled-back-only"],"occurs":{"event":"sg-entered"},"negatives":[{"scenario":"segment-rolled-back-only","faults":["defect-segment-event-before-commit"]}]},"faultModel":"fault-model-launch","assumptions":["a-model-abstraction"],"faultBasis":"restatement"},
    {"id":"m-segment-refresh-leaves-nobody-stale","kind":"invariant","models":"seg-021","statement":"Every refresh evaluates the person: the refresh that follows a change of the value brings membership to it, so no person stays stale for a second interval.","evaluate":{"method":"state-invariant","scenarios":["segment-time-turns-predicate","segment-refresh-finds-nothing"],"expr":"segment-refresh-flow.staleIntervals == 0","negatives":[{"scenario":"segment-time-turns-predicate","faults":["defect-segment-refresh-skips"]}]},"faultModel":"fault-model-launch","assumptions":["a-model-abstraction"],"faultBasis":"restatement"},
    {"id":"m-segment-refresh-enters","kind":"temporal","models":"seg-019","statement":"A person whose predicate turned true by time alone is entered by the refresh.","evaluate":{"method":"eventually","scenarios":["segment-time-turns-predicate"],"occurs":{"event":"sg-entered"},"negatives":[{"scenario":"segment-time-turns-predicate","faults":["segment-refresh-entry-disabled"]}]},"faultModel":"fault-model-launch","assumptions":["a-model-abstraction"],"faultBasis":"restatement"},
    {"id":"m-segment-refresh-exits","kind":"temporal","models":"seg-019","statement":"A person whose predicate turned false by time alone is removed by the refresh.","evaluate":{"method":"eventually","scenarios":["segment-time-turns-predicate"],"occurs":{"event":"sg-exited"},"negatives":[{"scenario":"segment-time-turns-predicate","faults":["segment-refresh-exit-disabled"]}]},"faultModel":"fault-model-launch","assumptions":["a-model-abstraction"],"faultBasis":"restatement"},
    {"id":"m-segment-refresh-finds-nothing-writes-nothing","kind":"temporal","models":"seg-019","statement":"A refresh that finds no change writes no entry event.","evaluate":{"method":"never","scenarios":["segment-refresh-finds-nothing"],"occurs":{"event":"sg-entered"},"negatives":[{"scenario":"segment-refresh-finds-nothing","faults":["defect-segment-refresh-enters-always"]}]},"faultModel":"fault-model-launch","assumptions":["a-model-abstraction"],"faultBasis":"restatement"},
    {"id":"m-segment-batches-bounded","kind":"invariant","models":"seg-028","statement":"No batch evaluates more than one hundred persons.","evaluate":{"method":"state-invariant","scenarios":["segment-predicate-change-batches","segment-predicate-changed-mid-rebuild"],"expr":"segment-rebuild-flow.widest <= 100","negatives":[{"scenario":"segment-predicate-change-batches","faults":["defect-segment-batch-unbounded"]}]},"faultModel":"fault-model-operations","assumptions":["a-model-abstraction"],"faultBasis":"restatement"},
    {"id":"m-segment-batches-cover-everyone","kind":"invariant","models":"seg-025","statement":"The persons evaluated and the persons waiting always add up to the persons of the current version: a batch of a superseded version adds none.","evaluate":{"method":"state-invariant","scenarios":["segment-predicate-change-batches","segment-predicate-changed-mid-rebuild"],"expr":"segment-rebuild-flow.evaluated + segment-rebuild-flow.remaining == segment-rebuild-flow.total","negatives":[{"scenario":"segment-predicate-changed-mid-rebuild","faults":["defect-segment-stale-batch-writes"]}]},"faultModel":"fault-model-operations","assumptions":["a-model-abstraction"],"faultBasis":"restatement"},
    {"id":"m-segment-batches-within-bound","kind":"invariant","models":"seg-023","statement":"A changed predicate takes no more batches than there are hundreds of persons.","evaluate":{"method":"state-invariant","scenarios":["segment-predicate-change-batches","segment-predicate-changed-mid-rebuild"],"expr":"segment-rebuild-flow.batches * 100 <= segment-rebuild-flow.total + 99","negatives":[{"scenario":"segment-predicate-change-batches","faults":["defect-segment-batch-single-person"]}]},"faultModel":"fault-model-operations","assumptions":["a-model-abstraction"],"faultBasis":"restatement"},
    {"id":"m-segment-batches-end","kind":"temporal","models":"seg-022","statement":"The batches of a changed predicate end.","evaluate":{"method":"eventually","scenarios":["segment-predicate-change-batches"],"occurs":{"event":"sg-rebuilt"},"negatives":[{"scenario":"segment-predicate-change-batches","faults":["segment-last-batch-disabled"]}]},"faultModel":"fault-model-operations","assumptions":["a-model-abstraction"],"faultBasis":"restatement"},
    {"id":"m-segment-superseded-batch-dropped","kind":"temporal","models":"seg-025","statement":"A batch of a superseded version is dropped.","evaluate":{"method":"eventually","scenarios":["segment-predicate-changed-mid-rebuild"],"occurs":{"event":"sg-batch-dropped"},"negatives":[{"scenario":"segment-predicate-changed-mid-rebuild","faults":["defect-segment-stale-batch-writes"]}]},"faultModel":"fault-model-launch","assumptions":["a-model-abstraction"],"faultBasis":"restatement"},
    {"id":"m-segment-chain-bounded","kind":"invariant","models":"seg-031","statement":"A chain through a segment and a workflow creates no more jobs than the hop limit of eight (D-700) allows.","evaluate":{"method":"state-invariant","scenarios":["segment-chain-runs-to-limit","segment-chain-edit-past-limit"],"expr":"segment-chain-flow.jobs <= 8","negatives":[{"scenario":"segment-chain-runs-to-limit","faults":["defect-segment-chain-unbounded"]}]},"faultModel":"fault-model-operations","assumptions":["a-model-abstraction"],"faultBasis":"restatement"},
    {"id":"m-segment-chain-past-limit-updates","kind":"invariant","models":"seg-032","statement":"Every edit updates membership, including the edits past the hop limit.","evaluate":{"method":"state-invariant","scenarios":["segment-chain-runs-to-limit","segment-chain-edit-past-limit"],"expr":"segment-chain-flow.updates == segment-chain-flow.edits","negatives":[{"scenario":"segment-chain-edit-past-limit","faults":["defect-segment-chain-cut-drops-update"]}]},"faultModel":"fault-model-operations","assumptions":["a-model-abstraction"],"faultBasis":"restatement"},
    {"id":"set-001","kind":"requirement","statement":"A setting definition SHALL state a name, a type taken from the declared types, a default of that type and the levels that may override it.","rationale":"A setting is typed metadata, so every value of it can be checked and every level that may change it is known.","evaluate":{"method":"property"},"ref":"SET-001","area":"09-administration","section":"Setting definitions","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-13","boundaryDetail":"`setting definition`","traces":["g-610","d-5040","d-5046","g-31"],"milestone":6,"inSection":"sec-administration-7","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"set-002","kind":"requirement","statement":"A setting definition whose default is not a value of its type SHALL be refused.","rationale":"A default that is of another type would give a read an answer that no writer could have written.","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"SET-002","area":"09-administration","section":"Setting definitions","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-13","boundaryDetail":"`setting definition`","traces":["g-611","d-5046"],"milestone":6,"inSection":"sec-administration-7","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"set-003","kind":"requirement","statement":"A setting definition of a tenant SHALL be refused when it has the name of a platform setting definition.","rationale":"A name has one meaning in every tenant.","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"SET-003","area":"09-administration","section":"Setting definitions","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-13","boundaryDetail":"`setting definition`","traces":["g-611","d-5047"],"milestone":6,"inSection":"sec-administration-7","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"set-004","kind":"requirement","statement":"A change of the type of a setting definition SHALL be refused while an override of the setting exists.","rationale":"No stored value is then ever of another type than its definition.","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"SET-004","area":"09-administration","section":"Setting definitions","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-13","boundaryDetail":"`setting definition`","traces":["g-611","d-5046"],"milestone":6,"inSection":"sec-administration-7","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"set-005","kind":"requirement","statement":"A platform setting definition SHALL be created and changed only by a release of the platform.","rationale":"The platform's definitions go through the review of a release, as feature flags do.","evaluate":{"method":"property"},"ref":"SET-005","area":"09-administration","section":"Setting definitions","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-19","boundaryDetail":"`setting definition`","traces":["g-610","d-5047","d-510"],"milestone":6,"inSection":"sec-administration-7","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"set-010","kind":"requirement","statement":"A read of a setting for a principal SHALL return the value of the most specific permitted override that reaches the principal, in the order person, team, tenant and platform, and the default when no such override exists.","rationale":"One order of levels gives one answer to every reader.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"SET-010","area":"09-administration","section":"Setting resolution","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`setting resolution`","traces":["g-610","d-5041","d-15"],"milestone":6,"inSection":"sec-administration-8","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"set-011","kind":"requirement","statement":"When several teams of a person hold an override of a setting, a read for the person SHALL return the value of the override of the team whose identifier comes first in ascending byte order.","rationale":"The order of teams has no hidden state, so the answer does not depend on when anyone joined or wrote.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"SET-011","area":"09-administration","section":"Setting resolution","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`setting resolution`","traces":["g-610","d-5042"],"milestone":6,"inSection":"sec-administration-8","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"set-012","kind":"requirement","statement":"A read of a setting SHALL name the level from which its value comes.","rationale":"A person who sees a value can see which level to change to change it.","evaluate":{"method":"property"},"ref":"SET-012","area":"09-administration","section":"Setting resolution","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-13","boundaryDetail":"`setting resolution`","traces":["g-610","d-5041"],"milestone":6,"inSection":"sec-administration-8","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"set-013","kind":"requirement","statement":"A read of a setting for an anonymous principal SHALL be answered from the tenant level, the platform level and the default only.","rationale":"An anonymous reader has no person and no team.","evaluate":{"method":"property"},"ref":"SET-013","area":"09-administration","section":"Setting resolution","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`setting resolution`","traces":["g-610","g-614","d-5041"],"milestone":6,"inSection":"sec-administration-8","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"set-014","kind":"requirement","statement":"A read of a setting SHALL ignore an override at a level that the definition does not allow or that a lock of the definition closes.","rationale":"A level that was closed after an override was written must not still decide the answer.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"SET-014","area":"09-administration","section":"Setting resolution","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`setting resolution`","traces":["g-611","d-5043"],"milestone":6,"inSection":"sec-administration-8","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"set-020","kind":"requirement","statement":"A write of an override at a level that the definition of the setting does not allow SHALL be refused.","rationale":"The definition is the list of who may change the value.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"SET-020","area":"09-administration","section":"Writing settings","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-13","boundaryDetail":"`setting override`","traces":["g-611","d-5043"],"milestone":6,"inSection":"sec-administration-9","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"set-021","kind":"requirement","statement":"A write of a value that is not a value of the type of the setting SHALL be refused.","rationale":"Every stored override is then of the type of its setting.","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"SET-021","area":"09-administration","section":"Writing settings","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-13","boundaryDetail":"`setting override`","traces":["g-611","d-5046"],"milestone":6,"inSection":"sec-administration-9","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"set-022","kind":"requirement","statement":"Removing an override SHALL make a read return the value of the next most specific permitted override, or the default when none remains.","rationale":"A person can undo their own choice and get what applied before it.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"SET-022","area":"09-administration","section":"Writing settings","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-13","boundaryDetail":"`setting override`","traces":["g-610","d-5041"],"milestone":6,"inSection":"sec-administration-9","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"set-023","kind":"requirement","statement":"A write at a level that a lock of the definition closes SHALL be refused.","rationale":"A lock is the platform or the tenant keeping a value for everyone below it.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"SET-023","area":"09-administration","section":"Writing settings","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-13","boundaryDetail":"`setting override`","traces":["g-611","d-5043"],"milestone":6,"inSection":"sec-administration-9","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"set-024","kind":"requirement","statement":"An override at a level that a lock closes SHALL be kept and apply again when the lock is lifted.","rationale":"Locking is reversible and deletes no data of a team or a person.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"SET-024","area":"09-administration","section":"Writing settings","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-13","boundaryDetail":"`setting override`","traces":["g-611","d-5043"],"milestone":6,"inSection":"sec-administration-9","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"set-025","kind":"requirement","statement":"A write that names a revision other than the current revision of its override SHALL be refused with a conflict that changes nothing.","rationale":"Two people who change one override at the same time cannot overwrite each other.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"SET-025","area":"09-administration","section":"Writing settings","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-13","boundaryDetail":"`setting override`","traces":["g-610","d-5045"],"milestone":6,"inSection":"sec-administration-9","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"set-030","kind":"requirement","statement":"A write at the platform level SHALL be refused unless the caller holds the capability setting-write-platform.","rationale":"The platform level changes every tenant.","evaluate":{"method":"property"},"ref":"SET-030","area":"09-administration","section":"Writing settings","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-13","boundaryDetail":"`setting override`","traces":["g-612","d-5044"],"milestone":6,"inSection":"sec-administration-9","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"set-031","kind":"requirement","statement":"A write at the tenant level SHALL be refused unless the caller holds the capability setting-write-tenant.","rationale":"The tenant level changes every person of the tenant.","evaluate":{"method":"property"},"ref":"SET-031","area":"09-administration","section":"Writing settings","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-13","boundaryDetail":"`setting override`","traces":["g-612","d-5044"],"milestone":6,"inSection":"sec-administration-9","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"set-032","kind":"requirement","statement":"A write at the team level SHALL be refused unless the caller holds the capability setting-write-team.","rationale":"The team level changes every member of the team.","evaluate":{"method":"property"},"ref":"SET-032","area":"09-administration","section":"Writing settings","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-13","boundaryDetail":"`setting override`","traces":["g-612","d-5044"],"milestone":6,"inSection":"sec-administration-9","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"set-033","kind":"requirement","statement":"A write at the person level SHALL be refused unless the caller holds the capability setting-write-person.","rationale":"Writing one's own settings is a capability that a tenant policy can withdraw.","evaluate":{"method":"property"},"ref":"SET-033","area":"09-administration","section":"Writing settings","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-13","boundaryDetail":"`setting override`","traces":["g-612","d-5044"],"milestone":6,"inSection":"sec-administration-9","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"set-034","kind":"requirement","statement":"A write at the person level SHALL be refused unless the override belongs to the caller.","rationale":"No one, the owner included, changes how another person's own pages look and behave.","evaluate":{"method":"property"},"ref":"SET-034","area":"09-administration","section":"Writing settings","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-13","boundaryDetail":"`setting override`","traces":["g-612","g-614","d-5044"],"milestone":6,"inSection":"sec-administration-9","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"set-040","kind":"requirement","statement":"A committed change of a setting SHALL produce a domain event that names the setting, the level and the subject and carries no value.","rationale":"A person-level value can be personal data, and the event log is kept for the restore window.","evaluate":{"method":"property"},"ref":"SET-040","area":"09-administration","section":"Change, pages and copies","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-16","boundaryDetail":"`setting notice`","traces":["g-613","d-5048","k-7"],"milestone":6,"inSection":"sec-administration-10","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"set-041","kind":"requirement","statement":"A change of a setting SHALL refresh, over the live connection, every open page whose view depends on the setting and whose reader's value the change can alter.","rationale":"A tenant that changes its accent sees every open page follow, as the site test shows.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"SET-041","area":"09-administration","section":"Change, pages and copies","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-16","boundaryDetail":"`setting notice`","traces":["g-613","d-5048"],"milestone":6,"inSection":"sec-administration-10","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"set-042","kind":"requirement","statement":"A change of a setting SHALL be recorded in the audit log with the previous value, the new value, the principal and the correlation identifier.","rationale":"A changed setting is a change of behaviour, and it is explained the same way as any other change (OPS-329).","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"SET-042","area":"09-administration","section":"Change, pages and copies","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-12","boundaryDetail":"`audit entry`","traces":["g-613","d-5048","g-30"],"milestone":6,"inSection":"sec-administration-10","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"set-043","kind":"requirement","statement":"A change of a person-level override SHALL reach only the open pages of that person.","rationale":"A person's own choice is not announced to anyone else.","evaluate":{"method":"property"},"ref":"SET-043","area":"09-administration","section":"Change, pages and copies","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-16","boundaryDetail":"`setting notice`","traces":["g-614","d-5048"],"milestone":6,"inSection":"sec-administration-10","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"set-050","kind":"requirement","statement":"The key of a stored view copy that depends on a setting SHALL contain the platform revision and the tenant revision of that setting.","rationale":"A change makes a new key, so a stale entry cannot be read by mistake (CPY-002).","evaluate":{"method":"property"},"ref":"SET-050","area":"09-administration","section":"Change, pages and copies","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-15","boundaryDetail":"`copy key`","traces":["g-613","d-14","d-5049"],"milestone":6,"inSection":"sec-administration-10","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"set-051","kind":"requirement","statement":"A change of a definition, a lock or an override of a setting SHALL raise the revision of the setting at the level where the change was made.","rationale":"The revision is what a copy key follows.","evaluate":{"method":"property"},"ref":"SET-051","area":"09-administration","section":"Change, pages and copies","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-15","boundaryDetail":"`copy key`","traces":["g-613","d-14","d-5049"],"milestone":6,"inSection":"sec-administration-10","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"set-052","kind":"requirement","statement":"No shared copy SHALL hold a value that comes from a person-level override.","rationale":"No shared copy holds anything that depends on who is asking (K-7).","evaluate":{"method":"property"},"ref":"SET-052","area":"09-administration","section":"Change, pages and copies","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-15","boundaryDetail":"`copy key`","traces":["g-614","k-7","d-5049"],"milestone":6,"inSection":"sec-administration-10","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"set-053","kind":"requirement","statement":"The audience class of a principal for a read that depends on a setting SHALL be refined by the level from which the value comes and, at the team level, by the team.","rationale":"Principals who are given different values cannot be served one copy.","evaluate":{"method":"property"},"ref":"SET-053","area":"09-administration","section":"Change, pages and copies","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`audience class`","traces":["g-614","d-15","d-5049"],"milestone":6,"inSection":"sec-administration-10","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"m-st-most-specific-wins","kind":"invariant","models":"set-010","statement":"A read never answers from a less specific level while a more specific permitted override exists.","evaluate":{"method":"state-invariant","scenarios":["st-person-over-team","st-teams-ordered","st-removal-falls-back","st-locked-level"],"expr":"st-resolution-flow.reads == 0 || ((st-resolution-flow.seenLocked == 1 || st-resolution-flow.seenPerson == 0 || st-resolution-flow.from == 3) && (st-resolution-flow.seenLocked == 1 || st-resolution-flow.seenTeamAllowed == 0 || (st-resolution-flow.seenTeamAlpha == 0 && st-resolution-flow.seenTeamBeta == 0) || st-resolution-flow.from >= 2) && (st-resolution-flow.seenTenant == 0 || st-resolution-flow.from >= 1))","negatives":[{"scenario":"st-person-over-team","faults":["defect-st-team-before-person"]}]},"faultModel":"fault-model-launch","assumptions":["a-model-abstraction"],"faultBasis":"restatement"},
    {"id":"m-st-teams-ordered-by-identifier","kind":"invariant","models":"set-011","statement":"When two teams hold an override, a read that comes from the team level returns the value of the team whose identifier comes first, whichever team wrote first.","evaluate":{"method":"state-invariant","scenarios":["st-teams-ordered","st-person-over-team"],"expr":"st-resolution-flow.reads == 0 || st-resolution-flow.from != 2 || st-resolution-flow.seenTeamAlpha == 0 || st-resolution-flow.value == st-resolution-flow.seenTeamAlpha","negatives":[{"scenario":"st-teams-ordered","faults":["defect-st-latest-team"]}]},"faultModel":"fault-model-launch","assumptions":["a-model-abstraction"],"faultBasis":"restatement"},
    {"id":"m-st-concurrent-writers-lose-nothing","kind":"invariant","models":"set-025","statement":"A write that names a revision that is no longer current is not committed, so no change is overwritten by a writer who had not seen it.","evaluate":{"method":"state-invariant","scenarios":["st-concurrent-writers"],"expr":"st-resolution-flow.lost == 0","negatives":[{"scenario":"st-concurrent-writers","faults":["defect-st-accept-stale"]}]},"faultModel":"fault-model-launch","assumptions":["a-model-abstraction"],"faultBasis":"fault"},
    {"id":"m-st-closed-level-refuses-write","kind":"invariant","models":"set-020","statement":"A write at a level that the definition closed is not committed.","evaluate":{"method":"state-invariant","scenarios":["st-closed-level"],"expr":"st-resolution-flow.badWrites == 0","negatives":[{"scenario":"st-closed-level","faults":["defect-st-accept-closed"]}]},"faultModel":"fault-model-launch","assumptions":["a-model-abstraction"],"faultBasis":"restatement"},
    {"id":"m-st-locked-level-refuses-write","kind":"invariant","models":"set-023","statement":"A write below a lock is not committed.","evaluate":{"method":"state-invariant","scenarios":["st-locked-level"],"expr":"st-resolution-flow.badWrites == 0","negatives":[{"scenario":"st-locked-level","faults":["defect-st-accept-locked"]}]},"faultModel":"fault-model-launch","assumptions":["a-model-abstraction"],"faultBasis":"restatement"},
    {"id":"m-st-removal-falls-back","kind":"temporal","models":"set-022","statement":"After the person removes their own override, a read returns the team value.","evaluate":{"method":"eventually","scenarios":["st-removal-falls-back"],"expr":"st-resolution-flow.from == 2 && st-resolution-flow.value == 5","negatives":[{"scenario":"st-removal-falls-back","faults":["st-removal-lost"]}]},"faultModel":"fault-model-launch","assumptions":["a-model-abstraction"],"faultBasis":"fault"},
    {"id":"m-st-committed-override-is-read","kind":"temporal","models":"set-010","statement":"A committed person-level override is what the next read returns.","evaluate":{"method":"eventually","scenarios":["st-person-over-team"],"expr":"st-resolution-flow.from == 3 && st-resolution-flow.value == 7","negatives":[{"scenario":"st-person-over-team","faults":["st-person-write-disabled"]}]},"faultModel":"fault-model-launch","assumptions":["a-model-abstraction"],"faultBasis":"restatement"},
    {"id":"m-st-lifted-lock-restores-levels","kind":"temporal","models":"set-024","statement":"When the lock is lifted, a read returns the person value that the lock had hidden and kept.","evaluate":{"method":"eventually","scenarios":["st-locked-level"],"expr":"st-resolution-flow.from == 3 && st-resolution-flow.value == 7","negatives":[{"scenario":"st-locked-level","faults":["st-unlock-disabled"]}]},"faultModel":"fault-model-launch","assumptions":["a-model-abstraction"],"faultBasis":"restatement"},
    {"id":"agg-001","kind":"requirement","statement":"A named query SHALL be able to declare aggregates, each with a kind of count, sum, minimum, maximum or top, the declared field it reads and a scan bound.","rationale":"Counts and rankings are part of the interface the tenant chose to publish, and each states what it may cost.","evaluate":{"method":"property"},"ref":"AGG-001","area":"07-content","section":"Aggregate declaration","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-9","boundaryDetail":"`named query`","traces":["g-615","d-5060","g-31"],"milestone":6,"inSection":"sec-content-253","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"agg-002","kind":"requirement","statement":"A named query SHALL be refused when an aggregate it declares reads or groups by a field that the query does not declare.","rationale":"An aggregate reaches the fields the tenant published and no others.","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"AGG-002","area":"07-content","section":"Aggregate declaration","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-9","boundaryDetail":"`named query`","traces":["g-615","d-5060"],"milestone":6,"inSection":"sec-content-253","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"agg-003","kind":"requirement","statement":"A request for an aggregate that its named query does not declare SHALL be refused.","rationale":"A client cannot ask for a computation the tenant did not choose to publish.","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"AGG-003","area":"07-content","section":"Aggregate declaration","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-9","boundaryDetail":"`aggregate result`","traces":["g-615","d-5060"],"milestone":6,"inSection":"sec-content-253","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"agg-004","kind":"requirement","statement":"A request for an aggregate that filters on a field the named query does not declare SHALL be refused.","rationale":"The filters of an aggregate are the filters the tenant published (CMS-165).","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"AGG-004","area":"07-content","section":"Aggregate declaration","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-9","boundaryDetail":"`aggregate result`","traces":["g-615","d-5060"],"milestone":6,"inSection":"sec-content-253","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"agg-005","kind":"requirement","statement":"An aggregate SHALL be able to be grouped by one declared field.","rationale":"A leaderboard or a progress figure is one figure for each value of a field.","evaluate":{"method":"property"},"ref":"AGG-005","area":"07-content","section":"Aggregate declaration","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-9","boundaryDetail":"`named query`","traces":["g-615","d-5060"],"milestone":6,"inSection":"sec-content-253","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"agg-010","kind":"requirement","statement":"A count SHALL be the number of records that meet the filter and that the reader may read.","rationale":"A count is what the reader could count by hand.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"AGG-010","area":"07-content","section":"Aggregate results","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-9","boundaryDetail":"`aggregate result`","traces":["g-615","d-5061","d-5063"],"milestone":6,"inSection":"sec-content-254","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"agg-011","kind":"requirement","statement":"A sum SHALL be the total of the values of its declared field over the records that the reader may read, leaving out a record that has no value.","rationale":"A missing value adds nothing.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"AGG-011","area":"07-content","section":"Aggregate results","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-9","boundaryDetail":"`aggregate result`","traces":["g-615","d-5063"],"milestone":6,"inSection":"sec-content-254","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"agg-012","kind":"requirement","statement":"A minimum or a maximum SHALL be the least or the greatest value of its declared field over the records that the reader may read, and null when there is none.","rationale":"An empty set has no least value, and the answer says so.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"AGG-012","area":"07-content","section":"Aggregate results","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-9","boundaryDetail":"`aggregate result`","traces":["g-615","d-5063"],"milestone":6,"inSection":"sec-content-254","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"agg-013","kind":"requirement","statement":"A top aggregate of n SHALL list the n records that the reader may read with the greatest or the least value of its declared field, equal values in ascending order of record identifier.","rationale":"The same records always give the same list.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"AGG-013","area":"07-content","section":"Aggregate results","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-9","boundaryDetail":"`aggregate result`","traces":["g-615","d-5063"],"milestone":6,"inSection":"sec-content-254","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"agg-014","kind":"requirement","statement":"A grouped aggregate SHALL give one result for each distinct value of its group field, and one for the records that have no value, in ascending order of the value.","rationale":"A client can show the groups in an order that does not change between requests.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"AGG-014","area":"07-content","section":"Aggregate results","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-9","boundaryDetail":"`aggregate result`","traces":["g-615","d-5063"],"milestone":6,"inSection":"sec-content-254","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"agg-015","kind":"requirement","statement":"An aggregate SHALL examine only the records that the policies of the audience class of the reader permit the reader to read.","rationale":"An aggregate is a read like any other, decided by the same policies (SRH-150).","evaluate":{"method":"property"},"ref":"AGG-015","area":"07-content","section":"Aggregate results","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-9","boundaryDetail":"`aggregate result`","traces":["g-616","d-5061","g-20"],"milestone":6,"inSection":"sec-content-254","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"agg-016","kind":"requirement","statement":"The result of an aggregate SHALL equal the result of computing the same aggregate one record at a time over the records that the reader may read.","rationale":"A figure that differs from the sum of its parts is wrong for the reader who sees the parts.","evaluate":{"method":"property"},"ref":"AGG-016","area":"07-content","section":"Aggregate results","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-9","boundaryDetail":"`aggregate result`","traces":["g-616","d-5061"],"milestone":6,"inSection":"sec-content-254","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"agg-017","kind":"requirement","statement":"A record SHALL be left out of an aggregate when the reader may not read a field that the aggregate names.","rationale":"A count or a group never reveals a field the reader may not read.","evaluate":{"method":"property"},"ref":"AGG-017","area":"07-content","section":"Aggregate results","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-9","boundaryDetail":"`aggregate result`","traces":["g-616","d-5061","g-20"],"milestone":6,"inSection":"sec-content-254","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"agg-020","kind":"requirement","statement":"An aggregate that would examine more records than its declared scan bound SHALL be refused with the error scan-bound-exceeded before any record is read.","rationale":"An expensive aggregate is refused by its plan before it costs the platform anything (CMS-255).","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"AGG-020","area":"07-content","section":"Aggregate bounds","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-9","boundaryDetail":"`aggregate result`","traces":["g-617","d-5062","k-100"],"milestone":6,"inSection":"sec-content-255","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"agg-021","kind":"requirement","statement":"A refused aggregate SHALL return no result, whole or in part.","rationale":"A client cannot mistake part of the records for all of them.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"AGG-021","area":"07-content","section":"Aggregate bounds","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-9","boundaryDetail":"`aggregate result`","traces":["g-617","d-5062"],"milestone":6,"inSection":"sec-content-255","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"agg-022","kind":"requirement","statement":"A sum of integers that does not fit the type of its field SHALL be refused with the error sum-overflow.","rationale":"A wrapped or rounded sum is a wrong answer that looks right.","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"AGG-022","area":"07-content","section":"Aggregate bounds","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-9","boundaryDetail":"`aggregate result`","traces":["g-617","d-5063"],"milestone":6,"inSection":"sec-content-255","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"agg-023","kind":"requirement","statement":"A named query SHALL be refused when it declares an aggregate whose scan bound is above the platform maximum.","rationale":"The platform bounds what a tenant can make a request cost.","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"AGG-023","area":"07-content","section":"Aggregate bounds","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-9","boundaryDetail":"`named query`","traces":["g-617","d-5062"],"milestone":6,"inSection":"sec-content-255","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"agg-030","kind":"requirement","statement":"The key of a stored aggregate result SHALL contain the tenant, the query, the aggregate, its arguments, the audience class, the schema version and the revision of each object type the aggregate reads.","rationale":"A change produces a new key, so a stale result cannot be read by mistake (CPY-002).","evaluate":{"method":"property"},"ref":"AGG-030","area":"07-content","section":"Aggregate copies","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-15","boundaryDetail":"`copy key`","traces":["g-618","d-14","d-5064"],"milestone":6,"inSection":"sec-content-256","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"agg-031","kind":"requirement","statement":"A request SHALL NOT be answered from an aggregate result computed before the last commit to an object type that the aggregate reads.","rationale":"A leaderboard that ignores the last score is wrong at the moment it matters.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"AGG-031","area":"07-content","section":"Aggregate copies","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-15","boundaryDetail":"`copy key`","traces":["g-618","d-14","d-5064"],"milestone":6,"inSection":"sec-content-256","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"agg-032","kind":"requirement","statement":"A stored aggregate result SHALL be served only to principals of the audience class it was stored for.","rationale":"A result stored for editors is not an answer for readers (CPY-006).","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"AGG-032","area":"07-content","section":"Aggregate copies","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-15","boundaryDetail":"`audience class`","traces":["g-618","g-20","d-5065"],"milestone":6,"inSection":"sec-content-256","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"agg-033","kind":"requirement","statement":"The audience class of a principal for an aggregate SHALL be derived by the kernel from the policies of the tenant.","rationale":"Who may share a result is an authorisation question and has one answer (CPY-005).","evaluate":{"method":"property"},"ref":"AGG-033","area":"07-content","section":"Aggregate copies","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`audience class`","traces":["g-618","d-15","d-5065"],"milestone":6,"inSection":"sec-content-256","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"agg-034","kind":"requirement","statement":"A stored aggregate result SHALL NOT be a shared copy.","rationale":"A result can hold a principal, and no shared copy holds anything that depends on who is asking (K-7).","evaluate":{"method":"property"},"ref":"AGG-034","area":"07-content","section":"Aggregate copies","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-15","boundaryDetail":"`copy key`","traces":["g-618","k-7","d-5065"],"milestone":6,"inSection":"sec-content-256","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"agg-040","kind":"requirement","statement":"An aggregate SHALL read the records of one tenant only.","rationale":"No query of tenant data spans tenants (NG-6).","evaluate":{"method":"property"},"ref":"AGG-040","area":"07-content","section":"Aggregate scope and delivery","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-9","boundaryDetail":"`aggregate result`","traces":["g-619","ng-6","d-5066"],"milestone":6,"inSection":"sec-content-257","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"agg-041","kind":"requirement","statement":"A view section that names an aggregate SHALL deliver the result of that aggregate for the reader in place of rows.","rationale":"A leaderboard or a progress figure is delivered like any other part of a view.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"AGG-041","area":"07-content","section":"Aggregate scope and delivery","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-9","boundaryDetail":"`view`","traces":["g-615","d-5067","g-31"],"milestone":6,"inSection":"sec-content-257","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"agg-042","kind":"requirement","statement":"The result of an aggregate SHALL name the object types it depends on.","rationale":"Invalidation is exact because the kernel says what an answer was made from (CPY-004).","evaluate":{"method":"property"},"ref":"AGG-042","area":"07-content","section":"Aggregate scope and delivery","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`strata_kernel::read`","traces":["g-618","d-14","d-5064"],"milestone":6,"inSection":"sec-content-257","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"m-ag-result-is-current","kind":"invariant","models":"agg-031","statement":"A result that is served is the result of the revision of the object types at the time of the request.","evaluate":{"method":"state-invariant","scenarios":["ag-commit-between","ag-repeat-ask"],"expr":"ag-copy-flow.asks == 0 || ag-copy-flow.servedRevision == ag-copy-flow.askedRevision","negatives":[{"scenario":"ag-commit-between","faults":["defect-ag-serve-stale"]}]},"faultModel":"fault-model-launch","assumptions":["a-model-abstraction"],"faultBasis":"fault"},
    {"id":"m-ag-result-stays-in-its-class","kind":"invariant","models":"agg-032","statement":"A result that is served was stored for the audience class of the reader who asked.","evaluate":{"method":"state-invariant","scenarios":["ag-two-classes","ag-repeat-ask"],"expr":"ag-copy-flow.asks == 0 || ag-copy-flow.servedClass == ag-copy-flow.askedClass","negatives":[{"scenario":"ag-two-classes","faults":["defect-ag-serve-other-class"]}]},"faultModel":"fault-model-launch","assumptions":["a-model-abstraction"],"faultBasis":"restatement"},
    {"id":"m-ag-never-partial","kind":"invariant","models":"agg-021","statement":"An aggregate that would examine more records than its bound is never answered in part.","evaluate":{"method":"state-invariant","scenarios":["ag-over-bound"],"expr":"ag-copy-flow.partial == 0","negatives":[{"scenario":"ag-over-bound","faults":["defect-ag-answer-partial"]}]},"faultModel":"fault-model-launch","assumptions":["a-model-abstraction"],"faultBasis":"restatement"},
    {"id":"m-ag-bound-refused","kind":"temporal","models":"agg-020","statement":"An aggregate that would examine more records than its bound is refused by name.","evaluate":{"method":"eventually","scenarios":["ag-over-bound"],"occurs":{"event":"ag-refused-bound"},"negatives":[{"scenario":"ag-over-bound","faults":["ag-bound-refusal-disabled"]}]},"faultModel":"fault-model-launch","assumptions":["a-model-abstraction"],"faultBasis":"restatement"},
    {"id":"m-ag-result-is-reused","kind":"temporal","models":"agg-030","statement":"A second request of the same audience class under the same key is answered from the stored result.","evaluate":{"method":"eventually","scenarios":["ag-repeat-ask"],"occurs":{"event":"ag-served-from-copy"},"negatives":[{"scenario":"ag-repeat-ask","faults":["ag-copy-serving-disabled"]}]},"faultModel":"fault-model-launch","assumptions":["a-model-abstraction"],"faultBasis":"restatement"},
    {"id":"m-ag-recomputed-after-commit","kind":"temporal","models":"agg-031","statement":"A request after a commit to an object type the aggregate reads is computed again from the records.","evaluate":{"method":"eventually","scenarios":["ag-commit-between"],"expr":"ag-copy-flow.computed == 2","negatives":[{"scenario":"ag-commit-between","faults":["ag-computing-disabled"]}]},"faultModel":"fault-model-launch","assumptions":["a-model-abstraction"],"faultBasis":"fault"},
    {"id":"cms-1020","kind":"requirement","statement":"The Markdown parser SHALL read at most 200000 bytes of a source, nest quotes at most 8 deep and inline markup at most 8 deep, keeping what is nested deeper as text, so that no source overflows the stack or takes more than linear time per level.","rationale":"A request or a tenant record field made of nested quote markers or unmatched brackets otherwise stops the process for every tenant.","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"CMS-1020","area":"07-content","section":"Markup and expressions","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-9","boundaryDetail":"`strata_substrate::markdown::parse`","traces":["k-12"],"milestone":2,"inSection":"sec-content-250","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"adm-1080","kind":"requirement","statement":"Revoking a role from a person, revoking a role from a team and removing a person from a team SHALL be refused unless the acting principal could confer that role under ADM-152, for every role the team holds when a person is removed from it.","rationale":"Taking a role away is as strong as giving it: a member manager who may not hand out the owner or an editor role otherwise strips it from every holder.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"ADM-1080","area":"09-administration","section":"Roles and teams","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`strata_kernel::transition`","traces":["g-153","k-13"],"milestone":3,"inSection":"sec-administration-2","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"adm-1081","kind":"requirement","statement":"A change that revokes a role from a person, revokes a role from a team or removes a person from a team SHALL be refused when it would leave a tenant that has an owner without any principal holding the owner role, counting the owner role held through a team as well as the role assigned directly.","rationale":"A tenant with no owner cannot be administered again, and a count that ignores teams is passed by a revocation made through a team.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"ADM-1081","area":"09-administration","section":"Roles and teams","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`strata_kernel::transition`","traces":["g-153","k-13"],"milestone":3,"inSection":"sec-administration-2","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"adm-1085","kind":"requirement","statement":"A role SHALL be treated as granting the powers that the policies of the tenant give it as well as the permissions listed for it, so that conferring it under ADM-152 asks the acting principal to hold every one of those powers.","rationale":"A role that lists no permission but is empowered by a policy would otherwise be handed out by anyone who manages members.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"ADM-1085","area":"09-administration","section":"Roles and teams","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`strata_kernel::transition`","traces":["g-153","k-13"],"milestone":3,"inSection":"sec-administration-2","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"adm-1082","kind":"requirement","statement":"An invitation SHALL record the time at which it expires, fourteen days after it was issued, and SHALL NOT be redeemed at or after that time or when it records none.","rationale":"An invitation that never lapses is a standing grant of roles to anyone who later controls the address.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"ADM-1082","area":"09-administration","section":"Invitations and onboarding","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`strata_kernel::transition`","traces":["g-153","k-13"],"milestone":3,"inSection":"sec-administration-3","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"adm-1083","kind":"requirement","statement":"A principal who manages members and could confer every role that an invitation offers SHALL be able to revoke it before it is redeemed, and a revoked invitation SHALL NOT be redeemed.","rationale":"An invitation issued in error or to the wrong address needs a way to be withdrawn.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"ADM-1083","area":"09-administration","section":"Invitations and onboarding","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`strata_kernel::transition`","traces":["g-153","k-13"],"milestone":3,"inSection":"sec-administration-3","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"adm-1084","kind":"requirement","statement":"Redeeming an invitation SHALL be refused unless its issuer still manages members and could confer every role that the invitation offers at the time of redemption.","rationale":"The invitation stands on the authority of the person who issued it, so an invitation from someone who has since been demoted grants nothing.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"ADM-1084","area":"09-administration","section":"Invitations and onboarding","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`strata_kernel::transition`","traces":["g-153","k-13"],"milestone":3,"inSection":"sec-administration-3","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"krn-1080","kind":"requirement","statement":"A request to create, update or delete a record that the acting principal has no permission to make SHALL be refused with the same error whether or not the object type or the record exists, and only a principal who may make the request SHALL be told that the type or the record is missing.","rationale":"A refusal that differs between a missing and an existing record lets a caller with no permission list which ids and object types exist.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"KRN-1080","area":"01-core","section":"Decisions","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`strata_kernel::transition`","traces":["g-24","g-11"],"milestone":3,"inSection":"sec-kernel-2","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"ops-1260","kind":"requirement","statement":"A write that carries an idempotency key SHALL record the key in the tenant's own database, in the same atomic step as the commit, scoped by the tenant and by the principal that chose it, so that a key is unknown to every other principal and every other tenant.","rationale":"A key recorded after the commit, or in a shared place, can be lost or leak between callers: a retry then commits twice or reads another caller's result.","evaluate":{"method":"property"},"ref":"OPS-1260","area":"09-operations","section":"Failure containment","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-2","boundaryDetail":"`strata_storage_api::Store::commit`","traces":["g-15","g-14"],"milestone":2,"inSection":"sec-operations-6","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"ops-1261","kind":"requirement","statement":"A request that repeats an idempotency key which the tenant has recorded for the same principal, with the same intent, SHALL receive the output, evidence, revision and event sequence of the first request without a second decision and without a second commit, including after the process has restarted, and a commit that loses a race SHALL look the key up again before it decides again so that two concurrent requests with one key commit once.","rationale":"A client that retries after a lost reply or a restart must change the tenant once and learn what the first request did.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"OPS-1261","area":"09-operations","section":"Failure containment","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-2","boundaryDetail":"`strata_storage_api::execute_by`","traces":["g-15","g-14"],"milestone":2,"inSection":"sec-operations-6","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"ops-1262","kind":"requirement","statement":"A request that repeats an idempotency key with an intent different from the one the key was first used with SHALL be refused as an invalid intent and SHALL commit nothing.","rationale":"A reused key is a client defect; answering it with the first result would report a change the caller did not ask for.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"OPS-1262","area":"09-operations","section":"Failure containment","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-2","boundaryDetail":"`strata_storage_api::execute_by`","traces":["g-15","g-14"],"milestone":2,"inSection":"sec-operations-6","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"ops-1263","kind":"requirement","statement":"A tenant database SHALL keep an idempotency key for 24 hours from the commit that recorded it and SHALL forget it afterwards, after which the same key names a new request; each commit SHALL delete the keys past that period in its own transaction.","rationale":"Keys that are kept forever grow the tenant database without bound; a stated period tells a client how long a retry is safe.","evaluate":{"method":"property"},"ref":"OPS-1263","area":"09-operations","section":"Failure containment","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-2","boundaryDetail":"`strata_storage_api::IDEMPOTENCY_RETENTION_MS`","traces":["g-15","g-14"],"milestone":2,"inSection":"sec-operations-6","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"ops-1264","kind":"requirement","statement":"An idempotency key SHALL be 1 to 255 visible ASCII characters, a request with a malformed key SHALL be refused before any work is done, and a request with a key from a caller who is not signed in SHALL be refused, because every anonymous caller is one principal.","rationale":"A bounded key keeps the record small, and a key shared by all anonymous callers would let one read another's first result.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"OPS-1264","area":"09-operations","section":"Failure containment","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-2","boundaryDetail":"`Idempotency-Key`","traces":["g-15","g-14"],"milestone":2,"inSection":"sec-operations-6","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"ops-1265","kind":"requirement","statement":"A write SHALL NOT be committed after the deadline of its request has passed: the deadline is the instant at which the request is answered as timed out, it SHALL be checked immediately before the commit, and a write refused for that reason SHALL report that nothing was committed. A caller that was told the request timed out SHALL learn the outcome by repeating the request with the same idempotency key.","rationale":"A timeout that cancels nothing leaves a write that commits after the caller was told it failed, so that a retry duplicates it.","evaluate":{"method":"property"},"ref":"OPS-1265","area":"09-operations","section":"Failure containment","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-2","boundaryDetail":"`strata_runtime::server::work_deadline`","traces":["g-15","g-14"],"milestone":2,"inSection":"sec-operations-6","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"krn-1280","kind":"requirement","statement":"The kernel SHALL refuse a record that holds a string longer than 65536 bytes, a list of more than 1000 items, or that is larger than 262144 bytes in its JSON encoding, with the error limit-exceeded.","rationale":"A tenant that can store a string or a list of any size makes every later read of that record cost that much, for every request.","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"KRN-1280","area":"01-core","section":"Limits and paging","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`strata_kernel::transition`","traces":["g-4"],"milestone":1,"inSection":"sec-kernel-1280","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"krn-1281","kind":"requirement","statement":"The kernel SHALL refuse a value in a unique field whose JSON encoding is longer than 200 bytes, with the error limit-exceeded, so that a lookup of a unique value is always served by an index.","rationale":"A long unique value is not indexed, so each create would otherwise scan the object type.","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"KRN-1281","area":"01-core","section":"Limits and paging","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`strata_kernel::transition`","traces":["g-4"],"milestone":1,"inSection":"sec-kernel-1280","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"krn-1282","kind":"requirement","statement":"The kernel SHALL refuse a schema that defines more than 200 object types, 100 fields in one object type, 500 policies or 500 named queries, or a named query whose limit is not from 1 to 200, with the error invalid-schema.","rationale":"A schema is loaded on every request, so its size is the cost of every request of the tenant.","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"KRN-1282","area":"01-core","section":"Limits and paging","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`strata_kernel::transition`","traces":["g-4"],"milestone":1,"inSection":"sec-kernel-1280","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"krn-1283","kind":"requirement","statement":"The kernel SHALL refuse a ChangeSchema intent that carries more than 200 changes, with the error limit-exceeded.","rationale":"One intent cannot ask the platform to rebuild a schema without a bound.","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"KRN-1283","area":"01-core","section":"Limits and paging","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`strata_kernel::transition`","traces":["g-4"],"milestone":1,"inSection":"sec-kernel-1280","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"krn-1284","kind":"requirement","statement":"The kernel SHALL refuse a read of records that names more than 200 ids, with the error limit-exceeded.","rationale":"A list of ids is a list of loads, and the reader chooses its length.","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"KRN-1284","area":"01-core","section":"Limits and paging","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`strata_kernel::read`","traces":["g-4"],"milestone":1,"inSection":"sec-kernel-1280","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"krn-1285","kind":"requirement","statement":"A read of a named query SHALL take an optional page size and an optional cursor and SHALL return a cursor when more rows may follow. The page size is the one the read names, else the limit the query declares, else 50, and it SHALL be refused with the error limit-exceeded when it is above 200.","rationale":"A query with no limit returns a page, not the whole object type.","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"KRN-1285","area":"01-core","section":"Limits and paging","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`strata_kernel::read`","traces":["g-4"],"milestone":1,"inSection":"sec-kernel-1280","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"krn-1286","kind":"requirement","statement":"A read of a named query that has no filter and orders by nothing or by the record id ascending SHALL load at most 200 records of the object type, whatever their number, and SHALL return a cursor that continues after the last record it examined.","rationale":"Such a query is served by a window of the object type in id order, so its cost does not grow with the table.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"KRN-1286","area":"01-core","section":"Limits and paging","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`strata_kernel::read`","traces":["g-4"],"milestone":1,"inSection":"sec-kernel-1280","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"krn-1287","kind":"requirement","statement":"A named query that has a filter or an order that no index plan serves (KRN-2520) SHALL be served by a scan of its object type, and its cursor SHALL be an offset into the sorted rows.","rationale":"A filter or an order that no index answers needs every record, so it is not served by a window or an index. This states which queries are bounded and which are not.","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"KRN-1287","area":"01-core","section":"Limits and paging","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`strata_kernel::read`","traces":["g-4"],"milestone":1,"inSection":"sec-kernel-1280","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"krn-1288","kind":"requirement","statement":"A read of a named query that is served by a scan SHALL be refused with the error limit-exceeded when its object type holds more than 10000 records, and it SHALL load no more than 10001 records to decide so.","rationale":"This is the bound on what a plan may read (CMS-255): the same number as the platform maximum of an aggregate scan bound (AGG-023).","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"KRN-1288","area":"01-core","section":"Limits and paging","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`strata_kernel::read`","traces":["g-4"],"milestone":1,"inSection":"sec-kernel-1280","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"run-1380","kind":"requirement","statement":"The backend SHALL write every authentication decision and every security audit event to the audit trail of the tenant it concerns, in the store, before the request that caused it is answered, so that the entry survives a restart; the in-memory rings of recent decisions and recent events SHALL be a cache for diagnostics only, kept apart from each other so that a flood of sign-in decisions cannot push a security event out of its ring, and the backend SHALL log every decision.","rationale":"A trail held in a bounded ring in memory loses its oldest entries to a flood of failed sign-ins and all of them at a restart, so it cannot explain a past decision (IDN-021).","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"RUN-1380","area":"01-core","section":"Production safety of the backend","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-19","boundaryDetail":"`audit trail`","traces":["g-11","g-30"],"milestone":2,"inSection":"sec-runtime-1380","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"run-1381","kind":"requirement","statement":"The route that reports every tenant's diagnostics SHALL answer not found unless the backend was started for development, because the backend holds no operator identity to hold a caller to and the service token it requires is shared with the gateway, and each call to it in development SHALL be an audit entry; a tenant's own diagnostics SHALL contain no other tenant's identifier and no count or health detail that spans tenants.","rationale":"A holder of the shared service token otherwise reads every tenant's sessions and audit entries with no grant and no record, and a tenant learns which other tenants fail and how busy they are.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"RUN-1381","area":"01-core","section":"Production safety of the backend","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-19","boundaryDetail":"`/internal/platform/diagnostics`","traces":["g-27","g-30"],"milestone":2,"inSection":"sec-runtime-1380","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"run-1382","kind":"requirement","statement":"The development routes of the backend (/internal/dev/reset, /internal/dev/expire-session, /internal/dev/outbox, /internal/dev/age-authentication, /internal/dev/mail-outbox, /internal/dev/clock and /internal/dev/identity-outage) SHALL be compiled only into a build made with the cargo feature development and mounted only when STRATA_DEV is 1, and a backend built without that feature SHALL refuse to start when STRATA_DEV is 1, naming the feature.","rationale":"A production binary that carries a clock-skew switch, an outage switch and a fixture reset is one environment variable away from using them.","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"RUN-1382","area":"01-core","section":"Production safety of the backend","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-19","boundaryDetail":"`development feature`","traces":["g-27"],"milestone":2,"inSection":"sec-runtime-1380","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"run-1383","kind":"requirement","statement":"A backend that was not started for development SHALL refuse to start, naming STRATA_SMTP_URL, when no SMTP server is configured, and SHALL refuse to start, naming STRATA_TENANTS, when the directory of tenant bundles does not exist.","rationale":"A start that keeps mail in memory and sends none loses every sign-in link and recovery message without saying so, and a start without tenants serves nothing without saying why.","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"RUN-1383","area":"01-core","section":"Production safety of the backend","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-19","boundaryDetail":"`startup`","traces":["g-27"],"milestone":2,"inSection":"sec-runtime-1380","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"run-1384","kind":"requirement","statement":"The backend SHALL log each failed purge of its janitor with the name of what it purged, SHALL give the outbox publisher telemetry that is written to the log, and SHALL report in its health answer whether the publisher is running and how many of its ticks failed, answering not ok when the publisher has stopped.","rationale":"A purge or a publisher that fails without a trace leaves expired sessions to accumulate and committed events unpublished while health reports ok.","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"RUN-1384","area":"01-core","section":"Production safety of the backend","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-19","boundaryDetail":"`/internal/health`","traces":["g-27"],"milestone":2,"inSection":"sec-runtime-1380","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"run-1385","kind":"requirement","statement":"The backend SHALL NOT write the verified address of the acting person into the journal entry of a transition; the journal context SHALL hold the tenant, principal, session, time and correlation only.","rationale":"The journal is kept for good, and a person's address written into every entry outlives the account and any request to erase it.","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"RUN-1385","area":"01-core","section":"Production safety of the backend","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-19","boundaryDetail":"`journal entry`","traces":["g-11"],"milestone":2,"inSection":"sec-runtime-1380","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"run-1386","kind":"requirement","statement":"The backend SHALL answer not found to a request for a Lean verification run (/internal/lab/verify) unless it was started for development.","rationale":"The verification run starts the build tool of the Lean project on the machine, which a production backend has no reason to do for any schema manager.","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"RUN-1386","area":"01-core","section":"Production safety of the backend","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-19","boundaryDetail":"`/internal/lab/verify`","traces":["g-27"],"milestone":2,"inSection":"sec-runtime-1380","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"run-1387","kind":"requirement","statement":"The backend SHALL read its configuration from these environment variables and no others (a variable that an OIDC provider entry names in client_secret_env is the one exception, because the operator chooses its name); an unset or empty variable takes the default given in brackets, and a whole-number variable that is not a number is a refusal to start, except STRATA_DRAIN_TIMEOUT_SECS, which takes its default when it is not a positive number. Address and secrets: STRATA_BACKEND_ADDR, the loopback address to listen on [127.0.0.1:4101]; STRATA_SERVICE_TOKEN, the secret the gateway presents, at least 24 characters [none: required]. STRATA_OPERATOR_TOKEN, the secret the platform operator presents in the x-strata-operator header to read the platform diagnostics, at least 24 characters and not the service token [unset: the platform diagnostics answer \"not found\" outside development]. Storage: STRATA_STORE, the adapter, sqlite or memory [sqlite]; STRATA_DB, the control database file [var/strata.db]; STRATA_TENANT_FILES, the directory of tenant database files [<database name>-tenants beside the control database]; STRATA_TENANTS, the directory of tenant bundles, which must exist outside development [tenants]; STRATA_LEAN_DIR, the Lean project the verification run builds [lean]. Mode: STRATA_DEV, 1 to start for development, which needs the development cargo feature [unset]. Sessions and sign-in: STRATA_SESSION_TTL_MS, the absolute session lifetime [43200000]; STRATA_SESSION_IDLE_MS, the idle session lifetime [7200000]; STRATA_PASSKEY_CHALLENGE_TTL_MS, the life of a passkey challenge [300000]; STRATA_LINK_TTL_MS, the life of an emailed sign-in link [900000]. Mail: STRATA_SMTP_URL, the SMTP server, required outside development [unset]; STRATA_MAIL_FROM, the sender address for it [unset]; STRATA_MAIL_DIR, where the development sink writes messages [var/mail]. Federation: STRATA_OIDC_CONFIG and STRATA_SAML_CONFIG, the files that list the OIDC and SAML providers [unset: no provider]. Second factors: STRATA_SECOND_FACTOR_REALMS, the comma-separated tenants whose policy requires a second factor [none]; STRATA_STEP_UP_AGE_MS, how recent a sign-in must be for a sensitive action [900000]; STRATA_RECOVERY_DELAY_MS, the wait between a recovery request and its completion [86400000]; STRATA_FACTOR_KEY, the key that seals factor secrets and signing keys, at least 32 characters and not the service token, required outside development [the built-in key in development]; STRATA_FACTOR_KEY_PREVIOUS, the comma-separated earlier keys that still open what they sealed, each held to the same rules as STRATA_FACTOR_KEY, for a rotation [none]. Limits, each at least 1: STRATA_SOCKETS_PER_SESSION [8]; STRATA_SOCKETS_PER_SOURCE [32]; STRATA_DIAG_PER_SOCKET, browser log lines per development socket [50]; STRATA_DIAG_PER_SOURCE, browser log lines per source per minute [200]; STRATA_LOGINS_PER_SOURCE, sign-in attempts per source per minute [30]; STRATA_ARGON2_MEMORY_MIB, the memory that concurrent password hashes may take together [64]; STRATA_ARGON2_WAIT_MS, how long a sign-in waits for a place to hash [3000]; STRATA_ARGON2_PER_TENANT, the hashes one tenant may hold at once [2]; STRATA_BLOCKING_PER_TENANT, the blocking store calls one tenant may have running or waiting [16]; STRATA_BLOCKING_QUEUE, the blocking store calls all tenants together may have running or waiting [256]; STRATA_LAB_WORKERS, threads that run Impact Lab projections [2]; STRATA_LAB_QUEUE, projections that may wait for a thread [4]; STRATA_LAB_RUNS_PER_TENANT, projections one tenant may have running or waiting [2]; STRATA_VERIFY_INTERVAL_MS, the least time between two verification runs of a tenant [60000]. Connection handling, read by the shared server of the backend and the gateway, each a positive number: STRATA_HEADER_TIMEOUT_SECS, the time a client has to finish its request headers [10]; STRATA_REQUEST_TIMEOUT_SECS, the time a request has to be answered before it gets 408 [30]; STRATA_WRITE_IDLE_TIMEOUT_SECS, the time a client may stop reading before its connection is dropped [30]; STRATA_MAX_CONNECTIONS, open connections in all [2048]; STRATA_MAX_CONNECTIONS_PER_SOURCE, open connections from one peer address [512]; STRATA_DRAIN_TIMEOUT_SECS, the time open connections have to finish after a stop is asked for [30].","rationale":"A variable that the specification does not name is configuration an operator cannot find, review or refuse.","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"RUN-1387","area":"01-core","section":"Production safety of the backend","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-19","boundaryDetail":"`environment`","traces":["g-27"],"milestone":2,"inSection":"sec-runtime-1380","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"gwy-1400","kind":"requirement","statement":"The gateway SHALL read its configuration from these environment variables and no others; an unset or empty variable takes the default given in brackets, and a whole-number variable that is not a number is a refusal to start, except STRATA_DRAIN_TIMEOUT_SECS, which takes its default when it is not a positive number. STRATA_BFF_ADDR, the address to listen on [127.0.0.1:4100]; STRATA_BACKEND_URL, the base URL of the backend [http://127.0.0.1:4101]; STRATA_SERVICE_TOKEN, the secret it presents to the backend, at least 24 characters [none: required]; STRATA_SITES, the comma-separated host=tenant pairs this deployment serves, required outside development [in development: 127.0.0.1=fieldnotes, localhost=fieldnotes and tidewater.localhost=tidewater]; STRATA_ORIGINS, the comma-separated origins allowed to make state-changing requests [every site host on the gateway's port and on port 5173]; STRATA_WEB_DIST, the directory of the built web application [web/dist]; STRATA_DEV, 1 to start for development [unset]; STRATA_TRUSTED_PROXIES, the comma-separated proxy addresses whose forwarded-address header is believed [none]; STRATA_BFF_TOKEN_SECRET, the secret that request tokens are derived from [the service token outside development; random in development]; STRATA_BFF_SOCKETS_PER_SESSION, the sockets one session may hold open [8]; STRATA_BFF_SOCKETS_PER_SOURCE, the sockets one source may hold open [32]; STRATA_BFF_REQUESTS_PER_MINUTE, the requests one source may make per minute [600]; STRATA_HOSTS_MAX_AGE_SECS, the age at which the list of hosts learned from the backend is fetched again [60]; STRATA_HOSTS_MISS_INTERVAL_SECS, the least time between two calls to the backend for that list [5]; and, read by the shared server, STRATA_HEADER_TIMEOUT_SECS [10], STRATA_REQUEST_TIMEOUT_SECS [30], STRATA_WRITE_IDLE_TIMEOUT_SECS [30], STRATA_MAX_CONNECTIONS [2048], STRATA_MAX_CONNECTIONS_PER_SOURCE [512] and STRATA_DRAIN_TIMEOUT_SECS [30], each as the backend reads it.","rationale":"A variable that the specification does not name is configuration an operator cannot find, review or refuse.","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"GWY-1400","area":"01-core","section":"Production configuration of the gateway","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-9","boundaryDetail":"`environment`","traces":["g-250"],"milestone":2,"inSection":"sec-runtime-1420","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"gwy-1401","kind":"requirement","statement":"A gateway that is not started for development (STRATA_DEV unset) SHALL refuse to start, naming STRATA_SITES, when STRATA_SITES is unset, and SHALL serve no demonstration tenant unless started for development.","rationale":"A production start that falls back to demonstration tenants on loopback host names serves a real tenant at addresses nobody chose.","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"GWY-1401","area":"01-core","section":"Production configuration of the gateway","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-9","boundaryDetail":"`STRATA_SITES`","traces":["g-250"],"milestone":2,"inSection":"sec-runtime-1420","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"gwy-1402","kind":"requirement","statement":"The key of the request tokens that the gateway issues to browsers without a session SHALL come from configuration (STRATA_BFF_TOKEN_SECRET, or the shared service token when that is unset) outside development, so that a token survives a restart and is accepted by every instance of one deployment; only a process started for development MAY draw a random key.","rationale":"A key drawn per process refuses every anonymous browser's sign-in after a restart, a rolling deploy or when a second instance answers.","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"GWY-1402","area":"01-core","section":"Production configuration of the gateway","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-9","boundaryDetail":"`request token`","traces":["g-250"],"milestone":2,"inSection":"sec-runtime-1420","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"gwy-1403","kind":"requirement","statement":"A response under /assets/ SHALL carry the year-long immutable cache header only when its status is a success, and the gateway SHALL answer a request for a source map (a path ending in .map) under /assets/ with 404.","rationale":"A failure cached for a year by a browser or a content delivery network outlasts the deploy that caused it, and a source map published to everyone discloses the application's source.","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"GWY-1403","area":"01-core","section":"Production configuration of the gateway","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-9","boundaryDetail":"`Cache-Control`","traces":["g-250"],"milestone":2,"inSection":"sec-runtime-1420","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"gwy-1404","kind":"requirement","statement":"Every response SHALL carry a Permissions-Policy header, and a gateway one of whose configured origins is https SHALL add Strict-Transport-Security and the upgrade-insecure-requests directive to the Content-Security-Policy of its responses.","rationale":"A browser that is not told to use https only reaches the site over https after a first plain request, and features the page does not use stay available to any script that runs.","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"GWY-1404","area":"01-core","section":"Production configuration of the gateway","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-9","boundaryDetail":"`Strict-Transport-Security`","traces":["g-250"],"milestone":2,"inSection":"sec-runtime-1420","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"gwy-1405","kind":"requirement","statement":"The gateway SHALL limit the page requests and view reads of one source address to a number per minute that STRATA_BFF_REQUESTS_PER_MINUTE sets, answering the excess with 429 and a Retry-After header, and SHALL log a warning once when a request carries X-Forwarded-For while STRATA_TRUSTED_PROXIES is empty.","rationale":"Every unknown address costs two backend calls and the gateway otherwise has no limit on them; behind a proxy that is not trusted, every visitor shares one source address.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"GWY-1405","area":"01-core","section":"Production configuration of the gateway","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-9","boundaryDetail":"`source address`","traces":["g-250"],"milestone":2,"inSection":"sec-runtime-1420","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"gwy-1406","kind":"requirement","statement":"A sign-out request SHALL clear the session cookie in its response even when the call to the backend fails, answering with the failure.","rationale":"A visitor who cannot leave while the backend is unavailable keeps a credential in a browser they meant to give up.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"GWY-1406","area":"01-core","section":"Production configuration of the gateway","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-9","boundaryDetail":"`POST /api/logout`","traces":["g-250"],"milestone":2,"inSection":"sec-runtime-1420","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"gwy-1407","kind":"requirement","statement":"On SIGTERM or an interrupt a server SHALL stop accepting connections, let its open connections finish for at most STRATA_DRAIN_TIMEOUT_SECS seconds (default 30), and then drop those still open.","rationale":"An orchestrator that sends SIGTERM and a process that ignores it ends in a kill with no drain, and a drain with no deadline never ends.","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"GWY-1407","area":"01-core","section":"Production configuration of the gateway","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-9","boundaryDetail":"`SIGTERM`","traces":["g-250"],"milestone":2,"inSection":"sec-runtime-1420","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"gwy-1408","kind":"requirement","statement":"The diagnostics that the gateway returns to a tenant SHALL contain no count that spans tenants, including the gateway's open sockets and requests in flight.","rationale":"A tenant's schema manager otherwise learns how busy the other tenants are.","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"GWY-1408","area":"01-core","section":"Production configuration of the gateway","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-9","boundaryDetail":"`/api/diagnostics`","traces":["g-250"],"milestone":2,"inSection":"sec-runtime-1420","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"gwy-1409","kind":"requirement","statement":"The origin that the gateway publishes in the SAML metadata of a site SHALL be the first https origin of the site in alphabetical order, or when it has none the first origin of the site in alphabetical order, whatever order the origins were configured in.","rationale":"A provider's administrator who is given a development origin configures the provider against an address that does not serve the site.","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"GWY-1409","area":"01-core","section":"Production configuration of the gateway","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-9","boundaryDetail":"`SAML metadata`","traces":["g-250"],"milestone":2,"inSection":"sec-runtime-1420","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"ten-1200","kind":"requirement","statement":"The archive of a tenant export SHALL contain no credential, session, challenge, API grant, identity provider secret, connector secret or delivery key.","rationale":"An archive leaves the platform as a file, so it holds what the owner needs to leave with and nothing that signs a person in or opens another system (ADM-161, D-6200).","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"TEN-1200","area":"02-tenancy","section":"Life cycle","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-3","boundaryDetail":"`POST /tenants/{id}/export`","traces":["g-1","d-6200","d-701"],"milestone":2,"realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"ten-1201","kind":"requirement","statement":"An import of a tenant archive SHALL create each person without a credential and without a session, SHALL issue one bootstrap credential for the first owner as provisioning does (TEN-500), and SHALL leave every provider secret, connector secret, delivery key and API grant to be entered or issued again.","rationale":"A restored archive does not bring back the sign-in of anyone, so an archive that is stolen or imported twice signs nobody in (D-6200).","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"TEN-1201","area":"02-tenancy","section":"Life cycle","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-3","boundaryDetail":"`import`","traces":["g-1","d-6200"],"milestone":2,"realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"idn-1202","kind":"requirement","statement":"A contract on the list of sensitive operations of D-6201 SHALL state a step-up age in its authorisation and a step-up-required error of kind forbidden, a call refused for want of a fresh authentication SHALL change nothing, and a specification that lists such a contract without both SHALL be refused.","rationale":"One list says which operations need a fresh authentication, and a contract that is on it cannot omit the check without the specification failing (D-6201).","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"IDN-1202","area":"03-identity","section":"Factors, step-up and recovery","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-4","boundaryDetail":"`stepUp`","traces":["g-8","d-6201","d-4915"],"milestone":3,"realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"ops-1203","kind":"requirement","statement":"No tenant role SHALL hold the capability that changes a platform flag or a quota, and a tenant SHALL change only a tenant switch that the release record of a flag defines, and turn it on only where the release record enables the flag for that tenant.","rationale":"A tenant that sets its own quota or enables a platform-gated flag has no limit (D-6202, OPS-328).","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"OPS-1203","area":"09-operations","section":"Releases and change","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-19","boundaryDetail":"`flags-manage`","traces":["g-303","g-4","d-6202"],"milestone":12,"realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"bil-1204","kind":"requirement","statement":"A plan change by an owner SHALL be refused unless the billing account of the tenant is in good standing, and a change to or from the Enterprise plan SHALL be refused unless the platform operator has recorded a contract for the tenant.","rationale":"Enterprise quotas are set by contract (D-508), so a tenant cannot choose them for itself (D-6202).","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"BIL-1204","area":"02-tenancy","section":"Plans","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-3","boundaryDetail":"`change-plan`","traces":["g-157","d-508","d-6202"],"milestone":12,"realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"cnv-1205","kind":"requirement","statement":"The assistant SHALL be available to a tenant only while the release record of the assistant flag enables it for the tenant and an owner of the tenant has turned it on, and an owner SHALL NOT be able to turn on a flag that the release record has not enabled.","rationale":"CNV-500 and OPS-328 both hold: the release record is the platform gate and the owner is the tenant switch inside it (D-6202).","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"CNV-1205","area":"09-conversation","section":"Model provider","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-11","boundaryDetail":"`assistant-flag`","traces":["g-205","d-514","d-6202"],"milestone":12,"realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"sec-1206","kind":"requirement","statement":"A platform component SHALL present a service credential that carries the service role of that component alone, and a service call SHALL be refused with forbidden unless the capability it needs is conferred by that role.","rationale":"A compromised component reaches what its own role reaches and no more (SEC-004, D-6203).","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"SEC-1206","area":"08-platform","section":"Keys and credentials","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-6","boundaryDetail":"`component credential`","traces":["k-6","g-12","g-266","d-6203"],"milestone":2,"realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"sec-1207","kind":"requirement","statement":"The audit log SHALL derive the actor of an entry from the credential of the calling component and SHALL accept no actor from the caller, and it SHALL refuse an entry whose tenant is not the tenant that the credential names (TEN-257).","rationale":"A component that could name its own actor could forge the history of any tenant (D-6203).","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"SEC-1207","area":"08-platform","section":"Keys and credentials","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-12","boundaryDetail":"`append-audit-entry`","traces":["g-30","g-266","d-6203"],"milestone":2,"realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"sec-1208","kind":"requirement","statement":"Ending the sessions of a principal SHALL need the capability session-end, and a component that holds only the capability session-verify SHALL be refused.","rationale":"Looking a session up and ending it are different powers (D-6203).","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"SEC-1208","area":"08-platform","section":"Keys and credentials","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-4","boundaryDetail":"`end-principal-sessions`","traces":["g-9","g-266","d-6203"],"milestone":3,"realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"agt-1209","kind":"requirement","statement":"An invocation through the operation catalogue SHALL be refused with forbidden unless the caller holds every capability that the authorisation of the underlying contract requires and one of its roles. For example, an author who invokes the catalogue entry of delete-tenant, export-tenant or issue-access-grant is refused, nothing is changed, and the refusal is audited.","rationale":"The catalogue is another way to reach a contract and not a way round its authorisation (AGT-014, D-6210).","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"AGT-1209","area":"06-agents","section":"Authorise, attribute and limit","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-11","boundaryDetail":"`invoke-operation`","traces":["k-13","g-25","d-6210"],"milestone":7,"realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"prv-1210","kind":"requirement","statement":"A support grant SHALL record its purpose and its scope, SHALL expire at most 72 hours after it is issued, SHALL be issued only to a holder of the role support or platform-operator, and SHALL NOT be issued, and every request made under it SHALL be refused, when the tenant sets forbid-platform-access, or when the grant is expired, withdrawn or issued for another tenant or another operator.","rationale":"A grant is a bounded and purposeful permission, and the tenant can say no (D-352, D-6204).","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"PRV-1210","area":"09-privacy","section":"Access by platform staff","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-350","boundaryDetail":"`POST /tenants/{id}/access-grants`","traces":["g-354","g-165","d-352","d-6204"],"milestone":10,"realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"prv-1211","kind":"requirement","statement":"A diagnostic that platform staff or the platform operating agent run in a tenant SHALL be refused unless a live support grant of that tenant covers it, and the run SHALL be audited with the grant.","rationale":"An operator acts in a tenant only under a grant, diagnostics included (G-165, D-6204).","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"PRV-1211","area":"09-privacy","section":"Access by platform staff","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-350","boundaryDetail":"`run-diagnostic`","traces":["g-354","g-165","d-6204"],"milestone":10,"realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"ten-1212","kind":"requirement","statement":"A restore of a tenant SHALL leave every session, challenge, API grant and support grant ended, SHALL leave removed role assignments, team memberships and credentials, rotated or removed secrets, and withdrawn support grants removed as they were after the restore point, and SHALL NOT lift a legal hold.","rationale":"A restore that brings back revoked access gives an attacker the old access again (D-6206).","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"TEN-1212","area":"02-tenancy","section":"Life cycle","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-3","boundaryDetail":"`tenant restore`","traces":["g-39","g-266","d-6206"],"milestone":12,"realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"ops-1213","kind":"requirement","statement":"The restorable window of a tenant database SHALL be 30 days unless the tenant chooses another and SHALL NOT be shorter than 14 days, and a restore inside the window SHALL lose at most 5 minutes of committed changes.","rationale":"DEP-011, OPS-320 and D-522 state one window, one floor and one recovery point (D-6205).","evaluate":{"method":"budget"},"ref":"OPS-1213","area":"09-operations","section":"Data safety","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-3","boundaryDetail":"`tenant restore`","traces":["g-302","g-39","d-522","d-6205"],"milestone":12,"realisation":"operational"},
    {"id":"prv-1214","kind":"requirement","statement":"The deletion of a tenant SHALL be requested by an owner with a fresh authentication, SHALL notify every owner of the tenant when it is requested and when it is cancelled, SHALL be executed only after the grace period, and SHALL end in a certificate that names the key destruction, each backup image, each export, the retained source database of a move, each fork and the state held by the key service.","rationale":"A deletion is irreversible, so a stolen session cannot start it unseen, and the certificate shows nothing was left behind (PRV-354, D-6207).","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"PRV-1214","area":"09-privacy","section":"Data subject rights","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-3","boundaryDetail":"`DELETE /tenants/{id}`","traces":["g-22","g-350","d-705","d-6207"],"milestone":6,"realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"obs-1215","kind":"requirement","statement":"The retention of audit entries SHALL be at least one year for every tenant, and a tenant policy SHALL be refused when it sets a shorter period.","rationale":"A tenant under attack could otherwise shorten the audit log to hide the attack (D-6208).","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"OBS-1215","area":"06-agents","section":"Audit","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-12","boundaryDetail":"`audit retention`","traces":["g-30","d-539","d-6208"],"milestone":8,"realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"obs-1216","kind":"requirement","statement":"Expiry of audit entries SHALL record the sequence number and the hash of the newest entry it removes as a checkpoint, the audit log SHALL write the head of each tenant chain to the platform audit store every 15 minutes, and verification SHALL report a break for a chain that stops short of the anchored head or does not chain from its checkpoint.","rationale":"A removal at the end of the log leaves every remaining hash valid, so only a head kept outside the tenant database shows it (OBS-007, D-6208).","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"OBS-1216","area":"06-agents","section":"Audit","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-12","boundaryDetail":"`verify-audit-chain`","traces":["g-30","d-20","d-6208"],"milestone":8,"realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"obs-1217","kind":"requirement","statement":"Every security-relevant operation SHALL write an audit entry that names its actor, its target and its outcome, and every authorisation that is refused for such an operation SHALL write one as well. The security-relevant operations are the operations of D-6201, exports of tenant or subject data, erasure, restore, deletion, role, team and invitation changes, support-grant issue and withdrawal, changes of a plan, flag or quota, and the revocation of a session or grant.","rationale":"The audit log is the evidence of who did what, and an operation outside it leaves none (D-6208).","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"OBS-1217","area":"06-agents","section":"Audit","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-12","boundaryDetail":"`audit coverage`","traces":["g-30","g-165","d-6201","d-6208"],"milestone":8,"realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"obs-1218","kind":"requirement","statement":"Every act of a platform operator or service on the control plane, namely provisioning, suspension, resumption, move, platform setting write, platform flag or quota change, recording of a contract, diagnostic and opening of the operator console, SHALL write an entry to the platform audit store that names the operator or component, the tenant when there is one, the target and the outcome, and the entry SHALL be kept seven years.","rationale":"The platform answers for its own actions in a record that no tenant controls (D-707, D-6208).","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"OBS-1218","area":"06-agents","section":"Audit","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-12","boundaryDetail":"`platform audit store`","traces":["g-30","g-165","d-707","d-6208"],"milestone":8,"realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"tok-1219","kind":"requirement","statement":"A verifier SHALL check the signature, the expiry and the revocation notices of an access token and SHALL apply a notice of a revoked grant, a revoked session or a retired signing key within 5 seconds, and a verifier whose notice feed is older than 5 seconds SHALL introspect the token or refuse it and SHALL NOT accept it on signature and expiry alone.","rationale":"D-5, TOK-007 and local verification state one rule: short lifetimes bound exposure, and a notice feed makes revocation prompt (D-6209).","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"TOK-1219","area":"03-identity","section":"Verify and revoke","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-6","boundaryDetail":"`token verification`","traces":["g-28","g-10","d-5","d-6209"],"milestone":4,"realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"ten-1220","kind":"requirement","statement":"A tenant SHALL be in exactly one of six states recorded in the tenant directory: provisioning, active, suspended, moving, restoring and deleting. The permitted changes are provisioning to active; active to suspended, moving, restoring or deleting; suspended to active, restoring or deleting; moving to active; and restoring to the state it left, so that a restore SHALL NOT lift a suspension. Moving is the read-only window of a move (MIG-568), not the copy before it. Deleting SHALL NOT change to any state, and a takedown of a moving or restoring tenant SHALL end that operation first (MIG-571).","rationale":"Every behaviour of a tenant is decided by one named state, so no request is judged by a guess. The states are those of D-6220.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"TEN-1220","area":"02-tenancy","section":"Life cycle","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-3","boundaryDetail":"`tenant state`","traces":["g-1","d-6220"],"milestone":2,"inSection":"sec-tenancy-4","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"ten-1221","kind":"requirement","statement":"A gateway SHALL serve published content of a tenant only in the states active and moving, and in the state suspended with a commercial reason (payment-overdue, trial-ended or owner-request). In provisioning, restoring and deleting, and in suspended with a takedown reason (abuse, legal-order or security-incident), it SHALL answer every request for a host of the tenant with a fixed platform notice that holds no content of the tenant and is held by no cache for more than 60 seconds.","rationale":"A takedown that leaves the site up is not a takedown (THR-262). A commercial suspension keeps the public site readable.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"TEN-1221","area":"02-tenancy","section":"Life cycle","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-3","boundaryDetail":"`published content`","traces":["g-1","d-6220"],"milestone":2,"inSection":"sec-tenancy-4","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"ten-1222","kind":"requirement","statement":"A tenant SHALL accept a state-changing request only in the state active. In every other state it SHALL refuse the request and change no data of the tenant, no queue and no counter, except the owner operations that TEN-1225 keeps.","rationale":"A write accepted by a tenant that the platform has stopped is a write the platform cannot answer for.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"TEN-1222","area":"02-tenancy","section":"Life cycle","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-3","boundaryDetail":"`state-changing request`","traces":["g-1","d-6220"],"milestone":2,"inSection":"sec-tenancy-4","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"ten-1223","kind":"requirement","statement":"Jobs, workflow steps, outbox publication, outbound webhooks, mail of the tenant and agent runs SHALL start only in the state active. When a tenant leaves active, nothing new SHALL start, a run in flight SHALL be stopped within 60 seconds, and queued work SHALL be kept and not run until the tenant is active again. Under a takedown reason, queued webhooks and mail SHALL be discarded and SHALL NOT be sent after a release. Mail that the platform itself sends to the owners about the state of the tenant SHALL be exempt.","rationale":"A suspension that leaves automation, mail and outbound calls running does not stop an abusive tenant.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"TEN-1223","area":"02-tenancy","section":"Life cycle","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-3","boundaryDetail":"`background work`","traces":["g-1","d-6220"],"milestone":2,"inSection":"sec-tenancy-4","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"ten-1224","kind":"requirement","statement":"In the state suspended with a commercial reason, a session of a principal of the tenant SHALL be honoured for reads and for the owner operations of TEN-1225. With a takedown reason, only a session of an owner that has passed a step-up SHALL be honoured, and only for those owner operations; every other session SHALL be refused and kept, except under security-incident, where every session and token of the tenant SHALL be revoked when the suspension is recorded. In provisioning, restoring and deleting no session SHALL be honoured. Moving SHALL honour sessions for reads.","rationale":"A suspended tenant that still honours every session is only partly suspended, and a compromised tenant must not keep its sessions.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"TEN-1224","area":"02-tenancy","section":"Life cycle","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-3","boundaryDetail":"`session`","traces":["g-1","d-6220"],"milestone":2,"inSection":"sec-tenancy-4","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"ten-1225","kind":"requirement","statement":"In every state except provisioning, restoring and deleting, an owner SHALL keep the right to request the deletion of the tenant and to cancel a request, and, unless the reason is legal-order or security-incident, to export the tenant. A suspension SHALL NOT shorten or end the grace period of a requested deletion. The platform SHALL tell every owner the state and the reason class when it changes, except where a legal order forbids it and the audit entry records that.","rationale":"A tenant that is stopped for non-payment still belongs to its owner, and the owner can leave with the data. An export under a legal order or an incident would hand the data to the party under suspicion.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"TEN-1225","area":"02-tenancy","section":"Life cycle","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-3","boundaryDetail":"`owner operation`","traces":["g-1","d-6220"],"milestone":2,"inSection":"sec-tenancy-4","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"thr-1226","kind":"requirement","statement":"The platform SHALL take a tenant down only through the operator contract take-down-tenant (CT-565), which needs the capability takedown-issue held by the role platform-operator. The operation SHALL set the state suspended with a takedown reason, purge the edge copies of every host of the tenant (EDG-008), and write an audit entry with the operator, the reason, a reference to the order or ticket, and the time. Ending a takedown SHALL need release-takedown (CT-567) by an operator other than the one who issued it.","rationale":"Abuse is stopped by a named operation of one role, which another operator must confirm to reverse.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"THR-1226","area":"09-threat","section":"Abuse and takedown","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-10","boundaryDetail":"`take-down-tenant`","traces":["g-262","d-6220"],"milestone":6,"inSection":"sec-threat-255","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"thr-1227","kind":"requirement","statement":"The platform SHALL take one host of a tenant down through the operator contract take-down-host (CT-566), which needs the capability takedown-issue. The domain binding SHALL be marked taken down, the edge copies stored under the host SHALL be purged (CT-104), every gateway SHALL answer that host with the fixed platform notice, certificate renewal for the host SHALL stop, and every other host and the state of the tenant SHALL stay as they were.","rationale":"A takedown of a domain (THR-262) must not stop the other sites of a tenant that did nothing wrong.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"THR-1227","area":"09-threat","section":"Abuse and takedown","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-10","boundaryDetail":"`take-down-host`","traces":["g-262","d-6220"],"milestone":6,"inSection":"sec-threat-255","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"arc-1228","kind":"requirement","statement":"After a suspension with a takedown reason, a takedown of a host, or a deletion is recorded in the directory, no gateway SHALL serve published content of that tenant or host later than 60 seconds after the record when it can reach the control plane, and none SHALL serve it later than 15 minutes after it last reached the control plane when it cannot (ARC-500). The control plane SHALL push the change to every gateway and SHALL repeat it until each acknowledges. A takedown requested while the control plane cannot record it SHALL be refused with unavailable and change nothing.","rationale":"The 15-minute copy of D-528 is a limit for losing the control plane, not a delay allowed to a takedown.","evaluate":{"method":"budget"},"ref":"ARC-1228","area":"09-architecture","section":"Control plane and wake index","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-3","boundaryDetail":"`takedown bound`","traces":["g-101","g-262","d-528","d-6221"],"milestone":2,"inSection":"sec-arch-2","realisation":"operational"},
    {"id":"arc-1229","kind":"requirement","statement":"A gateway SHALL hold a directory entry whose state is not active, and a host binding marked taken down, for at most 60 seconds before it asks the control plane again. While the control plane cannot be reached it SHALL keep treating such an entry as it was, SHALL NOT serve the tenant or host, and SHALL NOT let its age make it active.","rationale":"Resuming costs one refresh of 60 seconds, and an outage never turns a suspension into service.","evaluate":{"method":"budget"},"ref":"ARC-1229","area":"09-architecture","section":"Control plane and wake index","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-3","boundaryDetail":"`directory entry`","traces":["g-101","g-262","d-528","d-6221"],"milestone":2,"inSection":"sec-arch-2","realisation":"operational"},
    {"id":"ten-1230","kind":"requirement","statement":"Provisioning SHALL deliver the bootstrap credential of the first owner only to the mail address of that owner given when the tenant is provisioned, through the mail service. The credential SHALL NOT appear in an output, response, log or audit entry of provision-tenant, or be shown to the platform operator or to any other caller; the operator SHALL see only whether it was issued, accepted or has expired.","rationale":"The first owner holds the first credential alone, so no operator holds a standing way into the tenant (D-509, CT-033).","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"TEN-1230","area":"02-tenancy","section":"Provisioning","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-3","boundaryDetail":"`bootstrap credential`","traces":["g-2","d-509","d-6222"],"milestone":2,"inSection":"sec-tenancy-2","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"ten-1231","kind":"requirement","statement":"A tenant SHALL be created, and its hosts routed, in a running platform without a restart of any component. A component that resolves a tenant by host name SHALL read the tenant directory and SHALL NOT take its map of hosts to tenants from configuration read at start. A host that a gateway does not hold SHALL be resolved from the directory at once, and a tenant SHALL serve its first request within 60 seconds of becoming active.","rationale":"A platform that needs a restart to add a tenant cannot run thousands of them.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"TEN-1231","area":"02-tenancy","section":"Provisioning","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-3","boundaryDetail":"`tenant directory`","traces":["g-2"],"milestone":2,"inSection":"sec-tenancy-2","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"ten-1232","kind":"requirement","statement":"The directory SHALL record a tenant as provisioning from the first commit of the run that creates any part of it (directory row, database, key or stored files), and SHALL change it to active in the last commit only, after the layout, the template and the first owner credential are in place. On start, and at every sweep, a tenant found provisioning SHALL be resumed from its last completed step, each step being safe to repeat, or, after 3 failed attempts, rolled back by removing its database, files, key and directory entry and recording the rollback. A tenant in provisioning SHALL NOT be served or offered to anyone.","rationale":"A tenant half built by a crash must be repaired or removed, not left as an active tenant that is missing its layout (TEN-002, TEN-003).","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"TEN-1232","area":"02-tenancy","section":"Provisioning","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-3","boundaryDetail":"`tenant state`","traces":["g-2"],"milestone":2,"inSection":"sec-tenancy-2","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"ten-1233","kind":"requirement","statement":"A failure of one tenant to start, to resume provisioning, to install a bundle or to migrate its layout SHALL be recorded against that tenant, which SHALL stay unavailable and report the cause, and SHALL NOT stop the start of the platform or of any other tenant. Readiness SHALL report the number of tenants that failed.","rationale":"One bad tenant must not take every other tenant down.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"TEN-1233","area":"02-tenancy","section":"Provisioning","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-3","boundaryDetail":"`tenant start`","traces":["g-2"],"milestone":2,"inSection":"sec-tenancy-2","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"ten-1234","kind":"requirement","statement":"A fork made by fork-tenant (CT-166) SHALL be a tenant of kind fork with its own identifier, its own database and its own encryption key, stored with its logs and mail in the region of the primary placement of its source (TEN-005, PRV-371). It SHALL have no credential for or route to the source database, SHALL NOT receive sessions, tokens, credentials, signing keys, webhook secrets, queued jobs or outbox entries of the source, and SHALL start with jobs, mail, webhooks and agents off, so that it sends nothing outside the platform.","rationale":"A copy for a preview that shares a key, a region or a live effect with its source is a second production tenant nobody watches.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"TEN-1234","area":"02-tenancy","section":"Life cycle","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-3","boundaryDetail":"`fork`","traces":["g-1","d-6223"],"milestone":2,"inSection":"sec-tenancy-4","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"ten-1235","kind":"requirement","statement":"A fork SHALL be deleted with its database, files and key when 7 days have passed, when the projection it serves is applied or discarded, or when its source is deleted, whichever comes first, and SHALL NOT be backed up. A tenant SHALL have at most 2 forks made in any 7 days, and the storage of a fork SHALL count against the plan quota of its source. Only an owner of the source, after a step-up, SHALL read a fork, each read SHALL be audited in the source tenant, and a platform operator SHALL read it only under a support grant (G-165).","rationale":"A fork holds the personal data of its source, so its life, size and readers are bounded.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"TEN-1235","area":"02-tenancy","section":"Life cycle","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-3","boundaryDetail":"`fork lifetime`","traces":["g-1","d-6223"],"milestone":2,"inSection":"sec-tenancy-4","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"ten-1236","kind":"requirement","statement":"A subject erasure in the source tenant SHALL be applied to every live fork of it before the erasure is reported complete, and a fork that cannot be reached SHALL be deleted instead. A fork made at a revision earlier than an erasure SHALL have that erasure applied before its first read. The receipt of the erasure (PRV-353) SHALL list each fork reached or deleted.","rationale":"An erased person must not survive in a preview copy.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"TEN-1236","area":"02-tenancy","section":"Life cycle","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-3","boundaryDetail":"`fork erasure`","traces":["g-1","g-350","d-6223"],"milestone":2,"inSection":"sec-tenancy-4","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"ten-1237","kind":"requirement","statement":"The starter of a sandbox SHALL be a visitor who proves control of a mail address with a single-use code sent to it, and SHALL NOT need a principal, since a principal belongs to one tenant (D-500). That visitor SHALL become the first owner of the new tenant of kind sandbox, and the control database SHALL hold the address only as a keyed hash, deleted with the sandbox.","rationale":"A sandbox is started with no operator step (ADM-154), and the control database must hold no personal data (D-500).","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"TEN-1237","area":"09-administration","section":"Invitations and onboarding","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-3","boundaryDetail":"`POST /sandboxes`","traces":["g-154","d-500","d-6224"],"milestone":3,"inSection":"sec-administration-3","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"ten-1238","kind":"requirement","statement":"At most one live sandbox SHALL exist for one verified mail address, and one source address SHALL start at most 3 sandboxes in 24 hours. A start beyond either limit SHALL be refused and SHALL create nothing.","rationale":"Without a per-person cap, one person fills the platform with free tenants.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"TEN-1238","area":"09-administration","section":"Invitations and onboarding","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-3","boundaryDetail":"`sandbox limit`","traces":["g-154","d-6224"],"milestone":3,"inSection":"sec-administration-3","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"ten-1239","kind":"requirement","statement":"move-tenant SHALL refuse a target placement in a region other than the primary region of the tenant (D-23, TEN-005, PRV-371), and SHALL refuse a tenant that is not in the state active. The refusal SHALL change nothing, and a change of region SHALL NOT be done by a move.","rationale":"A move that crosses a region breaks residency without the owner having agreed to it.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"TEN-1239","area":"02-tenancy","section":"Moving a tenant","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-553","boundaryDetail":"`move-tenant`","traces":["g-558","d-23","d-6224"],"milestone":2,"inSection":"sec-migration-7","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"eml-1560","kind":"requirement","statement":"A send that a product requests SHALL create its message jobs and inbox notices in the transaction that commits the change it belongs to, SHALL name a message category and an allowance class, and SHALL take effect once for each idempotency key of the tenant within seven days of the first use of that key, and a repeat of a key with other inputs SHALL be refused with the error conflict.","rationale":"The product needs the same promise the platform gives its own mail (EML-005, EML-006): no message for a change that did not happen, and no second message for a retried step.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"EML-1560","area":"04-automation","section":"Product sends, categories and measurement","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-451","boundaryDetail":"`send-message`","traces":["g-453","g-155","d-451","d-6560"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-email-1560","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"eml-1561","kind":"requirement","statement":"A send to a segment SHALL resolve its recipients in batches of at most one hundred persons in ascending order of principal identifier, each batch in its own transaction, SHALL give no person more than one message for the send, and SHALL tell the sender only the numbers of recipients sent, held, suppressed and failed, and no recipient.","rationale":"A campaign to a large segment must not hold the tenant database in one transaction (SEG-028), and the sender learns no more about membership than the policies of the sender allow (D-5020, SEG-033).","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"EML-1561","area":"04-automation","section":"Product sends, categories and measurement","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-451","boundaryDetail":"`send-message`","traces":["g-453","g-608","d-5020","d-5080","d-6561"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-email-1560","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"eml-1562","kind":"requirement","statement":"Suppression and preference SHALL be recorded for each message category: an unsubscribe from one promotional category, or from all promotional categories, SHALL NOT suppress mail of a required or transactional category or sign-in mail; only a permanent bounce SHALL suppress every category; and a recipient SHALL be able to resubscribe through a link that works without a sign-in and that removes an unsubscribe suppression only.","rationale":"A marketing unsubscribe that also stopped a receipt or a password link would be a defect that the recipient cannot repair, and a recipient who unsubscribed by mistake is owed a way back (EML-020).","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"EML-1562","area":"04-automation","section":"Product sends, categories and measurement","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-451","boundaryDetail":"`suppression list`","traces":["g-453","d-6562","d-5080"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-email-1560","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"eml-1563","kind":"requirement","statement":"The mail allowance of a tenant SHALL be counted in three classes, sign-in, transactional and bulk: sign-in mail SHALL NOT count against the allowance, bulk mail SHALL be held once it has used eighty percent of the monthly allowance, transactional mail SHALL be held only when the whole allowance is used, and the dispatcher SHALL release sign-in mail before transactional mail and transactional mail before bulk mail, across tenants.","rationale":"One tenant's campaign must not hold the product mail of the same tenant behind it, nor delay the sign-in or transactional mail of another tenant (EML-021).","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"EML-1563","area":"04-automation","section":"Product sends, categories and measurement","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-451","boundaryDetail":"`mail quota`","traces":["g-453","g-4","d-6563","d-508"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-email-1560","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"eml-1564","kind":"requirement","statement":"The dispatcher SHALL hold the bulk mail of a tenant whose complaint rate over the last seven days is at least 0.5 percent, or whose permanent bounce rate over the same days is at least 10 percent, each measured over at least 1000 messages the provider accepted, SHALL hold the transactional mail of a tenant whose complaint rate is at least 1 percent, SHALL leave sign-in mail and the mail of other tenants unaffected, and SHALL end the hold when both rates are below their warning levels of 0.1 percent and 5 percent.","rationale":"One provider account serves every tenant (D-523), so the complaints of one tenant must not cost the delivery of the others.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"EML-1564","area":"04-automation","section":"Product sends, categories and measurement","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-451","boundaryDetail":"`delivery report`","traces":["g-453","g-4","d-523","d-6564"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-email-1560","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"eml-1565","kind":"requirement","statement":"Each message SHALL carry the category, the template, the send and the optional reference of the request that made it; the mail log SHALL keep them with the state; list-mail-messages SHALL filter by state, category, template, reference and period; and count-mail-messages SHALL return the number of messages in each state grouped by reference, category or template and SHALL offer no count of opens or clicks.","rationale":"A campaign is measured by what was sent, held, suppressed, bounced and complained about, with no tracking of readers (NG-8, D-5080).","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"EML-1565","area":"04-automation","section":"Product sends, categories and measurement","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-451","boundaryDetail":"`mail log`","traces":["g-453","ng-8","d-5080","d-6571"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-email-1560","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"eml-1566","kind":"requirement","statement":"A subject, a recipient address, a sender name and a reply-to address of a message SHALL be refused with the error invalid, before any job is created, when any of them contains a carriage return, a line feed or a NUL byte, a rendered subject included, and an address field SHALL hold one address only.","rationale":"A line break in a header begins a new header, which lets tenant content add recipients or content to a message (EDG-255 is the same rule for HTTP).","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"EML-1566","area":"04-automation","section":"Product sends, categories and measurement","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-18","boundaryDetail":"`submit-message`","traces":["g-453","g-46","d-6572"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-email-1560","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"eml-1567","kind":"requirement","statement":"A delivery report SHALL be accepted only when it carries the signature of the configured provider and a timestamp that differs from the receipt time by at most five minutes; SHALL be mapped to its tenant and message by the provider reference recorded when the message was submitted; SHALL leave a report with an unknown reference recorded as unmatched and change nothing else; and SHALL change nothing when the provider event identifier was seen within the last seven days.","rationale":"A captured report replayed later would silence a real address (EML-019), and a report must reach the one tenant whose message it concerns.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"EML-1567","area":"04-automation","section":"Product sends, categories and measurement","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-18","boundaryDetail":"`delivery report`","traces":["g-453","g-46","d-6569"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-email-1560","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"ntf-1568","kind":"requirement","statement":"A notice topic SHALL be one to four labels of lower case letters, digits and hyphens joined by dots, each label beginning with a letter, at most 96 bytes; the platform SHALL produce only the topics approval.requested, approval.decided, form.submitted, file.scan-finished, mail.sending-warning and mail.sending-held, and a tenant SHALL produce only topics that begin with app.; and a subscription SHALL name one topic or a prefix that ends in .*.","rationale":"A topic with a grammar can be filtered, subscribed to and checked, and a product cannot collide with a platform topic.","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"NTF-1568","area":"04-automation","section":"Product notices, preferences and digests","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-154","boundaryDetail":"`topic`","traces":["g-155","d-6566"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-notifications-1560","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"ntf-1569","kind":"requirement","statement":"An inbox SHALL let its recipient, and no other principal, mark a notice read, mark it unread and remove it; a call on the notice of another recipient SHALL answer not-found; the unread count SHALL equal the number of unread notices that a list without a state filter returns; a list SHALL filter by state and by topic; and a removal SHALL end the inbox item and publish its end.","rationale":"The inbox is the person's own and a badge count must agree with the list (NTF-151, NTF-152).","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"NTF-1569","area":"04-automation","section":"Product notices, preferences and digests","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-154","boundaryDetail":"`inbox`","traces":["g-155","g-151"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-notifications-1560","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"ntf-1570","kind":"requirement","statement":"A notice template SHALL be stored as tenant metadata holding a title, structured blocks and content tokens, SHALL be rendered once for each recipient with that recipient as the reader into text only, and a notice made from it SHALL omit the values of each record that its recipient has no right to read.","rationale":"Notices are templated like mail so a product writes its wording once as data (EML-012, EML-016, CTK-019, NTF-150).","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"NTF-1570","area":"04-automation","section":"Product notices, preferences and digests","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-154","boundaryDetail":"`notice template`","traces":["g-155","g-20","k-450"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-notifications-1560","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"ntf-1571","kind":"requirement","statement":"A person SHALL be able to set, for each message category and each channel, one of on, off and digest; a message of a category that the person set to off for a channel SHALL NOT be delivered on that channel unless its category is required; a person SHALL be able to set quiet hours and a mute time, with quiet hours deferring and a mute dropping the mail and live push of every category that is not required while the inbox still stores the notice; and sign-in mail SHALL ignore all of these.","rationale":"People decide what reaches them, and the platform keeps what it owes them (WG-5004).","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"NTF-1571","area":"04-automation","section":"Product notices, preferences and digests","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-154","boundaryDetail":"`notification preference`","traces":["g-155","d-6565"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-notifications-1560","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"ntf-1572","kind":"requirement","statement":"A person whose mode for a category and channel is digest SHALL receive the notices of that category created in each period as one message that lists them, once for each period, with no message for an empty period and no second message for a notice in the digest; and the step send-digest SHALL do the same for a window that a workflow names.","rationale":"Many small events become one message, and a retried run sends it once.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"NTF-1572","area":"04-automation","section":"Product notices, preferences and digests","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-154","boundaryDetail":"`digest`","traces":["g-155","d-6573"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-notifications-1560","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"sch-1573","kind":"requirement","statement":"Each tenant SHALL have a time zone and each person MAY have one, each a name of the IANA time zone database, held as the platform setting time-zone at the tenant level and at the person level with the default UTC; a local time of a person SHALL be read in the zone of the person, then the zone of the tenant, then UTC; and a wall-clock time SHALL mean that time in that zone, where a time that does not exist because clocks go forward is read at the offset that held before the change and a time that occurs twice is the first of the two.","rationale":"Send at 09:00 local, quiet hours and digests need a zone, and the daylight saving rule decides whether they fire once or twice or never (RFC 5545 section 3.3.5).","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"SCH-1573","area":"04-automation","section":"Time and domain events","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-7","boundaryDetail":"`time-zone`","traces":["g-453","d-6567","d-5005"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-scheduling-1560","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"sch-1574","kind":"requirement","statement":"A recurrence SHALL be the RRULE value of RFC 5545 section 3.3.10 limited to FREQ of HOURLY, DAILY, WEEKLY or MONTHLY, INTERVAL, BYDAY without an ordinal, BYMONTHDAY, one BYHOUR, one BYMINUTE, COUNT and UNTIL, with the added part TZID naming the zone in which the BY parts are read, the tenant zone when it is absent; HOURLY SHALL step by elapsed hours and the other frequencies by wall-clock days, a month without the named day being skipped; and a rule outside this subset SHALL be refused with the error invalid.","rationale":"One named standard with a stated subset can be checked, and daylight saving changes cannot make a daily rule fire twice (WFL-011, SCH-003).","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"SCH-1574","area":"04-automation","section":"Time and domain events","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-7","boundaryDetail":"`define-schedule`","traces":["g-13","d-6567"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-scheduling-1560","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"sch-1575","kind":"requirement","statement":"A mail outcome of delivered, bounced, complained or unsubscribed, the reading of an inbox notice, the submission of a form and the end of the scan of a file SHALL each produce a domain event in the transaction that records it; and a selector SHALL be able to name event kinds, segments, ledger units and record transitions as well as object types, an absent member matching everything, members combining as AND and the values of one member as OR.","rationale":"A product reacts to what happened, not only to record changes (SCH-004, D-5023).","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"SCH-1575","area":"04-automation","section":"Time and domain events","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-7","boundaryDetail":"`selector`","traces":["g-13","g-155","d-6568"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-scheduling-1560","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"sch-1576","kind":"requirement","statement":"A tenant SHALL be able to declare at most 32 event kinds, each named with the prefix app. and the grammar of an event kind, with at most 16 payload fields of the scalar types and a list of the roles that may read it; a product SHALL emit such an event only through emit-event in the transaction of its change; and an event of an undeclared kind, with a payload that does not match its declaration or of a platform kind SHALL be refused with the error invalid.","rationale":"A product names its own facts without a change to the kernel (D-103) and without a way to forge a platform event.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"SCH-1576","area":"04-automation","section":"Time and domain events","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-7","boundaryDetail":"`emit-event`","traces":["g-13","d-103","d-6568"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-scheduling-1560","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"int-1577","kind":"requirement","statement":"A delivery to an inbound webhook endpoint SHALL carry a timestamp that the signature covers, SHALL be refused with the error unauthenticated, in one answer for an unknown endpoint and for a wrong signature, SHALL be refused with the error stale-delivery when its timestamp differs from the receipt time by more than five minutes, SHALL be refused with the error too-large when its body exceeds one mebibyte, SHALL run once for each event identifier within seven days, and SHALL be limited to 600 deliveries a minute for each endpoint.","rationale":"A captured delivery replayed later must not start a run (WFL-255), and an attacker learns nothing about which endpoints exist.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"INT-1577","area":"04-automation","section":"Inbound webhook endpoints","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-150","boundaryDetail":"`receive-inbound-webhook`","traces":["g-156","g-46","d-6569"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-integrations-1560","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"int-1578","kind":"requirement","statement":"An owner SHALL be able to create an inbound webhook endpoint and to rotate its secret; the secret SHALL be shown once at creation or rotation, be sealed under the key of the tenant and be written to no log; and after a rotation both the new and the previous secret SHALL verify for twenty-four hours and then only the new one.","rationale":"A secret that cannot be replaced is a secret that leaks for good, and a sender needs time to switch (WFL-254, EML-004).","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"INT-1578","area":"04-automation","section":"Inbound webhook endpoints","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-150","boundaryDetail":"`webhook endpoint`","traces":["g-156","g-46","d-6569"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-integrations-1560","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"wfl-1579","kind":"requirement","statement":"The outbound rule SHALL allow an outbound call only over HTTPS on port 443 to an address that the outbound gate resolved and judged, and SHALL refuse any other scheme, any other port, an address that carries a user name or a password, and a redirect to any of these.","rationale":"Tenant automation reaches the public internet by one protocol on one port, so plain text, internal services on odd ports and credentials in addresses are not available to it (WFL-008, WFL-250, WFL-251, WFL-252).","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"WFL-1579","area":"04-automation","section":"The outbound rule","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-7","boundaryDetail":"`outbound gate`","traces":["g-156","g-46","d-6570"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-workflows-1560","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"int-1580","kind":"requirement","statement":"A tenant bundle SHALL carry one section for each kind of entity a tenant declares: record types, roles, capabilities, policies, queries, views, workflows, segments, setting definitions, ledger units, pools and limits, mail templates, notice templates and tokens, with named places for triggers, automations and composite operations.","rationale":"A product whose parts fit in no section would need a separate call for each of them, and what it installs could not be reviewed as one change.","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"INT-1580","area":"04-automation","section":"Product bundles: install, upgrade and remove","lifecycle":"active","realisation":"checked","boundary":"b-21","boundaryDetail":"`tenant bundle`","traces":["g-167","g-103","g-31"],"milestone":7,"inSection":"sec-product-bundles"},
    {"id":"int-1581","kind":"requirement","statement":"Installing, upgrading and removing a product SHALL each be one product change whose projection is shown before it applies, applied with all of its edits or none, and a removal SHALL refuse a record type that still has records unless the removal states that the records are deleted.","rationale":"A product that half-installs leaves a tenant in a state no bundle describes, and removal that silently deletes records destroys data.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"INT-1581","area":"04-automation","section":"Product bundles: install, upgrade and remove","lifecycle":"active","realisation":"checked","boundary":"b-product-lifecycle","boundaryDetail":"`product change`","traces":["g-167","g-103"],"milestone":7,"inSection":"sec-product-bundles"},
    {"id":"int-1582","kind":"requirement","statement":"Each entity a product installs SHALL have an id that begins with the namespace of its product and SHALL be recorded in the tenant catalogue as owned by that product, and an install SHALL be refused when an entity with one of its ids exists and is not owned by that product, and a schema change from outside the product SHALL be refused when it changes an entity that a product owns.","rationale":"A removal can find a product's parts only if every part names its owner, and two products must not take the same name.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"INT-1582","area":"04-automation","section":"Product bundles: install, upgrade and remove","lifecycle":"active","realisation":"checked","boundary":"b-product-lifecycle","boundaryDetail":"`product change`","traces":["g-167","g-103"],"milestone":7,"inSection":"sec-product-bundles"},
    {"id":"int-1583","kind":"requirement","statement":"A bundle SHALL declare the platform releases it supports, and an install or upgrade on a release outside them SHALL be refused; installing a bundle of the same product and version again SHALL change nothing, and an upgrade to a version that is not greater SHALL be refused.","rationale":"A bundle written for one platform release must not land on another, and a retry of an install must not duplicate or fail.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"INT-1583","area":"04-automation","section":"Product bundles: install, upgrade and remove","lifecycle":"active","realisation":"checked","boundary":"b-21","boundaryDetail":"`tenant bundle`","traces":["g-167","g-103","g-31"],"milestone":7,"inSection":"sec-product-bundles"},
    {"id":"prv-1584","kind":"requirement","statement":"A field of a tenant record type that holds personal data SHALL declare the kind of personal data and whose data it is, a schema change that declares one without the other SHALL be refused, and the field SHALL be stored sealed under the key of its data subject.","rationale":"Export, rectification, restriction and erasure can reach only the fields that name their subject.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"PRV-1584","area":"09-privacy","section":"Personal data of tenant record types","lifecycle":"active","realisation":"checked","boundary":"b-2","boundaryDetail":"`record declaration`","traces":["g-351","k-350"],"milestone":2,"inSection":"sec-tenant-personal-data"},
    {"id":"prv-1585","kind":"requirement","statement":"A tenant record type that has a field with a personal declaration SHALL declare a retention rule, and a schema change that leaves such a type without one SHALL be refused.","rationale":"PRV-356 gives each record type a retention rule; for a type with personal data the rule cannot be left to a default that no one chose.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"PRV-1585","area":"09-privacy","section":"Personal data of tenant record types","lifecycle":"active","realisation":"checked","boundary":"b-2","boundaryDetail":"`record declaration`","traces":["g-351","k-350"],"milestone":2,"inSection":"sec-tenant-personal-data"},
    {"id":"prv-1586","kind":"requirement","statement":"Subject export, rectification, restriction and erasure SHALL reach every field of every tenant record type that declares the principal as its data subject, the search entries and shared copies that hold such a field, and the file content that such a field refers to, and the erasure receipt SHALL name each record, search entry and file reached.","rationale":"A product's profile, messages and awards are personal data the platform holds on the tenant's behalf.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"PRV-1586","area":"09-privacy","section":"Personal data of tenant record types","lifecycle":"active","realisation":"checked","boundary":"b-2","boundaryDetail":"`record declaration`","traces":["g-351","k-350"],"milestone":2,"inSection":"sec-tenant-personal-data"},
    {"id":"prv-1587","kind":"requirement","statement":"A field of kind free-text or file SHALL be sealed as a whole under the key of its subject, a file referred to only by such fields SHALL be stored and rendered sealed under that key, and the platform SHALL make no attempt to find personal data in a field that does not declare it.","rationale":"Prose and file bytes cannot be searched for personal data reliably; declaring the field is what makes erasure certain.","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"PRV-1587","area":"09-privacy","section":"Personal data of tenant record types","lifecycle":"active","realisation":"checked","boundary":"b-2","boundaryDetail":"`record declaration`","traces":["g-351","k-350"],"milestone":2,"inSection":"sec-tenant-personal-data"},
    {"id":"prv-1588","kind":"requirement","statement":"An erasure of a principal SHALL delete the search entries that hold a field of that principal in the same commit as the key destruction, SHALL refuse a principal that does not exist for the tenant with not-found, and a search entry SHALL hold a personal field only when its declaration states that the field is searchable.","rationale":"The key destruction makes the stored field unreadable, but an index entry made from the plain value would still answer a search.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"PRV-1588","area":"09-privacy","section":"Personal data of tenant record types","lifecycle":"active","realisation":"checked","boundary":"b-2","boundaryDetail":"`record declaration`","traces":["g-351","k-350"],"milestone":2,"inSection":"sec-tenant-personal-data"},
    {"id":"krn-1589","kind":"requirement","statement":"The kernel SHALL evaluate the read expression of a field for the reading principal and the record on every read path, and a field that the principal may not read SHALL be absent from the answer of a record read, a query, a view, a delivery list, an event, an export and a search result, as if the field did not exist.","rationale":"A field-level rule that only some paths evaluate is a rule a reader can step around.","evaluate":{"method":"property"},"ref":"KRN-1589","area":"01-core","section":"Field-level read","lifecycle":"active","realisation":"checked","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`strata_kernel::read`","traces":["g-20"],"milestone":1,"inSection":"sec-field-read"},
    {"id":"srh-1590","kind":"requirement","statement":"A search SHALL match only the fields that the reader may read, a query or a segment that names a field the reader may not read SHALL be refused with field-forbidden, and a record SHALL be left out of an aggregate as AGG-017 states.","rationale":"Matching a hidden field lets a reader confirm its content by trying words.","evaluate":{"method":"property"},"ref":"SRH-1590","area":"07-content","section":"Field-level read","lifecycle":"active","realisation":"checked","boundary":"b-151","boundaryDetail":"`search query`","traces":["g-161","g-20"],"milestone":11,"inSection":"sec-field-read"},
    {"id":"cms-1591","kind":"requirement","statement":"A field of the file type SHALL hold the hash of a stored file, a principal SHALL read a file only when the principal may read a record that refers to it through a field that the principal may read, and a file that no record refers to SHALL be readable only by the principal that uploaded it until it is attached or removed after 24 hours.","rationale":"File privacy follows the record that shows the file, so one rule decides both.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"CMS-1591","area":"07-content","section":"File fields and uploads","lifecycle":"active","realisation":"checked","boundary":"b-9","boundaryDetail":"`file reference field`","traces":["g-33","g-20"],"milestone":7,"inSection":"sec-file-fields"},
    {"id":"edg-1592","kind":"requirement","statement":"Signing an address for a private file SHALL be refused unless the caller and the principal named both may read the file, the expiry SHALL be at most 3600 seconds after the signing, delivery SHALL be refused unless the session of the request is that of the principal named and that principal may still read the file, and a shared cache SHALL hold no private file.","rationale":"A signed address is a credential: it must say who may use it, for how long, and stop working when the right to read does.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"EDG-1592","area":"05-delivery","section":"Signed media addresses","lifecycle":"active","realisation":"checked","boundary":"b-10","boundaryDetail":"`signed address`","traces":["g-33","g-20"],"milestone":11,"inSection":"sec-signed-addresses"},
    {"id":"cms-1593","kind":"requirement","statement":"An upload SHALL be refused before any byte is stored when its size exceeds the smallest of the platform maximum of 104857600 bytes, the file limit of the tenant and the cap of the field, a file larger than 1048576 bytes SHALL be sent in chunks of at most 8388608 bytes, and the completion of the scan and of each declared rendition SHALL each produce a domain event.","rationale":"A single call with the whole content has no bound, and a product cannot react to a file that is ready if nothing says so.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"CMS-1593","area":"07-content","section":"File fields and uploads","lifecycle":"active","realisation":"checked","boundary":"b-chunked-upload","boundaryDetail":"`chunked upload`","traces":["g-33"],"milestone":7,"inSection":"sec-file-fields"},
    {"id":"adm-1594","kind":"requirement","statement":"A capability that a product file declares SHALL have an id that begins with the namespace of its product, and a product capability SHALL be required only by the operations of that product and SHALL NOT be listed as a requirement of any platform operation.","rationale":"A product needs finer grants than the platform's, but one that could gate a platform operation would extend the platform.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"ADM-1594","area":"09-administration","section":"Product and member capabilities","lifecycle":"active","realisation":"checked","boundary":"b-21","boundaryDetail":"`module bundle`","traces":["g-103","g-153"],"milestone":7,"inSection":"sec-member-capabilities"},
    {"id":"adm-1595","kind":"requirement","statement":"A principal that holds self-record-write, self-file-upload and self-events-read and none of content-write, events-subscribe and media-sign SHALL be able to change only records it created or that name it as their data subject, upload only into a file field its policies let it write, and read only events about records it may read, and SHALL be refused every draft, article and publication operation.","rationale":"Self-service must not carry authoring with it.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"ADM-1595","area":"09-administration","section":"Product and member capabilities","lifecycle":"active","realisation":"checked","boundary":"b-4","boundaryDetail":"`role assignment`","traces":["g-153","k-13"],"milestone":3,"inSection":"sec-member-capabilities"},
    {"id":"cms-1596","kind":"requirement","statement":"A record type that declares a publication state SHALL have the contracts publish-content, withdraw-content, submit-for-review and schedule-publication, a type marked for review SHALL start a run of its review workflow on submission and SHALL accept publishing only after that run is approved, and a scheduled publication SHALL run as the principal that scheduled it, authorised again at the time.","rationale":"Publication belongs to any content type, and review is only a workflow step if the record and the run are linked.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"CMS-1596","area":"07-content","section":"Publication contracts and language","lifecycle":"active","realisation":"checked","boundary":"b-content-publication","boundaryDetail":"`publication contract`","traces":["g-151","g-17"],"milestone":6,"inSection":"sec-publication-language"},
    {"id":"cms-1597","kind":"requirement","statement":"A request SHALL carry the language of its reader in its context, a record type that declares a language field SHALL hold one language for each record, and a record requested in a language it lacks SHALL be answered in the first fallback language of the tenant that the record has, or the default language of the tenant.","rationale":"Localisation needs the language of the record, the language of the reader and the order of fallback to be data.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"CMS-1597","area":"07-content","section":"Publication contracts and language","lifecycle":"active","realisation":"checked","boundary":"b-9","boundaryDetail":"`delivery request`","traces":["g-31","g-161"],"milestone":6,"inSection":"sec-publication-language"},
    {"id":"idn-1598","kind":"requirement","statement":"The platform SHALL hold a settings schema for the lockout and throttle numbers, the session lifetimes, the allowed second factors, the password policy, whether registration is open, the audit retention, the outbound allow-list, the file limits and the webhook limits, each marked platform-fixed or tightenable, and a value on the looser side of its platform default, or outside the floor and ceiling the platform holds, SHALL be refused.","rationale":"The text lets a realm or a tenant tighten these values, so the values and the direction of tightening must be defined.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"IDN-1598","area":"03-identity","section":"Realm and tenant configuration","lifecycle":"active","realisation":"checked","boundary":"b-4","boundaryDetail":"`realm configuration`","traces":["g-9","k-16"],"milestone":3,"inSection":"sec-realm-tenant-settings"},
    {"id":"arc-1599","kind":"requirement","statement":"Every public contract SHALL name its optimistic-concurrency input expected-version, its pagination inputs cursor and limit with the output next and a largest limit of 100, its idempotency input idempotency-key, and its error kinds from the platform vocabulary, and a specification with a contract that breaks one of these SHALL be refused.","rationale":"One name for each convention lets a product author learn it once, and a rule keeps the next contract from drifting.","evaluate":{"method":"property"},"ref":"ARC-1599","area":"09-architecture","section":"Contract conventions","lifecycle":"active","realisation":"checked","boundary":"b-9","boundaryDetail":"`contract conventions`","traces":["g-103"],"milestone":2,"inSection":"sec-contract-conventions"},
    {"id":"ten-1140","kind":"requirement","statement":"An explicit tenant input of a public contract SHALL equal the tenant resolved from the host and the session of the request; the gateway SHALL refuse a request whose tenant input differs, record the refusal as an audit entry and raise an alert to the platform operators.","rationale":"The gateway takes the tenant from the host name alone (GWY-001), so a tenant named in a request body is a claim to be checked and never an instruction; an attempt to name another tenant is a boundary attempt (THR-259).","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"TEN-1140","area":"02-tenancy","section":"Tenant inputs of public contracts","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-9","boundaryDetail":"`tenant` input","traces":["g-20","k-6"],"milestone":2,"inSection":"sec-tenancy-1140","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"cms-1540","kind":"requirement","statement":"The tenant rule language SHALL evaluate a + b, a - b and a * b over two integers to their exact integer result, and SHALL fail the evaluation with the error integer-overflow when an operand or the result is outside -(2^53-1) to 2^53-1.","rationale":"A threshold that wraps or saturates is a wrong answer without a trace; the range is the one every evaluator holds exactly (D-5004).","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"CMS-1540","area":"07-content","section":"Arithmetic and time in rules","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`tenant rule language`","traces":["g-20","d-6540"],"milestone":2,"inSection":"sec-composition-2","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"cms-1541","kind":"requirement","statement":"For a timestamp t and an integer d, the tenant rule language SHALL evaluate t + d and t - d to the timestamp d milliseconds after and before t, and ms_between(a, b) to b minus a in milliseconds, failing with integer-overflow as CMS-1540 states.","rationale":"Expiry, windows and \"within a week\" are written as arithmetic on the time the decision is given.","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"CMS-1541","area":"07-content","section":"Arithmetic and time in rules","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`tenant rule language`","traces":["g-20","d-6541"],"milestone":2,"inSection":"sec-composition-2","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"cms-1542","kind":"requirement","statement":"days(n), hours(n) and minutes(n) SHALL evaluate to n times 86,400,000, 3,600,000 and 60,000, failing with integer-overflow as CMS-1540 states.","rationale":"A duration is an integer of milliseconds, written readably.","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"CMS-1542","area":"07-content","section":"Arithmetic and time in rules","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`tenant rule language`","traces":["g-20","d-6541"],"milestone":2,"inSection":"sec-composition-2","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"cms-1543","kind":"requirement","statement":"concat(a, b) SHALL evaluate to the string a followed by the string b and SHALL fail with string-too-long when the result is longer than 4,096 bytes of UTF-8; text(v) SHALL evaluate an integer, a timestamp or a record reference to its decimal digits, a boolean to true or false, and a string to itself.","rationale":"A key built from several values has one spelling and a bounded length.","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"CMS-1543","area":"07-content","section":"Arithmetic and time in rules","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`tenant rule language`","traces":["g-20","d-6542"],"milestone":2,"inSection":"sec-composition-2","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"cms-1544","kind":"requirement","statement":"Every arithmetic, time, concat and text operator SHALL evaluate to null when any of its operands is null.","rationale":"Null propagates as it does through comparison, so a missing field cannot pass for zero.","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"CMS-1544","area":"07-content","section":"Arithmetic and time in rules","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`tenant rule language`","traces":["g-20","d-6540","d-6541","d-6542"],"milestone":2,"inSection":"sec-composition-2","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"cms-1545","kind":"requirement","statement":"A rule SHALL be refused when it is defined if an operand of +, - or * has a shape other than int, except a timestamp as the left operand of + or -, or if text is applied to a list.","rationale":"A rule that cannot evaluate is refused before it runs, not at the first request.","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"CMS-1545","area":"07-content","section":"Arithmetic and time in rules","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`tenant rule language`","traces":["g-20","d-6541","d-6543"],"milestone":2,"inSection":"sec-composition-2","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"cms-1546","kind":"requirement","statement":"The Rust and the JavaScript evaluators of the tenant rule language SHALL give the same value or the same error text for every case of the shared case table, which SHALL include each new operator at both ends of the integer range and with null operands.","rationale":"The language is generated for both; one table pins both to one meaning.","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"CMS-1546","area":"07-content","section":"Arithmetic and time in rules","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`tenant rule language`","traces":["g-20","d-6543"],"milestone":2,"inSection":"sec-composition-2","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"cms-1547","kind":"requirement","statement":"balance(unit, scope) SHALL evaluate to the balance of the account of the acting principal for that unit and scope, to 0 when no such account exists, and to null for an anonymous or system principal.","rationale":"A rule reads a count the ledger keeps instead of a field nobody may maintain (D-6559).","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"CMS-1547","area":"07-content","section":"Reads in rules","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`tenant rule language`","traces":["g-600","d-6544"],"milestone":11,"inSection":"sec-composition-3","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"cms-1548","kind":"requirement","statement":"in_segment(name) SHALL evaluate to whether the acting principal holds a membership of the named segment in the snapshot of the decision, to false for an anonymous principal, and SHALL fail with unknown-segment when the tenant has no segment of that name.","rationale":"Eligibility checked at decision time uses the segment instead of a copy of its predicate.","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"CMS-1548","area":"07-content","section":"Reads in rules","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`tenant rule language`","traces":["g-605","d-6544"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-composition-3","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"cms-1549","kind":"requirement","statement":"setting(name) SHALL evaluate to the value of the setting resolved for the acting principal as SET-010 states, and a rule that names a setting not defined, or of type f64, SHALL be refused when it is defined.","rationale":"A rule reads a resolved preference the same way a page does; the rule language has no fractional shape.","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"CMS-1549","area":"07-content","section":"Reads in rules","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`tenant rule language`","traces":["g-610","d-6544"],"milestone":6,"inSection":"sec-composition-3","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"cms-1550","kind":"requirement","statement":"A rule SHALL be refused when it is defined if it uses balance, in_segment or setting in a constraint, in_segment in a segment predicate, or balance in a query filter or a field default.","rationale":"Each read appears only where its meaning and its cost are settled (D-6545).","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"CMS-1550","area":"07-content","section":"Reads in rules","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`tenant rule language`","traces":["g-20","d-6545"],"milestone":11,"inSection":"sec-composition-3","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"cms-1551","kind":"requirement","statement":"A decision that evaluates balance, in_segment or setting SHALL load the records they read only through needs of its plan, and two reads of one name within one decision SHALL give one value.","rationale":"The kernel loads only what its plan names, and one decision sees one snapshot (K-100).","evaluate":{"method":"property"},"ref":"CMS-1551","area":"07-content","section":"Reads in rules","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`plan needs`","traces":["k-100","d-6544"],"milestone":11,"inSection":"sec-composition-3","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"cms-1552","kind":"requirement","statement":"The commit of a decision that read a balance, a membership or a setting SHALL be refused by the revision guard when one of the records it read changed after its snapshot, and the decision SHALL be made again on the new state.","rationale":"A check of a balance followed by a posting is then safe under concurrent requests, as two postings already are (LDG-017).","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"CMS-1552","area":"07-content","section":"Reads in rules","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-2","boundaryDetail":"`commit`","traces":["g-602","d-6544","d-5009"],"milestone":11,"inSection":"sec-composition-3","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"cms-1553","kind":"requirement","statement":"A policy condition or query filter that reads balance SHALL give its read an audience class of the acting person alone, one that reads in_segment SHALL give its read the class of the members or of the non-members of that segment, and one that reads setting SHALL refine it as SET-053 states.","rationale":"A copy is shared only between readers who would be answered alike (K-7).","evaluate":{"method":"property"},"ref":"CMS-1553","area":"07-content","section":"Reads in rules","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`audience class`","traces":["d-15","d-6545"],"milestone":11,"inSection":"sec-composition-3","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"cms-1554","kind":"requirement","statement":"A create or update of a tenant record that would give two records of its object type equal values in every field of one composite unique constraint SHALL be refused, naming the constraint.","rationale":"A retried writer creates one award per person and badge.","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"CMS-1554","area":"07-content","section":"Composite unique constraints","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`strata_kernel::transition`","traces":["g-20","d-6558"],"milestone":11,"inSection":"sec-composition-8","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"cms-1555","kind":"requirement","statement":"A record with null in any field of a composite unique constraint SHALL NOT be refused by that constraint.","rationale":"Null is unknown, as in SQL, so two incomplete records do not collide.","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"CMS-1555","area":"07-content","section":"Composite unique constraints","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`strata_kernel::transition`","traces":["g-20","d-6558"],"milestone":11,"inSection":"sec-composition-8","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"cms-1556","kind":"requirement","statement":"A schema change that declares a composite unique constraint over fewer than two or more than four fields, or over records that already hold two with equal values in every field of it, SHALL be refused, naming one such pair.","rationale":"A constraint that existing data breaks is never in force.","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"CMS-1556","area":"07-content","section":"Composite unique constraints","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`change-schema`","traces":["g-20","d-6558"],"milestone":11,"inSection":"sec-composition-8","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"cms-1557","kind":"requirement","statement":"The check of a composite unique constraint SHALL load only the records of the object type that hold the written values in the fields of the constraint.","rationale":"A uniqueness check does not load every record of the type (K-100).","evaluate":{"method":"property"},"ref":"CMS-1557","area":"07-content","section":"Composite unique constraints","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`plan needs`","traces":["k-100","d-6558"],"milestone":11,"inSection":"sec-composition-8","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"opr-1540","kind":"requirement","statement":"A tenant operation SHALL be stored as tenant metadata under the schema version, holding a name, typed inputs, its invokers, an optional subject record, conditions in the tenant rule language and steps of the kinds create-record, update-record, delete-record and post-ledger.","rationale":"A compound feature is data the kernel interprets, not code (NG-3).","evaluate":{"method":"property"},"ref":"OPR-1540","area":"10-product","section":"Tenant operations","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`decide-tenant-operation`","traces":["g-600","d-6546"],"milestone":11,"inSection":"sec-composition-4","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"opr-1541","kind":"requirement","statement":"An accepted invocation of a tenant operation SHALL commit every record change and every posting of its steps, with their domain events, in one transaction, and a refused invocation SHALL commit none of them.","rationale":"A redemption and the points it spends are one fact (LDG-009).","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"OPR-1541","area":"10-product","section":"Tenant operations","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-2","boundaryDetail":"`commit`","traces":["g-600","k-9","d-6548","d-5006"],"milestone":11,"inSection":"sec-composition-4","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"opr-1542","kind":"requirement","statement":"An invocation whose condition evaluates to false or null, or one of whose steps is refused, SHALL be refused with the code of that condition or refusal and SHALL change nothing.","rationale":"A partial invocation is never visible.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"OPR-1542","area":"10-product","section":"Tenant operations","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`decide-tenant-operation`","traces":["g-600","d-6548"],"milestone":11,"inSection":"sec-composition-4","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"opr-1543","kind":"requirement","statement":"The conditions of a tenant operation SHALL be evaluated on the state before any of its steps, and each step SHALL be applied to the state that the steps before it leave.","rationale":"One order of evaluation gives one answer, and a step sees what earlier steps did.","evaluate":{"method":"property"},"ref":"OPR-1543","area":"10-product","section":"Tenant operations","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`decide-tenant-operation`","traces":["g-600","d-6548"],"milestone":11,"inSection":"sec-composition-4","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"opr-1544","kind":"requirement","statement":"An invocation that repeats the operation, invoker and idempotency key of an accepted invocation of the previous seven days SHALL answer with its recorded result and change nothing when its inputs are the same, and SHALL be refused with idempotency-mismatch when they differ.","rationale":"A double click or a retry redeems once.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"OPR-1544","area":"10-product","section":"Tenant operations","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`decide-tenant-operation`","traces":["g-603","d-6548"],"milestone":11,"inSection":"sec-composition-4","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"opr-1545","kind":"requirement","statement":"The idempotency key of each posting that a step of a tenant operation makes SHALL be op:<operation id>:<invoker>:<invocation key>:<step id>.","rationale":"The ledger applies a repeated posting once even after the run record is gone (LDG-006).","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"OPR-1545","area":"10-product","section":"Tenant operations","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`decide-tenant-operation`","traces":["g-603","d-6548"],"milestone":11,"inSection":"sec-composition-4","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"opr-1546","kind":"requirement","statement":"An invocation SHALL be refused unless the caller is signed in, holds tenant-operation-invoke and is named by the invokers of the operation, and no other capability, such as ledger-post or content-write, SHALL be required of the caller.","rationale":"A member may redeem without being able to post or write directly (composition finding F3).","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"OPR-1546","area":"10-product","section":"Tenant operations","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`decide-tenant-operation`","traces":["g-20","d-6547"],"milestone":11,"inSection":"sec-composition-4","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"opr-1547","kind":"requirement","statement":"A schema change that defines or changes a tenant operation SHALL be refused unless the principal making it holds every capability and object permission that the steps of the operation use.","rationale":"An operation grants no more than its author holds, as a role does (ADM-152).","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"OPR-1547","area":"10-product","section":"Tenant operations","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`change-schema`","traces":["g-20","d-6547"],"milestone":11,"inSection":"sec-composition-4","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"opr-1548","kind":"requirement","statement":"A record that a step of a tenant operation creates SHALL name the invoker as its creator, and an entry that a step posts SHALL name the invoker as caused-by.","rationale":"The journal says who acted, not which operation.","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"OPR-1548","area":"10-product","section":"Tenant operations","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`decide-tenant-operation`","traces":["g-604","d-6547"],"milestone":11,"inSection":"sec-composition-4","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"opr-1549","kind":"requirement","statement":"A tenant operation with more than sixteen steps, more than eight posting steps, a condition longer than two hundred nodes, a step id equal to an input name, or a name of an object type, field, unit, pool, segment or setting that the tenant does not have SHALL be refused when it is defined.","rationale":"The plan and cost of an invocation are known before the first one runs.","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"OPR-1549","area":"10-product","section":"Tenant operations","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`change-schema`","traces":["g-608","d-6548","d-6546"],"milestone":11,"inSection":"sec-composition-4","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"opr-1550","kind":"requirement","statement":"Every tenant operation of a tenant SHALL be listed in the operation catalogue under the name tenant.<operation id>, with its inputs as its input schema and the schema version as its version, marked permitted for each principal its invokers name.","rationale":"Agents and people find and call the same operations (AGT-001, AGT-002).","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"OPR-1550","area":"10-product","section":"Tenant operations","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`list-operations`","traces":["g-20","d-6549"],"milestone":11,"inSection":"sec-composition-4","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"opr-1551","kind":"requirement","statement":"A schema change that removes an object type, a field, a unit, a pool, a segment or a setting that a tenant operation names SHALL be refused while the operation names it.","rationale":"An operation never refers to something that is gone.","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"OPR-1551","area":"10-product","section":"Tenant operations","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`change-schema`","traces":["g-20","d-6546"],"milestone":11,"inSection":"sec-composition-4","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"opr-1552","kind":"requirement","statement":"A dry run of an invocation SHALL return the result the invocation would have and SHALL commit nothing.","rationale":"An agent previews an operation as it previews any other (AGT-008).","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"OPR-1552","area":"10-product","section":"Tenant operations","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`decide-tenant-operation`","traces":["g-20","d-6549"],"milestone":11,"inSection":"sec-composition-4","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"opr-1553","kind":"requirement","statement":"A product file SHALL declare a tenant operation as an item of its operations section, a value of tenant-operation-def whose steps use only the step kinds of OPR-1540 and whose expressions are in the tenant rule language, and a product file that declares code to register, or a step outside tenant-operation-step, SHALL be refused.","rationale":"NG-3 holds over the phrase of D-103 (D-6546).","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"OPR-1553","area":"10-product","section":"Tenant operations","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`product layer`","traces":["g-20","d-6546","d-6549","ng-3"],"milestone":11,"inSection":"sec-composition-4","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"opr-1554","kind":"requirement","statement":"Each domain event that an accepted invocation commits SHALL carry the hop count 0, as a change requested by a person does.","rationale":"An invocation by a person starts a chain of triggers, it does not continue one (SCH-300).","evaluate":{"method":"property"},"ref":"OPR-1554","area":"10-product","section":"Tenant operations","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-2","boundaryDetail":"`commit`","traces":["g-606","d-6548"],"milestone":11,"inSection":"sec-composition-4","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"ldg-1540","kind":"requirement","statement":"A tenant policy SHALL be able to name the ledger, or the ledger of one unit, as its resource, with a condition that reads the owner, pool, unit and scope of an account and the amount, reason, caused_by and at of an entry, and a read under ledger-read SHALL return only the accounts and entries such policies permit.","rationale":"\"The owner reads their own\" becomes a policy (LDG-024).","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"LDG-1540","area":"10-product","section":"Ledger reach","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`authorize`","traces":["g-604","d-6550"],"milestone":11,"inSection":"sec-composition-5","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"ldg-1541","kind":"requirement","statement":"A signed-in person SHALL be able to read the balance and the entries of the accounts the person owns under ledger-read-own, and a read under ledger-read-own SHALL return nothing of an account owned by another principal or by a pool.","rationale":"A member sees their points without a capability that reaches anyone else's.","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"LDG-1541","area":"10-product","section":"Ledger reach","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`read-my-ledger-balance`","traces":["g-604","d-6550"],"milestone":11,"inSection":"sec-composition-5","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"ldg-1542","kind":"requirement","statement":"The floor, cap and cap per period declared for a unit SHALL apply to each account of the unit, of every scope, separately.","rationale":"One declaration bounds every promotion's stock and every person's count.","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"LDG-1542","area":"10-product","section":"Ledger reach","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`decide-ledger-posting`","traces":["g-602","d-6551"],"milestone":11,"inSection":"sec-composition-5","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"ldg-1543","kind":"requirement","statement":"A ranked listing of the accounts of a unit SHALL return at most one hundred accounts per page in order of balance, equal balances in ascending order of the owner, SHALL examine at most ten thousand accounts, and SHALL be refused with scan-bound-exceeded before it reads when it would examine more.","rationale":"A leaderboard has a stated cost (D-5062).","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"LDG-1543","area":"10-product","section":"Ledger reach","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-9","boundaryDetail":"`list-ledger-accounts`","traces":["g-604","d-6552","k-100"],"milestone":11,"inSection":"sec-composition-5","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"ldg-1544","kind":"requirement","statement":"A ranked listing SHALL leave out every account of which the policies of the reader do not permit every entry.","rationale":"A rank never discloses an entry the reader cannot read.","evaluate":{"method":"property"},"ref":"LDG-1544","area":"10-product","section":"Ledger reach","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-9","boundaryDetail":"`list-ledger-accounts`","traces":["g-604","d-6552","d-5011"],"milestone":11,"inSection":"sec-composition-5","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"ldg-1545","kind":"requirement","statement":"A debit to an account of a unit that declares an expiry SHALL consume the remaining credit of its periods oldest first.","rationale":"Points that expire first are spent first.","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"LDG-1545","area":"10-product","section":"Ledger reach","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`decide-ledger-posting`","traces":["g-601","d-6553"],"milestone":11,"inSection":"sec-composition-5","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"ldg-1546","kind":"requirement","statement":"For each account with credit remaining in a period whose life has ended, the platform SHALL post one entry of minus the remaining amount with the key expiry:<period start> and the reason expiry, no later than one day after the end of that life.","rationale":"Expiry is an entry, so the balance stays the sum of its entries (LDG-020).","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"LDG-1546","area":"10-product","section":"Ledger reach","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-7","boundaryDetail":"`expire-ledger-credits`","traces":["g-601","d-6553"],"milestone":11,"inSection":"sec-composition-5","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"ldg-1547","kind":"requirement","statement":"One transaction of the expiry of credits SHALL handle at most one hundred accounts.","rationale":"Expiry costs batches, as segments do.","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"LDG-1547","area":"10-product","section":"Ledger reach","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-7","boundaryDetail":"`expire-ledger-credits`","traces":["g-608","d-6553"],"milestone":11,"inSection":"sec-composition-5","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"ldg-1548","kind":"requirement","statement":"A holder of ledger-read SHALL be able to list every unit, pool and limit that the tenant has declared.","rationale":"A tenant can see what it declared.","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"LDG-1548","area":"10-product","section":"Ledger reach","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`list-ledger-definitions`","traces":["g-604","d-6554"],"milestone":11,"inSection":"sec-composition-5","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"ldg-1549","kind":"requirement","statement":"Removing a unit or a pool that an account names SHALL be refused, and removing a limit SHALL change no entry and no balance.","rationale":"Entries keep their unit; a limit applies to later postings only (LDG-016).","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"LDG-1549","area":"10-product","section":"Ledger reach","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`remove-ledger-definition`","traces":["g-601","d-6554"],"milestone":11,"inSection":"sec-composition-5","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"ldg-1550","kind":"requirement","statement":"A tenant SHALL hold at most 64 units, 64 pools and 10,000 account limits, and a declaration past one of these SHALL be refused.","rationale":"Definitions that every decision may load are few.","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"LDG-1550","area":"10-product","section":"Ledger reach","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`declare-ledger-unit`","traces":["g-608","d-6554"],"milestone":11,"inSection":"sec-composition-5","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"seg-1540","kind":"requirement","statement":"list-my-segments SHALL list to a signed-in person every segment marked visible to members that holds a membership of the person, and no other segment.","rationale":"A member learns their membership only where the tenant chose to show it.","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"SEG-1540","area":"04-automation","section":"Segment reach","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-7","boundaryDetail":"`list-my-segments`","traces":["g-607","d-6555"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-composition-6","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"seg-1541","kind":"requirement","statement":"A count of the members of a segment SHALL count only the persons whose subject records the reader may read, and SHALL be refused with scan-bound-exceeded when the reader may not read every subject record and the count would examine more than ten thousand memberships.","rationale":"A count is a read, filtered by policy, with a stated cost.","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"SEG-1541","area":"04-automation","section":"Segment reach","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-7","boundaryDetail":"`count-segment-members`","traces":["g-607","g-608","d-6555"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-composition-6","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"seg-1542","kind":"requirement","statement":"A preview of a draft predicate SHALL evaluate it for at most one thousand persons whose subject records the caller may read, SHALL change no state, and SHALL return how many matched and how many were examined.","rationale":"A definer sees the size of an audience before saving it.","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"SEG-1542","area":"04-automation","section":"Segment reach","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-7","boundaryDetail":"`preview-segment-predicate`","traces":["g-607","g-608","d-6555"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-composition-6","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"seg-1543","kind":"requirement","statement":"The batch and refresh jobs of a segment SHALL count against the job admission rate and the daily job quota of its tenant.","rationale":"The definitions of a tenant cause these jobs (D-508, SCH-302).","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"SEG-1543","area":"04-automation","section":"Segment reach","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-7","boundaryDetail":"`run-segment-batch`","traces":["g-608","d-6555","d-508"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-composition-6","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"seg-1544","kind":"requirement","statement":"A refresh for which the daily job quota of the tenant has no room SHALL be skipped and recorded on the segment with its time, and SHALL refuse no commit.","rationale":"Membership lags a refresh rather than the tenant's own changes failing.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"SEG-1544","area":"04-automation","section":"Segment reach","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-7","boundaryDetail":"`define-schedule`","traces":["g-608","d-6555"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-composition-6","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"seg-1545","kind":"requirement","statement":"A refresh of a segment whose time-dependent predicate is indexable SHALL evaluate only the persons whose recorded next change time is at or before the time of the refresh, and every person SHALL still enter or leave at the first refresh after the value changed.","rationale":"The cost of a refresh is the persons who change, not the persons there are.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"SEG-1545","area":"04-automation","section":"Segment reach","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-7","boundaryDetail":"`run-segment-batch`","traces":["g-608","d-6555"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-composition-6","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"seg-1546","kind":"requirement","statement":"A segment whose time-dependent predicate is not indexable SHALL declare a refresh interval of at least fifteen minutes, and a definition with a shorter one SHALL be refused.","rationale":"A full refresh is the expensive case and is spaced accordingly.","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"SEG-1546","area":"04-automation","section":"Segment reach","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-7","boundaryDetail":"`define-segment`","traces":["g-608","d-6555"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-composition-6","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"seg-1547","kind":"requirement","statement":"A tenant SHALL hold at most five time-dependent segments whose predicates are not indexable, and the definition of a sixth SHALL be refused.","rationale":"Full refreshes are bounded per tenant.","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"SEG-1547","area":"04-automation","section":"Segment reach","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-7","boundaryDetail":"`define-segment`","traces":["g-608","d-6555"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-composition-6","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"seg-1548","kind":"requirement","statement":"A segment definition SHALL name the field of its subject type that holds the principal of the person, and SHALL be refused when that field is not a required unique string field.","rationale":"The mapping from a record to a person is stated, not assumed (D-5020).","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"SEG-1548","area":"04-automation","section":"Segment reach","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-7","boundaryDetail":"`define-segment`","traces":["g-605","d-6555"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-composition-6","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"seg-1549","kind":"requirement","statement":"A posting to the account of a person SHALL evaluate, in the transaction that commits it, every segment whose predicate reads the balance of that unit for that person, and SHALL write the entry and exit events the evaluation causes.","rationale":"\"Level 2 at 500 points\" enters at the posting that crosses it.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"SEG-1549","area":"04-automation","section":"Segment reach","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-7","boundaryDetail":"`decide-segment-membership`","traces":["g-606","d-6559","d-6544"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-composition-6","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"seg-1550","kind":"requirement","statement":"A change of a person-level override SHALL evaluate in its transaction the segments whose predicate reads that setting for that person, and a change at the team, tenant or platform level SHALL evaluate them in batches as a change of predicate does.","rationale":"A segment over a preference stays current without a timer.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"SEG-1550","area":"04-automation","section":"Segment reach","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-7","boundaryDetail":"`decide-segment-membership`","traces":["g-606","d-6544"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-composition-6","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"set-1540","kind":"requirement","statement":"The argument of a view section SHALL be able to take its value from a setting resolved for the reader, and the copy of the view SHALL be keyed and classed as SET-050 and SET-053 state.","rationale":"A page that depends on a setting is declared, not hand-written (SET-041).","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"SET-1540","area":"09-administration","section":"Setting reach","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`view section`","traces":["g-610","d-6557"],"milestone":6,"inSection":"sec-composition-7","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"set-1541","kind":"requirement","statement":"The mail dispatcher and the notification service SHALL resolve the setting of a recipient with the value setting-resolve gives that recipient, and no tenant principal SHALL be able to resolve the setting of another person.","rationale":"Preferences decide delivery without exposing them to other people.","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"SET-1541","area":"09-administration","section":"Setting reach","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`resolve-setting-for`","traces":["g-610","d-6557"],"milestone":6,"inSection":"sec-composition-7","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"set-1542","kind":"requirement","statement":"A value resolved for a recipient SHALL be written to no log, no copy and no event.","rationale":"A person-level value can be personal data (D-5048).","evaluate":{"method":"property"},"ref":"SET-1542","area":"09-administration","section":"Setting reach","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`resolve-setting-for`","traces":["g-610","d-6557","d-5048"],"milestone":6,"inSection":"sec-composition-7","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"set-1543","kind":"requirement","statement":"The event of a change of a setting SHALL carry no value at any level.","rationale":"The journal and its subscribers never hold a preference (D-5048).","evaluate":{"method":"property"},"ref":"SET-1543","area":"09-administration","section":"Setting reach","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`setting-changed`","traces":["g-610","d-6557","d-5048"],"milestone":6,"inSection":"sec-composition-7","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"m-operation-all-or-nothing","kind":"invariant","models":"opr-1541","statement":"Every redemption record has its debit of the pool and its count for the person, and a refused invocation leaves none of them.","evaluate":{"method":"state-invariant","scenarios":["promotion-pool-exhausted","promotion-redeemed-and-retried"],"expr":"promotion-redeem-flow.redemptions == promotion-redeem-flow.poolDebits && promotion-redeem-flow.redemptions == promotion-redeem-flow.counta + promotion-redeem-flow.countb + promotion-redeem-flow.countd","negatives":[{"scenario":"promotion-pool-exhausted","faults":["defect-opr-partial-commit"]}]},"faultModel":"fault-model-launch","assumptions":["a-model-abstraction"],"faultBasis":"fault"},
    {"id":"m-operation-pool-within-floor","kind":"invariant","models":"ldg-1542","statement":"The stock of the promotion never goes below zero, whoever redeems.","evaluate":{"method":"state-invariant","scenarios":["promotion-pool-exhausted"],"expr":"promotion-redeem-flow.stock >= 0","negatives":[{"scenario":"promotion-pool-exhausted","faults":["defect-opr-pool-floor-ignored"]}]},"faultModel":"fault-model-launch","assumptions":["a-model-abstraction"],"faultBasis":"fault"},
    {"id":"m-operation-segment-checked","kind":"invariant","models":"opr-1542","statement":"No person outside the eligible segment redeems.","evaluate":{"method":"state-invariant","scenarios":["promotion-redeemed-and-retried"],"expr":"promotion-redeem-flow.nonMember == 0","negatives":[{"scenario":"promotion-redeemed-and-retried","faults":["defect-opr-segment-ignored"]}]},"faultModel":"fault-model-launch","assumptions":["a-model-abstraction"],"faultBasis":"fault"},
    {"id":"m-operation-once-per-key","kind":"invariant","models":"opr-1544","statement":"However often an invocation with one key arrives, the redemptions are as many as the keys that were applied.","evaluate":{"method":"state-invariant","scenarios":["promotion-redeemed-and-retried","promotion-redeem-delivered-twice"],"expr":"promotion-redeem-flow.redemptions == promotion-redeem-flow.keysApplied","negatives":[{"scenario":"promotion-redeemed-and-retried","faults":["defect-opr-replay-applies-again"]},{"scenario":"promotion-redeem-delivered-twice","faults":["defect-opr-replay-applies-again"]}]},"faultModel":"fault-model-launch","assumptions":["a-model-abstraction"],"faultBasis":"fault"},
    {"id":"m-operation-limit-per-person","kind":"invariant","models":"opr-1542","statement":"No person redeems more often than the promotion allows.","evaluate":{"method":"state-invariant","scenarios":["promotion-redeemed-and-retried","promotion-redeem-delivered-twice"],"expr":"promotion-redeem-flow.counta <= promotion-redeem-flow.limit && promotion-redeem-flow.countb <= promotion-redeem-flow.limit && promotion-redeem-flow.countd <= promotion-redeem-flow.limit","negatives":[{"scenario":"promotion-redeemed-and-retried","faults":["defect-opr-replay-applies-again"]}]},"faultModel":"fault-model-launch","assumptions":["a-model-abstraction"],"faultBasis":"fault"},
    {"id":"wfl-1520","kind":"requirement","statement":"A trigger SHALL be stored as tenant metadata under the schema version, holding one variant of trigger-event, an optional condition in the tenant rule language and the automation it starts, and only a principal holding automations-define SHALL define or remove one.","rationale":"A trigger is data like a segment or a workflow, so it is versioned, projected and exported with the tenant, and no tenant code runs (NG-3).","evaluate":{"method":"property"},"ref":"WFL-1520","area":"04-automation","section":"Triggers","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-7","boundaryDetail":"`trigger`","traces":["g-13","g-16","d-6520"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-automation-2","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"wfl-1521","kind":"requirement","statement":"A committed domain event SHALL start a run of the automation of each active trigger whose event variant matches it and whose condition is true on the parameters the event binds, and SHALL start no run for a trigger whose condition is false.","rationale":"A condition evaluated in the transaction of the event sees the state that the event describes, not a later one (D-6524).","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"WFL-1521","area":"04-automation","section":"Triggers","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-7","boundaryDetail":"`trigger`","traces":["g-13","d-6523","d-6524"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-automation-2","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"int-1522","kind":"requirement","statement":"A definition whose action is not a variant of the automation-step union, or whose trigger event is not a variant of the trigger-event union, SHALL be refused by define-automation, define-trigger and activate-workflow, and a product file that declares one SHALL be refused by specc with layer.outside-catalogue.","rationale":"INT-153 refuses what is outside the published catalogue; the two unions are that catalogue, so the refusal can be checked by a tool and by the platform alike.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"INT-1522","area":"04-automation","section":"The step catalogue","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-8","boundaryDetail":"`activation`","traces":["g-16","g-156","d-506","d-6522"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-automation-3","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"wfl-1523","kind":"requirement","statement":"A step SHALL be given only the inputs that its variant of automation-step declares, and a completed step SHALL record as its result the variant of automation-step-result of the same name, whose fields later steps read as param.<step>_<field>.","rationale":"Typed inputs and outputs are what let an automation be checked at definition instead of failing at run time.","evaluate":{"method":"property"},"ref":"WFL-1523","area":"04-automation","section":"The step catalogue","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-8","boundaryDetail":"`workflow step`","traces":["g-31","d-6522","d-6523"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-automation-3","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"sch-1524","kind":"requirement","statement":"Every attempt of one step SHALL carry the same idempotency key, derived from the tenant, the automation, the run, the step name and the member of a fan-out, and an effect carrying that key SHALL be applied once however many attempts are made.","rationale":"A retry after a lost result must not award a badge, post points or send a mail twice (SCH-015); a key that changed with the attempt would.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"SCH-1524","area":"04-automation","section":"Retries and effects","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-7","boundaryDetail":"`step job`","traces":["g-14","d-6528"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-automation-4","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"sch-1525","kind":"requirement","statement":"A failed step attempt SHALL be retried until the attempts of its retry policy are spent, each delay doubling from its first delay up to its maximum delay, and a step that spends them SHALL fail its run, run the compensations of its completed steps and write a dead-lettered exception record.","rationale":"Retries are bounded per step so that a step whose effect cannot succeed ends visibly instead of retrying for ever.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"SCH-1525","area":"04-automation","section":"Retries and effects","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-7","boundaryDetail":"`step job`","traces":["g-14","d-6529"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-automation-4","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"sch-1526","kind":"requirement","statement":"A step attempt that has not reported its result when the timeout of its step has passed SHALL count as a failed attempt, and a result reported for it afterwards SHALL be refused by the fencing token of its lease.","rationale":"A slow attempt and its retry must not both record an outcome (K-17).","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"SCH-1526","area":"04-automation","section":"Retries and effects","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-7","boundaryDetail":"`step job`","traces":["g-14","k-17","d-6529"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-automation-4","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"wfl-1527","kind":"requirement","statement":"Every intent of an automated step SHALL be decided by the kernel with the automation principal automation:<workflow-id> as its principal, holding the roles that the run-as of the automation names and no other.","rationale":"An automated step is authorised by the same policies as a person (K-13), and its authority is fixed when the automation is defined, not taken from whoever caused the event.","evaluate":{"method":"property"},"ref":"WFL-1527","area":"04-automation","section":"Authority","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-8","boundaryDetail":"`automation principal`","traces":["g-25","k-13","d-6525"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-automation-5","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"wfl-1528","kind":"requirement","statement":"Defining or activating an automation SHALL be refused when its run-as names a role that the defining principal may not confer under ADM-152.","rationale":"An automation must never hold what its definer does not, or defining one would be a way to gain a capability.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"WFL-1528","area":"04-automation","section":"Authority","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-8","boundaryDetail":"`automation definition`","traces":["g-25","d-6525"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-automation-5","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"wfl-1529","kind":"requirement","statement":"A change that leaves the definer of an automation unable to confer a role of its run-as, including the erasure of the definer, SHALL suspend the automation in the transaction of the change, and no step of it SHALL run until a principal who may confer every such role defines it again.","rationale":"The bound of WFL-1528 holds for as long as the automation exists, not only at the moment it was defined.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"WFL-1529","area":"04-automation","section":"Authority","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-8","boundaryDetail":"`automation definition`","traces":["g-25","d-6526"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-automation-5","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"wfl-1530","kind":"requirement","statement":"Each record change, ledger posting, message and notice made by an automated step SHALL name the automation principal as the principal that caused it and the run as its correlation, and the run record SHALL name the definer on whose authority the run acts.","rationale":"An automated change is attributable to the automation and to the person who gave it its authority (G-25), and caused-by is a principal (LDG-027).","evaluate":{"method":"property"},"ref":"WFL-1530","area":"04-automation","section":"Authority","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-8","boundaryDetail":"`automation principal`","traces":["g-25","d-6527"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-automation-5","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"wfl-1531","kind":"requirement","statement":"The automation worker SHALL write one run record for each automation run and one step record for each step it runs, each with its state, its attempts and the error of each failed attempt, and list-automation-runs and list-automation-steps SHALL answer them to a holder of automations-read.","rationale":"A tenant owner explains what an automation did from its records, without platform staff.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"WFL-1531","area":"04-automation","section":"Runs and exceptions","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-7","boundaryDetail":"`automation run`","traces":["g-14","g-156","d-6530"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-automation-6","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"sch-1532","kind":"requirement","statement":"A trigger that creates no job for an event because of the hop limit, the job quota, a suspended, inactive or removed automation, a repeated run key or a condition that cannot be evaluated, an event parked under D-519 and a dead-lettered step SHALL each write one exception record naming its reason in the transaction that decides it, listed by list-automation-exceptions.","rationale":"A missed badge award or a cut chain otherwise leaves no trace, and nobody can tell why nothing happened.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"SCH-1532","area":"04-automation","section":"Runs and exceptions","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-7","boundaryDetail":"`trigger`","traces":["g-14","d-6530"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-automation-6","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"sch-1533","kind":"requirement","statement":"A run SHALL carry the hop count of the event that started it, a wait step SHALL leave that count unchanged, every event committed by a step of the run SHALL carry the count plus one, and an event of a schedule SHALL carry the count zero.","rationale":"Waiting does not end a loop, so a chain through delayed steps meets the limit of eight like any other (SCH-300), while a multi-step campaign is one run and uses no hops at all (D-6531).","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"SCH-1533","area":"04-automation","section":"Chains, order and quota","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-7","boundaryDetail":"`trigger`","traces":["g-13","d-700","d-6531"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-automation-7","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"sch-1534","kind":"requirement","statement":"The runs that one trigger starts for events with the same run key SHALL start in the order of the sequence numbers of those events, and none SHALL start while an earlier one with the same key is open, except that the run of an event parked under D-519 starts after the owner releases it.","rationale":"A product that awards a level after a threshold depends on seeing the threshold first; a parked event must not stop a person's later events for ever (D-519).","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"SCH-1534","area":"04-automation","section":"Chains, order and quota","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-7","boundaryDetail":"`trigger`","traces":["g-13","d-519","d-6532"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-automation-7","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"sch-1535","kind":"requirement","statement":"A commit that creates jobs past the daily job quota of the tenant's plan SHALL commit its change, and each job past the quota SHALL be created due at the start of the next quota day and recorded as held, so that the quota never refuses the change that creates a job.","rationale":"The business change and its automation are separate: refusing a member's change because of the tenant's automation volume would break the product, and dropping the job would lose an award. Mail past its quota is held the same way (EML-021).","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"SCH-1535","area":"04-automation","section":"Chains, order and quota","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-7","boundaryDetail":"`job admission`","traces":["g-4","g-157","d-508","d-6533"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-automation-7","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"sch-1536","kind":"requirement","statement":"An automation with a run key SHALL start at most one run for each value of that key for as long as the automation exists, and an event whose key repeats SHALL start no run and write a declined exception record with reason run-key-repeated.","rationale":"Award once means once per person, not once per event: a balance that crosses a threshold, falls back and crosses again awards nothing new.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"SCH-1536","area":"04-automation","section":"Retries and effects","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-7","boundaryDetail":"`automation run`","traces":["g-14","d-6534"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-automation-4","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"wfl-1537","kind":"requirement","statement":"A wait step SHALL hold its run with no lease and SHALL resume it by a job due at the end of its duration or at the time its expression gives, and a wait of more than 366 days SHALL be refused when the automation is defined.","rationale":"A wait is a due job like any other (D-526), so a delayed follow-up costs nothing while it waits and survives a restart (WFL-004).","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"WFL-1537","area":"04-automation","section":"The step catalogue","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-8","boundaryDetail":"`wait step`","traces":["g-13","d-6535"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-automation-3","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"wfl-1538","kind":"requirement","statement":"A fan-out step SHALL run its step once for each member of its segment at the time each batch runs, in batches of at most its batch size and never more than one hundred members, each batch one job, and SHALL go to its next step once every member has reached an end.","rationale":"A segment can hold every person of a tenant, so its work is cut into the batches that D-5026 uses for evaluation.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"WFL-1538","area":"04-automation","section":"The step catalogue","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-8","boundaryDetail":"`fan-out step`","traces":["g-608","d-5026","d-6535"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-automation-3","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"wfl-1539","kind":"requirement","statement":"A change that moves a workflow field through a named transition SHALL start the runs of the triggers on record-updated for that object and transition, and an update-record step that sets a workflow field SHALL be decided by the kernel against the guard of the transition like any update by its principal.","rationale":"A record's state machine and the automation that reacts to it stay two definitions joined by one event, so the kernel keeps deciding transitions synchronously (D-6521).","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"WFL-1539","area":"04-automation","section":"Field workflows and automations","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-8","boundaryDetail":"`workflow field`","traces":["g-31","d-13","d-6521"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-automation-8","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"ten-1680","kind":"requirement","statement":"The backend SHALL keep, for each tenant, the host names that serve it and the origins each is reached at, SHALL list every binding of every tenant to a caller that presents the service token and to no other, and SHALL bind a host name to one tenant only: binding it to a second tenant, naming a tenant that does not exist, or giving an origin that is not http or https followed by a host and an optional port SHALL be refused.","rationale":"A gateway that can learn its sites only from an environment variable needs a restart for every tenant created while it runs; the list is what it learns them from, and a host that two tenants held would serve one of them the other's site.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"TEN-1680","area":"02-tenancy","section":"Host bindings","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-3","boundaryDetail":"`host binding`","traces":["g-1","d-6680"],"milestone":2,"inSection":"sec-tenancy-1680","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"gwy-1680","kind":"requirement","statement":"The gateway SHALL learn the host names it serves and their origins from the backend's list of host bindings, so that a tenant bound while the gateway runs is served on the next request that names its host and its origins are accepted for that site only; STRATA_SITES and STRATA_ORIGINS SHALL remain a static override that is consulted first and that no learned entry replaces.","rationale":"A tenant created at run time otherwise needs a gateway restart, and a list the backend could rewrite must not be able to move a host the operator pinned.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"GWY-1680","area":"01-core","section":"Tenant hosts, shutdown and slow clients at the edge","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-9","boundaryDetail":"`host list`","traces":["g-250","d-6680"],"milestone":2,"inSection":"sec-runtime-1680","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"gwy-1681","kind":"requirement","statement":"The gateway SHALL fetch the list of host bindings again when it is older than STRATA_HOSTS_MAX_AGE_SECS (default 60) and when a request names a host that no list holds, SHALL call the backend for it at most once per STRATA_HOSTS_MISS_INTERVAL_SECS (default 5) whatever asks and whether or not the call succeeds, SHALL share one call among concurrent requests, and SHALL stop believing a learned list that is more than ten times the maximum age old.","rationale":"Unknown host names are chosen by whoever sends them, so a refresh that follows each would let a scan of made-up names hammer the backend, and a list that is never retired keeps serving a host the backend dropped.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"GWY-1681","area":"01-core","section":"Tenant hosts, shutdown and slow clients at the edge","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-9","boundaryDetail":"`host list`","traces":["g-250","d-6680"],"milestone":2,"inSection":"sec-runtime-1680","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"gwy-1682","kind":"requirement","statement":"On a stop signal the server SHALL tell every long-lived task it holds (the WebSocket relays of the gateway and the WebSocket connections of the backend) to close, each SHALL send its Close frame and end, and the server SHALL wait for them within the drain deadline (STRATA_DRAIN_TIMEOUT_SECS) before it returns.","rationale":"An upgraded socket runs outside the connections the server drains, so without a signal it is cut at process exit with no Close frame and its browser cannot tell a stop from a failure.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"GWY-1682","area":"01-core","section":"Tenant hosts, shutdown and slow clients at the edge","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-19","boundaryDetail":"`stop signal`","traces":["g-250"],"milestone":2,"inSection":"sec-runtime-1680","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"gwy-1683","kind":"requirement","statement":"A gateway that is not started for development SHALL refuse a request that carries X-Forwarded-For while STRATA_TRUSTED_PROXIES names no proxy, with status 400 and the reason forwarded_without_trusted_proxies in the body; a gateway started for development SHALL serve the request and warn once.","rationale":"With no proxy trusted every visitor behind a proxy is one source for every limit, and a header that nothing believes is a sign of a deployment that is misconfigured.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"GWY-1683","area":"01-core","section":"Tenant hosts, shutdown and slow clients at the edge","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-9","boundaryDetail":"`X-Forwarded-For`","traces":["g-250"],"milestone":2,"inSection":"sec-runtime-1680","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"gwy-1684","kind":"requirement","statement":"A server SHALL drop a connection whose client has not read for STRATA_WRITE_IDLE_TIMEOUT_SECS (default 30) while the server has bytes to send for it, upgraded connections included, and SHALL free the place the connection held under the limit on open connections.","rationale":"A client that asks for a large response and never reads it otherwise holds one of a bounded number of connections for ever.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"GWY-1684","area":"01-core","section":"Tenant hosts, shutdown and slow clients at the edge","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-9","boundaryDetail":"`write idle timeout`","traces":["g-250"],"milestone":2,"inSection":"sec-runtime-1680","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"idn-1680","kind":"requirement","statement":"The message that tells the owner of a new tenant that the site is ready SHALL carry an invitation link that is accepted once, in whatever browser opens it, within seven days of its making and not after, and accepting it SHALL replace the password of the owner's account with the one the owner chooses, at least ten characters long, and sign nobody in.","rationale":"The sign-in link is bound to the browser that asked for it, and the owner has asked for nothing yet.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"IDN-1680","area":"03-identity","section":"The invitation of a new tenant's owner","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-4","boundaryDetail":"`POST /sign-in/invite/accept`","traces":["g-46","d-6681"],"milestone":2,"inSection":"sec-identity-1680","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"idn-1681","kind":"requirement","statement":"An invitation SHALL be stored under the hash of its identifier and SHALL hold the hash of its token, the principal and the origin of the site, and no email address and no value that opens the link.","rationale":"A copy of the store must open no invitation (PRV-365).","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"IDN-1681","area":"03-identity","section":"The invitation of a new tenant's owner","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-4","boundaryDetail":"`invitation`","traces":["g-46","d-6681"],"milestone":2,"inSection":"sec-identity-1680","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"idn-1682","kind":"requirement","statement":"An invitation SHALL be accepted only from the origin of the site it was made for, every attempt to accept one SHALL count against the limits of the invitation, the source and the realm, and an attempt that is refused SHALL NOT spend the invitation.","rationale":"A guess must neither be free nor be a way to spend the owner's only link.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"IDN-1682","area":"03-identity","section":"The invitation of a new tenant's owner","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-4","boundaryDetail":"`POST /sign-in/invite/accept`","traces":["g-46","d-6681"],"milestone":2,"inSection":"sec-identity-1680","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"int-1700","kind":"requirement","statement":"A value in a typed section of a product file SHALL conform to the platform type of its section, and specc and Exegra SHALL refuse a value that does not with layer.value-invalid, and a union value whose variant the platform union lacks with layer.outside-catalogue.","rationale":"One table of sections and one generic check keep the two tools from disagreeing and make a new section a row of the table (D-6700).","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"INT-1700","area":"10-product","section":"Tenant operations","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`product layer`","traces":["g-20","d-6700","d-6536","d-6580"],"milestone":11,"inSection":"sec-composition-4","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"int-1701","kind":"requirement","statement":"Every entity id of a product file SHALL begin with the namespace of its product, and a name in a typed section in that namespace SHALL be declared by the product file that holds it; specc and Exegra SHALL refuse an id outside the namespace with layer.namespace-missing, an undeclared name with layer.reference-unknown and a name that another product declares with layer.cross-product-reference.","rationale":"The namespace keeps the ids of two products apart and shows an installed entity its owner (D-6582, D-6597).","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"INT-1701","area":"10-product","section":"Tenant operations","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`product layer`","traces":["g-20","d-6582","d-6597","d-6700"],"milestone":11,"inSection":"sec-composition-4","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"int-1702","kind":"requirement","statement":"A product file SHALL declare every object type, ledger unit, ledger pool, template, role, policy and automation that its triggers, automations, operations and policies name, so that a tenant can install the product from its file alone, and the semantic hash of the platform SHALL NOT depend on any product file.","rationale":"A product that names what it does not declare cannot be installed (composition findings F4 and F9).","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"INT-1702","area":"10-product","section":"Tenant operations","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`product layer`","traces":["g-20","d-6700","d-6580"],"milestone":11,"inSection":"sec-composition-4","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"int-1920","kind":"requirement","statement":"The command specc bundle SHALL write, for one product file, one deterministic tenant bundle that holds every item of every typed section, role and capability of the file as the entry of its section in bundle-sections, with the product id, the version and the platform range of the product header, and SHALL refuse a product with no version (bundle.version-missing), a section that bundle-sections has no place for (bundle.section-no-place) and two entities that would share an id (bundle.id-collision) without writing a file.","rationale":"A tenant installs a product as a bundle, and a product file that cannot become one cannot be installed (D-6580, D-6920).","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"INT-1920","area":"10-product","section":"Tenant operations","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`product layer`","traces":["g-20","d-6920","d-6580","d-6700"],"milestone":11,"inSection":"sec-composition-4","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"int-1921","kind":"requirement","statement":"An install of a bundle SHALL install the record types with their fields, constraints, retention, publication and language declarations, the roles, role permissions, policies, queries, views, workflows, mail templates, notice templates, tokens, triggers, automations and operations it holds as one schema change that also records which product owns them, and SHALL refuse a bundle that fills a section the kernel has no intent for (capabilities, segments, settings, ledger units, pools and limits) as an invalid bundle that names each such section, without installing any part of it.","rationale":"A section that is silently left out would leave a tenant with a product that is not the one its owner reviewed (INT-154); naming it says what the release cannot yet take.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"INT-1921","area":"04-automation","section":"Product bundles: install, upgrade and remove","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-product-lifecycle","boundaryDetail":"`product change`","traces":["g-167","g-103","d-6580","d-6581"],"milestone":7,"inSection":"sec-product-bundles","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"int-1922","kind":"requirement","statement":"The tenant catalogue SHALL record, for an installed product, its version, the platform range it declared, the entities it owns and the schema version its install produced, and an install of the same product and version again SHALL return that schema version and run no schema change.","rationale":"A retry of an install must answer as the first did, so it needs the version the first install produced (D-6583).","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"INT-1922","area":"04-automation","section":"Product bundles: install, upgrade and remove","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-product-lifecycle","boundaryDetail":"`product change`","traces":["g-167","g-103","d-6582","d-6583"],"milestone":7,"inSection":"sec-product-bundles","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"agg-2320","kind":"requirement","statement":"A named query SHALL be refused when it declares more than 20 aggregates.","rationale":"The platform bounds what one query can ask of it.","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"AGG-2320","area":"07-content","section":"Aggregate declaration","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-9","boundaryDetail":"`named query`","traces":["g-615","d-7320"],"milestone":6,"inSection":"sec-content-253","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"agg-2321","kind":"requirement","statement":"A named query SHALL be refused when an aggregate it declares reads a field whose type the aggregate does not admit: an integer for a sum, an integer, a string or a timestamp for a minimum, a maximum or a top list, and a single value of a scalar type for a group.","rationale":"A sum of text or a group of lists has no stated meaning.","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"AGG-2321","area":"07-content","section":"Aggregate declaration","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-9","boundaryDetail":"`named query`","traces":["g-615","d-5060"],"milestone":6,"inSection":"sec-content-253","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"agg-2322","kind":"requirement","statement":"A named query SHALL be refused when it declares a count that names a field, a sum, minimum, maximum or top aggregate that names none, a top aggregate whose length is not from 1 to 100, or an aggregate of another kind that states a length.","rationale":"Each kind has the arguments it needs and no others.","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"AGG-2322","area":"07-content","section":"Aggregate declaration","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-9","boundaryDetail":"`named query`","traces":["g-615","d-5060","d-7320"],"milestone":6,"inSection":"sec-content-253","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"agg-2323","kind":"requirement","statement":"An aggregate that has more than 1000 groups SHALL be refused with the error group-bound-exceeded and no result.","rationale":"The size of an answer is bounded as the work to make it is.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"AGG-2323","area":"07-content","section":"Aggregate bounds","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-9","boundaryDetail":"`aggregate result`","traces":["g-617","d-7320"],"milestone":6,"inSection":"sec-content-255","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"agg-2324","kind":"requirement","statement":"An aggregate over an object type that holds more than 10000 records SHALL be refused with the error scan-bound-exceeded, and the kernel SHALL load no more than 10001 records to decide so.","rationale":"This is the bound on what a plan may read (CMS-255), the same as for a named query (KRN-1288).","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"AGG-2324","area":"07-content","section":"Aggregate bounds","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-9","boundaryDetail":"`aggregate result`","traces":["g-617","d-5062","d-7320"],"milestone":6,"inSection":"sec-content-255","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"agg-2325","kind":"requirement","statement":"An aggregate SHALL be refused with the error scan-bound-exceeded when the records that the reader may read and the filter selects are more than the scan bound it declares.","rationale":"The records counted against the bound are the records of the reader, so the refusal tells the reader nothing about records it may not read (D-5062).","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"AGG-2325","area":"07-content","section":"Aggregate bounds","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-9","boundaryDetail":"`aggregate result`","traces":["g-617","d-5062"],"milestone":6,"inSection":"sec-content-255","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"ops-2440","kind":"requirement","statement":"The runtime SHALL create the one instance of an implementation-level machine that has no instance key and creates its own records, in its initial state under a fixed key, when its system host is built, and a system host built over a store that already holds a record under that key SHALL leave the record as it is.","rationale":"Exegra starts that instance at the beginning; without it every event for the machine is dropped, and a second host would start it over (D-7440).","evaluate":{"method":"property"},"ref":"OPS-2440","area":"09-operations","section":"Failure containment","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-2","boundaryDetail":"`strata_runtime::System::new`","traces":["g-14","d-7440"],"milestone":2,"realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"ops-2441","kind":"requirement","statement":"A message of the machine outbox whose dispatch fails SHALL be dispatched at most 10 times, and the tenth failure SHALL move the message to the dead letters with its receiver, the number of attempts and the error of the last attempt, after which the runtime SHALL NOT dispatch it again.","rationale":"A message that always fails otherwise stays in the outbox and is retried for as long as the database exists (D-7441, OPS-305).","evaluate":{"method":"property"},"ref":"OPS-2441","area":"09-operations","section":"Failure containment","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-2","boundaryDetail":"`strata_runtime::RetryPolicy`","traces":["g-14","d-7441"],"milestone":2,"realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"ops-2442","kind":"requirement","statement":"The purge of the runtime SHALL delete the dead letters set aside more than 90 days before and the record of each machine instance that is in a terminal state and was last saved more than 90 days before, and SHALL delete no other record, no dead letter that is younger and no singleton instance.","rationale":"Rows that hold event JSON and instance state would otherwise stay as long as the database file (PRV-356, D-7441).","evaluate":{"method":"property"},"ref":"OPS-2442","area":"09-operations","section":"Failure containment","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-2","boundaryDetail":"`strata_runtime::System::purge`","traces":["g-14","d-7441"],"milestone":2,"realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"prv-2460","kind":"requirement","statement":"The erasure of a subject SHALL clear every field of a tenant record type that declares the principal as its data subject, by the creator of the record or by a text field that holds the principal id, and SHALL keep every field that declares no such subject and every record whose subject is another person.","rationale":"The erasure reaches what the declaration names, and nothing else.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"PRV-2460","area":"09-privacy","section":"Data subject rights","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-350","boundaryDetail":"`strata_kernel::erasure`","traces":["g-350","k-352"],"milestone":6,"inSection":"sec-privacy-2","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"prv-2461","kind":"requirement","statement":"An erasure of a subject SHALL decide at most 100 changed records at a time and SHALL return whether more remain and where the next decision continues, and a repeat after the last batch SHALL change nothing.","rationale":"A person with many records is erased in bounded commits, and a repeated request is safe.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"PRV-2461","area":"09-privacy","section":"Data subject rights","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-350","boundaryDetail":"`strata_kernel::erasure`","traces":["g-350","k-352"],"milestone":6,"inSection":"sec-privacy-2","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"prv-2462","kind":"requirement","statement":"The events an erasure of a subject writes SHALL carry no value of a field that was erased.","rationale":"The stream that is delivered and kept after the erasure must not bring the erased values back.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"PRV-2462","area":"09-privacy","section":"Data subject rights","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-350","boundaryDetail":"`strata_kernel::erasure`","traces":["g-350","k-352"],"milestone":6,"inSection":"sec-privacy-2","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"prv-2463","kind":"requirement","statement":"The receipt of an erasure SHALL list each copy it did not reach, with the reason, and SHALL state the restriction of processing and each legal hold in force when the erasure ended, and the erasure SHALL leave the audit log unchanged.","rationale":"An erasure that claims completeness it does not have is worse than none (PRV-353, PRV-359).","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"PRV-2463","area":"09-privacy","section":"Data subject rights","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-350","boundaryDetail":"`POST /api/subject-rights/erase`","traces":["g-350","k-352"],"milestone":6,"inSection":"sec-privacy-2","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"wfl-2200","kind":"requirement","statement":"A trigger SHALL start no run for an event about a record that its automation principal may not read, and a trigger whose condition names a field, or follows a reference into a record, that its automation principal may not read SHALL start no run and SHALL yield a declined exception with reason condition-failed.","rationale":"A condition decided with more authority than the automation holds would reveal, by which runs start, what its definer and its principal may not read (D-6524, D-7201).","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"WFL-2200","area":"04-automation","lifecycle":"active","milestone":5,"realisation":"checked","section":"Authority","boundary":"b-8","boundaryDetail":"`automation principal`","traces":["g-25","d-6524","d-6525","d-7201"],"inSection":"sec-automation-5"},
    {"id":"wfl-2201","kind":"requirement","statement":"define-trigger and define-automation SHALL record as defined-by the principal of the context, or none for the system, and as defined-at the time of the context, and SHALL ignore any value of either that the definition supplies.","rationale":"The definer bounds the authority of an automation for as long as it exists (WFL-1529), so it must be the principal the kernel authorised, not one a caller names (D-7204).","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"WFL-2201","area":"04-automation","lifecycle":"active","milestone":5,"realisation":"checked","section":"Authority","boundary":"b-8","boundaryDetail":"`automation definition`","traces":["g-25","d-6526","d-7204"],"inSection":"sec-automation-5"},
    {"id":"sch-2202","kind":"requirement","statement":"A record-updated event SHALL name, for each workflow of the record that fired a transition in the update, the name of that transition, and a trigger or a subscription selector naming a transition SHALL match only an update that fired a transition of that name.","rationale":"Two transitions between the same states with different guards are different transitions; a selector that inferred the transition from the values before and after would match both (D-7203).","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"SCH-2202","area":"04-automation","lifecycle":"active","milestone":5,"realisation":"checked","section":"Field workflows and automations","boundary":"b-8","boundaryDetail":"`workflow field`","traces":["g-31","d-6521","d-7203"],"inSection":"sec-automation-8"},
    {"id":"sch-2203","kind":"requirement","statement":"A trigger condition or run key whose evaluation needs a record that the snapshot of the transition does not hold SHALL refuse the transition with insufficient-state naming that record, and SHALL NOT be taken as false.","rationale":"A condition taken as false because a record was not loaded would silently lose a run that the committed state starts (D-6524, D-7200).","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"SCH-2203","area":"04-automation","lifecycle":"active","milestone":5,"realisation":"checked","section":"Triggers","boundary":"b-7","boundaryDetail":"`trigger`","traces":["g-13","d-6524","d-7200"],"inSection":"sec-automation-2"},
    {"id":"set-2300","kind":"requirement","statement":"A role permission that names a capability whose id has the product form SHALL be refused unless the tenant schema declares the capability, and a role whose id has a product namespace SHALL be refused a capability of another namespace.","rationale":"A capability that nobody declared confers nothing and hides a mistake, and a product capability is confined to its own product (D-6590, D-6701).","evaluate":{"method":"property"},"ref":"SET-2300","area":"09-administration","section":"Setting definitions","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-13","boundaryDetail":"`setting override`","traces":["g-610","d-7302"],"milestone":6,"inSection":"sec-administration-7","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"set-2301","kind":"requirement","statement":"A write of an override at the platform level through the tenant SHALL be refused, and a read SHALL be answered from the person, team and tenant overrides and the default while the control plane holds no platform value.","rationale":"The platform level is the control plane's (CT-303); until it holds values it contributes none.","evaluate":{"method":"property"},"ref":"SET-2301","area":"09-administration","section":"Writing settings","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-13","boundaryDetail":"`setting override`","traces":["g-612","d-7301"],"milestone":6,"inSection":"sec-administration-9","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"set-2302","kind":"requirement","statement":"Removing a setting definition SHALL remove the overrides of the setting in the same change, and SHALL be refused while a trigger names the setting.","rationale":"An override without a definition has no type and no level, and a trigger on a setting that does not exist could never fire.","evaluate":{"method":"property"},"ref":"SET-2302","area":"09-administration","section":"Setting definitions","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-13","boundaryDetail":"`setting override`","traces":["g-610","d-7300"],"milestone":6,"inSection":"sec-administration-7","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"set-2303","kind":"requirement","statement":"The revision of a setting SHALL rise by one at each change of its definition or of one of its overrides and SHALL NOT be reused, and an override SHALL carry the revision of the write that made it.","rationale":"A stale writer must never find the revision it read again after other changes (D-5045).","evaluate":{"method":"property"},"ref":"SET-2303","area":"09-administration","section":"Writing settings","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-13","boundaryDetail":"`setting override`","traces":["g-612","d-7303"],"milestone":6,"inSection":"sec-administration-9","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"set-2304","kind":"requirement","statement":"A trigger on a setting changing SHALL be refused unless the schema defines the setting.","rationale":"The kernel refuses a definition that names what does not exist (WFL-1520).","evaluate":{"method":"property"},"ref":"SET-2304","area":"09-administration","section":"Setting definitions","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-13","boundaryDetail":"`setting override`","traces":["g-610","d-7300"],"milestone":6,"inSection":"sec-administration-7","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"cms-2360","kind":"requirement","statement":"The JavaScript module that specc generates for the tenant rule language SHALL give the same syntax tree for the same text, the same text for the same syntax tree, the same shape or error text from the static check and the same value or error text from evaluation as the generated Rust module for every case of the shared case table, with the table run through the module under node by the specc test suite.","rationale":"A page that evaluates a rule must agree with the server that decides it; the table is the evidence that it does.","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"CMS-2360","area":"07-content","section":"Arithmetic and time in rules","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`tenant rule language`","traces":["g-20","d-7360","d-6543"],"milestone":2,"inSection":"sec-composition-2","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"cms-2361","kind":"requirement","statement":"The JavaScript module of the tenant rule language SHALL fail with integer-overflow when an operand or the result of checked arithmetic is not an integer within plus or minus (2^53 - 1), SHALL measure concat in bytes of UTF-8 and fail with string-too-long above 4,096, and SHALL refuse when parsing a number literal outside plus or minus (2^53 - 1).","rationale":"JavaScript numbers hold integers exactly only in that range, so the page refuses what it cannot compute exactly instead of rounding.","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"CMS-2361","area":"07-content","section":"Arithmetic and time in rules","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`tenant rule language`","traces":["g-20","d-7360","d-6540","d-6542"],"milestone":2,"inSection":"sec-composition-2","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"cms-2362","kind":"requirement","statement":"The Lab SHALL show, under each constraint rule and each workflow guard of its metadata view, that the page does not read the rule as the server printed it, when parsing the text with the JavaScript module of the tenant rule language fails or printing the result does not give the same text.","rationale":"The page parses the text the server prints; a disagreement between the two is shown where the rule is, not hidden.","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"CMS-2362","area":"07-content","section":"Arithmetic and time in rules","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`tenant rule language`","traces":["g-20","d-7360"],"milestone":2,"inSection":"sec-composition-2","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"int-2340","kind":"requirement","statement":"A schema change SHALL set and clear the retention, the publication, the language field and the translation group of an object type, a type with a personal field SHALL be refused unless the same change declares its retention, and a schema that declares none of them SHALL hash as it did before they existed.","rationale":"A tenant that cannot declare a personal field and its retention through the same operations as everything else cannot hold personal data at all (D-6584).","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"INT-2340","area":"04-automation","section":"Product bundles: install, upgrade and remove","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-product-lifecycle","boundaryDetail":"`product change`","traces":["g-167","g-103","d-6584","d-7340"],"milestone":7,"inSection":"sec-product-bundles","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"int-2341","kind":"requirement","statement":"A schema change that removes an object type SHALL be refused while records of the type exist unless it states that the records are deleted, and then SHALL delete them in the commit of the schema change; a schema change that removes a role SHALL be refused while a principal holds it.","rationale":"A removal that leaves records without a type, or people without the role they were given, would leave the tenant in a state no schema describes (D-6581).","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"INT-2341","area":"04-automation","section":"Product bundles: install, upgrade and remove","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-product-lifecycle","boundaryDetail":"`product change`","traces":["g-167","g-103","d-6581","d-7342"],"milestone":7,"inSection":"sec-product-bundles","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"int-2342","kind":"requirement","statement":"The ownership record of a product SHALL be written by the schema change that installs, upgrades or removes it, so that the entities of the product and the record of what it owns are one commit under one schema version.","rationale":"Two writes leave a window in which an entity exists that no product owns, and a retry that is refused as a conflict (D-6581, D-6582).","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"INT-2342","area":"04-automation","section":"Product bundles: install, upgrade and remove","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-product-lifecycle","boundaryDetail":"`product change`","traces":["g-167","g-103","d-6581","d-7341"],"milestone":7,"inSection":"sec-product-bundles","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"int-2343","kind":"requirement","statement":"A mail template, a notice template and a token SHALL be held in the tenant schema under its schema version; a template id SHALL name a mail template or a notice template and not both, a template SHALL have a one-line subject or title and a body that is JSON text, and a token whose expression does not parse SHALL be refused.","rationale":"A template with a header that has a line break is a header injection, and one that is not structured blocks cannot be rendered (EML-012, NTF-1570, CTK-002).","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"INT-2343","area":"04-automation","section":"Product bundles: install, upgrade and remove","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-product-lifecycle","boundaryDetail":"`product change`","traces":["g-167","d-6580","d-7341"],"milestone":7,"inSection":"sec-product-bundles","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"int-2344","kind":"requirement","statement":"An install of a bundle SHALL install the mail templates, notice templates, tokens, triggers, automations and operations it holds in the same schema change as its other sections, and SHALL refuse it with the problem text of the kernel when the kernel refuses a definition, and when an automation sends a template that neither the bundle nor the tenant declares, without installing any part of it.","rationale":"A bundle that is installed in part is not the product its owner reviewed (INT-154).","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"INT-2344","area":"04-automation","section":"Product bundles: install, upgrade and remove","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-product-lifecycle","boundaryDetail":"`product change`","traces":["g-167","g-103","d-6580","d-7341"],"milestone":7,"inSection":"sec-product-bundles","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"int-2345","kind":"requirement","statement":"An upgrade of a product SHALL create, change and remove the entities that differ between the installed version and the new one, found from the ownership record, in one schema change, and a removal of a product SHALL remove exactly the entities its record owns and no other.","rationale":"An upgrade that cannot find what a product owns would leave what the new version dropped, and a removal that guesses would take what a tenant made itself (D-6582).","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"INT-2345","area":"04-automation","section":"Product bundles: install, upgrade and remove","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-product-lifecycle","boundaryDetail":"`product change`","traces":["g-167","g-103","d-6582","d-7342"],"milestone":7,"inSection":"sec-product-bundles","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"int-2346","kind":"requirement","statement":"The routes install-bundle, upgrade-bundle, remove-bundle and list-installed-products SHALL be served: an owner changes, with a session that has authenticated recently, a dry run SHALL return the projection and change nothing, a request with an idempotency key SHALL change the tenant once, and a person who may manage the schema lists what is installed.","rationale":"An owner who installs a product at run time must see what it does before it does it, and a retry after a lost reply must not do it twice (INT-154, D-6595).","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"INT-2346","area":"04-automation","section":"Product bundles: install, upgrade and remove","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-product-lifecycle","boundaryDetail":"`product change`","traces":["g-167","g-103","d-6581","d-6595"],"milestone":7,"inSection":"sec-product-bundles","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"int-2347","kind":"requirement","statement":"The header of a product file SHALL take a version of three whole numbers and a platform range with a first release and optionally a later first release it does not support, specc and Exegra SHALL refuse a malformed one with layer.header-invalid, and a product file SHALL declare queries, views and workflows as values of query-def, view-def and workflow-def.","rationale":"A bundle needs the version and the platform range of its product, and a product that presents data or states the states of a field needs a place for them (D-6920, D-7343).","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"INT-2347","area":"04-automation","section":"Product bundles: install, upgrade and remove","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-product-lifecycle","boundaryDetail":"`product change`","traces":["g-20","d-6920","d-7343"],"milestone":7,"inSection":"sec-product-bundles","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"krn-2520","kind":"requirement","statement":"A named query whose filter has at its top level a condition field == value or field in list, on a field that is not a list and has no read condition, and that orders by nothing, by the record id ascending or by that field, or whose filter has at its top level a condition <, <=, > or >= on an integer or time field and that orders by that field, SHALL be served from the index of that field, and each page of candidates a read of it loads SHALL hold at most 200 records, whatever the number of records of the type.","rationale":"Lists of a person's threads, of an author's posts or of unread notices are equalities and ranges on one field; served from that field's index, their cost does not grow with the table.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"KRN-2520","area":"01-core","section":"Limits and paging","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`strata_kernel::read`","traces":["g-4"],"milestone":1,"inSection":"sec-kernel-1280","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"krn-2521","kind":"requirement","statement":"A read of a query served from an index SHALL examine at most 1600 candidates, SHALL return fewer rows than its page size only when its candidates ended or it examined 1600, and SHALL return a cursor that holds an index position (the value of the field and the record id), never a count, so that the next read continues exactly after the last candidate it examined whatever records were inserted or deleted in between.","rationale":"A reader who may see few records gets a short page rather than an unbounded read, and a cursor that names a position neither skips nor repeats a record when the table changes between pages.","evaluate":{"method":"property"},"ref":"KRN-2521","area":"01-core","section":"Limits and paging","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`strata_kernel::read`","traces":["g-4"],"milestone":1,"inSection":"sec-kernel-1280","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"krn-2522","kind":"requirement","statement":"The filter and the order of a named query SHALL be evaluated on each record as the reader receives it, without the fields the reader may not read; no query SHALL be served from the index of a field that has a read condition; and the cursor of a query served from the index of the field it orders by SHALL hold only the position of a record the reader may read.","rationale":"A hidden field that took part in which rows come back, in their order or in where a page ends would be read through the query.","evaluate":{"method":"property"},"ref":"KRN-2522","area":"01-core","section":"Limits and paging","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`strata_kernel::read`","traces":["g-4"],"milestone":1,"inSection":"sec-kernel-1280","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"krn-2523","kind":"requirement","statement":"For every reader, the rows of a read of a query served from an index, paged to the end, SHALL be the rows a scan of the same query returns, in the same order.","rationale":"An index plan is a way of reading, not a different answer.","evaluate":{"method":"property"},"ref":"KRN-2523","area":"01-core","section":"Limits and paging","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`strata_kernel::read`","traces":["g-4"],"milestone":1,"inSection":"sec-kernel-1280","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"krn-2524","kind":"requirement","statement":"A schema change that defines a named query served by a scan, or that turns a query served from an index into a scan, SHALL list in its evidence a passed check query-plan:<query> that says the query is a scan, that it is refused above 10000 records, and why it is not served from an index.","rationale":"A tenant learns at definition time which of its queries will stop working as its table grows, and what to change.","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"KRN-2524","area":"01-core","section":"Limits and paging","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`strata_kernel::read`","traces":["g-4"],"milestone":1,"inSection":"sec-kernel-1280","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"krn-2525","kind":"requirement","statement":"A store SHALL answer an index page of one value from one indexed lookup of the value's key in record id order, and an index page of a range of integers or of times from at most two indexed ranges of the order key, in the order of the value and then the record id; the record index SHALL hold no key for a value whose canonical JSON is longer than 240 bytes, and a probe for such a value SHALL be served by a scan.","rationale":"The order key is the number of an integer or a time, so a range is one index range; strings compare by their bytes and are equality-only, because a string longer than the key limit has no key.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"KRN-2525","area":"01-core","section":"Limits and paging","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`strata_kernel::read`","traces":["g-4"],"milestone":1,"inSection":"sec-kernel-1280","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"krn-2526","kind":"requirement","statement":"A view SHALL load, for each section, only the pages of candidates or the window its query reads and the records the section includes, and not every record of the object types it depends on, unless its reads still ask for more state after 32 rounds of loading.","rationale":"A view over a large type costs what its sections show.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"KRN-2526","area":"01-core","section":"Limits and paging","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`strata_kernel::read`","traces":["g-4"],"milestone":1,"inSection":"sec-kernel-1280","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"krn-2920","kind":"requirement","statement":"A named query whose filter has at its top level a condition field == value or field in list, on a field that is not a list and has no read condition, and that orders by one other attribute (an integer or time field that has no read condition, $created_at or $updated_at), ascending or descending, and that the index of the attribute does not serve (KRN-2520), SHALL be served from the pair index of the field and the attribute; each page of candidates a read of it loads SHALL hold at most 200 records, whatever the number of records of the type; and its rows, paged to the end, SHALL be the rows a scan of the same query returns, in the same order, a record whose value of the attribute is missing or null taking part in the order as the least value.","rationale":"Posts by this author newest first, unread notices for a person newest first and the redemptions of a promotion by time are equalities ordered by another attribute; served from a pair index, their cost does not grow with the table.","evaluate":{"method":"property"},"ref":"KRN-2920","area":"01-core","section":"Limits and paging","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`strata_kernel::read`","traces":["g-4"],"milestone":1,"inSection":"sec-kernel-1280","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"krn-2921","kind":"requirement","statement":"A store SHALL keep a pair index for exactly the pairs of a field and an attribute that the plans of the defined named queries of the tenant read: it SHALL build the index of a pair from the records of the type in the commit of the schema change that first defines a query that reads it, SHALL remove it in the commit of the schema change after which no query reads it, and SHALL update it in the commit of every record that is created, updated or deleted; it SHALL answer a pair page exactly as strata_kernel::query_plan::pair_page defines it; and while a record of the type holds a value of the attribute that is neither null, an integer nor a time, it SHALL answer the pages of that pair from the records of the type.","rationale":"An index kept only for the pairs tenants query costs writes in proportion to what is queried, and a record the index cannot order is still found.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"KRN-2921","area":"01-core","section":"Limits and paging","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`strata_kernel::read`","traces":["g-4"],"milestone":1,"inSection":"sec-kernel-1280","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"krn-2922","kind":"requirement","statement":"When a read finds that its snapshot lacks a record that a row refers to through a reference that the query filter, a read policy of the reader or a field read condition follows, the shell SHALL load, in the next round, each such record of every row the read examined and the page of candidates the read stopped at, and SHALL load each record by itself and not the whole object type it belongs to; the number of rounds of such a read SHALL be at most two more than the number of pages of candidates it examines, whatever its page size.","rationale":"A read policy that follows a reference into a large type costs the records the page refers to, not the type.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"KRN-2922","area":"01-core","section":"Limits and paging","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`strata_kernel::read`","traces":["g-4"],"milestone":1,"inSection":"sec-kernel-1280","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"krn-2923","kind":"requirement","statement":"The query-plan warning of a schema change that leaves a named query served by a scan (KRN-2524) SHALL name one change that would let an index serve the query (ordering by its first order key alone, ordering by the record id ascending, ordering by $created_at, or removing the read condition of one field) and the index that would then serve it, or, when no such single change exists, SHALL say so and name the pair index that the filter and the order of the query point at and why it is not derived.","rationale":"A tenant learns at definition time not only that a query will stop working as its table grows but what to change so that it does not.","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"KRN-2923","area":"01-core","section":"Limits and paging","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`strata_kernel::read`","traces":["g-4"],"milestone":1,"inSection":"sec-kernel-1280","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"srh-2780","kind":"requirement","statement":"A record type SHALL declare the fields its search index holds, and a field it does not declare SHALL NOT be indexed.","rationale":"An index of every field would hold what the type never meant to be found.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"SRH-2780","area":"07-content","section":"Declaration","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-151","boundaryDetail":"`search query`","traces":["g-161","d-7780"],"milestone":11,"inSection":"sec-search-2","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"srh-2781","kind":"requirement","statement":"A declaration of searchable fields SHALL be refused when it names a field the type lacks, a field whose type is not text, a personal field whose declaration is not searchable, a field twice, or more than 20 fields.","rationale":"A personal field is found only where its declaration allows it (D-6585), and text alone has words.","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"SRH-2781","area":"07-content","section":"Declaration","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-151","boundaryDetail":"`searchable declaration`","traces":["g-161","d-6585","d-7780"],"milestone":11,"inSection":"sec-search-2","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"srh-2782","kind":"requirement","statement":"The search index SHALL hold the tokens of each searchable field of each record of a tenant, written in the commit that writes the record and removed in the commit that deletes the record or rewrites the field.","rationale":"A deleted record is not found and an edited one is found by its new words (SRH-152).","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"SRH-2782","area":"07-content","section":"Index","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-151","boundaryDetail":"`search entry`","traces":["g-161","g-22","d-7781"],"milestone":11,"inSection":"sec-search-2","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"srh-2783","kind":"requirement","statement":"A text SHALL become tokens by splitting it at every run of characters that are not alphanumeric, lowercasing each word with the Unicode lowercase mapping, cutting each to 64 characters, keeping a repeated token once and keeping at most 1000 tokens of a field, and the memory store and the SQLite adapter SHALL use the same definition.","rationale":"Two stores that disagree about what a word is give two answers to one search.","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"SRH-2783","area":"07-content","section":"Index","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-151","boundaryDetail":"`search entry`","traces":["g-161","d-7780"],"milestone":11,"inSection":"sec-search-2","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"srh-2784","kind":"requirement","statement":"A search SHALL match a field when every word of the query is the start of a token of the field, and SHALL return a record when at least one field matches; the words of a query SHALL NOT combine across fields.","rationale":"A record found on the words of two fields would be found because of a field the reader may not read.","evaluate":{"method":"property"},"ref":"SRH-2784","area":"07-content","section":"Queries","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-151","boundaryDetail":"`search query`","traces":["g-161","g-20","d-7780"],"milestone":11,"inSection":"sec-search-2","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"srh-2785","kind":"requirement","statement":"A search SHALL return a record only when at least one field that matched is a field the reader may read, SHALL return the readable fields that matched and no others, and SHALL return the record without the fields the reader may not read; a word that only a field the reader may not read holds SHALL NOT produce a hit for that reader and SHALL for a reader who may read it.","rationale":"A hit on a hidden field lets a reader confirm its content by trying words (D-6586).","evaluate":{"method":"property"},"ref":"SRH-2785","area":"07-content","section":"Field-level read","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-151","boundaryDetail":"`search query`","traces":["g-161","g-20","d-6586","d-7781"],"milestone":11,"inSection":"sec-search-2","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"srh-2786","kind":"requirement","statement":"A search SHALL return its hits in ascending order of object type and record id, and a request that carries the cursor of an earlier page SHALL resume after the last candidate that page examined, so that no record appears twice and none is skipped whatever was inserted or deleted between the pages.","rationale":"A reader who pages through results sees each result once.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"SRH-2786","area":"07-content","section":"Queries","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-151","boundaryDetail":"`search query`","traces":["g-161","d-7781"],"milestone":11,"inSection":"sec-search-2","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"srh-2787","kind":"requirement","statement":"A search SHALL examine at most 1000 candidates, whatever the reader may read of them, and when it has examined them before its page is full SHALL return the hits found with a cursor that resumes after the last candidate examined.","rationale":"The work of a search is bounded as the work of a read is (KRN-1286).","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"SRH-2787","area":"07-content","section":"Queries","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-151","boundaryDetail":"`search query`","traces":["g-161","d-7781"],"milestone":11,"inSection":"sec-search-2","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"srh-2788","kind":"requirement","statement":"A search SHALL be refused when its query has no word, more than 8 different words or more than 200 bytes, when its page size is not from 1 to 200, and when it names an object type that does not exist.","rationale":"The size of a query is bounded as the work it causes is.","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"SRH-2788","area":"07-content","section":"Queries","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-151","boundaryDetail":"`search query`","traces":["g-161","d-7780","d-7781"],"milestone":11,"inSection":"sec-search-2","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"srh-2789","kind":"requirement","statement":"A search SHALL read the search entries of the tenant of the request only, and SHALL return no record of another tenant.","rationale":"There is no search across tenants (NG-10).","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"SRH-2789","area":"07-content","section":"Queries","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-151","boundaryDetail":"`search query`","traces":["g-161","ng-10"],"milestone":11,"inSection":"sec-search-2","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"srh-2790","kind":"requirement","statement":"The route that serves a search SHALL be counted against the per-source request rate of the gateway, and a request over it SHALL be refused with a Retry-After value in seconds (CMS-168).","rationale":"A search is open to anyone and costs a read of the tenant, so one source may not use it without limit.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"SRH-2790","area":"07-content","section":"Queries","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-151","boundaryDetail":"`search query`","traces":["g-161","d-7781"],"milestone":11,"inSection":"sec-search-2","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"srh-2791","kind":"requirement","statement":"A search index rebuilt from the records and the schema of the tenant alone SHALL answer every search as the index it replaces, and a commit that changes which fields of a type are searchable SHALL rebuild the entries of that type in its own transaction.","rationale":"The index is derived, so it can always be made again.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"SRH-2791","area":"07-content","section":"Index","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-151","boundaryDetail":"`search entry`","traces":["g-161","d-7781"],"milestone":11,"inSection":"sec-search-2","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"ldg-2880","kind":"requirement","statement":"A ranked listing of the accounts of a unit read under a policy over the ledger SHALL count and show only the accounts the reader may read, and the scan bound SHALL count the accounts examined.","rationale":"A rank discloses neither the position nor the existence of an account the reader may not read.","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"LDG-2880","area":"10-product","section":"Ledger reach","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-9","boundaryDetail":"`list-ledger-accounts`","traces":["g-604","d-7880","d-6552"],"milestone":11,"inSection":"sec-composition-5","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"ldg-2881","kind":"requirement","statement":"A read of the balance or of the entries of an account that the policies of the reader do not permit SHALL answer as an account that does not exist.","rationale":"No account and an account the reader may not read are not told apart (CT-282).","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"LDG-2881","area":"10-product","section":"Ledger reach","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`read-ledger-balance`","traces":["g-604","d-7880"],"milestone":11,"inSection":"sec-composition-5","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"ldg-2882","kind":"requirement","statement":"The limit of one account SHALL be kept in the ledger and loaded by its own need with the posting that applies it, and no read of the tenant schema SHALL carry it.","rationale":"Ten thousand limits do not load with every schema (D-6554).","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"LDG-2882","area":"10-product","section":"Ledger reach","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`decide-ledger-posting`","traces":["g-608","d-7881","k-100"],"milestone":11,"inSection":"sec-composition-5","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"ldg-2883","kind":"requirement","statement":"An account SHALL keep at most thirty-six buckets of credit, and a credit that would open another SHALL be merged so that the oldest credit lives longer and not shorter.","rationale":"The header stays small and the holder is not worse off.","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"LDG-2883","area":"10-product","section":"Ledger reach","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`decide-ledger-posting`","traces":["g-601","d-7882"],"milestone":11,"inSection":"sec-composition-5","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"ldg-2884","kind":"requirement","statement":"The expiry of credits SHALL be carried by one job per tenant that creates the next job in the transaction that reports it, and SHALL find the accounts with credit due through an index of their oldest bucket.","rationale":"Expiry depends on no schedule and no scan.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"LDG-2884","area":"10-product","section":"Ledger reach","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-7","boundaryDetail":"`expire-ledger-credits`","traces":["g-601","d-7883"],"milestone":11,"inSection":"sec-composition-5","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"ldg-2885","kind":"requirement","statement":"An entry whose key begins with expiry: SHALL be written only by the expiry of credits, and a posting that uses such a key SHALL be refused.","rationale":"An expiry entry never collides with a key a poster chose.","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"LDG-2885","area":"10-product","section":"Ledger reach","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`decide-ledger-posting`","traces":["g-601","d-7882"],"milestone":11,"inSection":"sec-composition-5","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"ldg-2886","kind":"requirement","statement":"Verifying a balance SHALL replay the journal of the account and report whether the stored balance equals the sum, the stored and the replayed amounts and the first number missing from the journal.","rationale":"A tampered header and a lost entry are found (LDG-019, LDG-020).","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"LDG-2886","area":"10-product","section":"Ledger reach","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`verify-ledger-balance`","traces":["g-608","d-5003"],"milestone":11,"inSection":"sec-composition-5","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"ldg-2887","kind":"requirement","statement":"A socket notice of an entry posted to an account SHALL be sent only to a subscriber whom the read decision of the kernel lets read the account, and SHALL name the account, the unit, the scope and the number of the entry and never the owner.","rationale":"A subscriber hears of what it may read and learns no person from it (SCH-1575).","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"LDG-2887","area":"10-product","section":"Ledger reach","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`ledger-entry-posted`","traces":["g-604","d-7884","d-5008"],"milestone":11,"inSection":"sec-composition-5","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"agg-2860","kind":"requirement","statement":"The audience class of a principal for a result SHALL be the set of the principal's roles that the Read policies, the field read rules and the filter of the result name, when no condition that applies to the principal mentions the principal or the clock, and SHALL be the principal alone when one does or when the kernel cannot resolve what the result reads.","rationale":"Two principals share a class only when nothing the kernel decides about the result can tell them apart, and any doubt makes a principal individual (CPY-005, AGG-033).","evaluate":{"method":"property"},"ref":"AGG-2860","area":"07-content","section":"Aggregate copies","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`audience class`","traces":["g-618","d-15","d-5065","d-7860"],"milestone":6,"inSection":"sec-content-256","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"agg-2861","kind":"requirement","statement":"A result for an audience class that is one principal alone SHALL NOT be stored.","rationale":"A leaderboard that holds a principal, or an answer that depends on who asks, is no copy for another reader (K-7, AGG-034).","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"AGG-2861","area":"07-content","section":"Aggregate copies","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`audience class`","traces":["g-618","k-7","d-5065"],"milestone":6,"inSection":"sec-content-256","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"agg-2862","kind":"requirement","statement":"A commit that writes or deletes a record of an object type SHALL raise the change counter of that type, and a stored aggregate result SHALL be served only while the counters of the object types it depends on are those it was stored under.","rationale":"The counter is the version of a copy, so a copy made before a commit is never found after it (AGG-031).","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"AGG-2862","area":"07-content","section":"Aggregate copies","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`audience class`","traces":["g-618","d-14","d-5064","d-7860"],"milestone":6,"inSection":"sec-content-256","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"bil-2800","kind":"requirement","statement":"A call of a served contract beyond a quota of the specification on that contract SHALL be refused with the error throttled, naming the quota and carrying the number of seconds after which the next call is permitted, and the call SHALL be counted again from the start of the next window.","rationale":"A refused caller learns which limit it met and when to come back, and a limit that never reopens would be an outage.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"BIL-2800","area":"09-operations","section":"Admission and deadlines","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-9","boundaryDetail":"`429`","traces":["g-301","k-300","d-7800"],"milestone":6,"inSection":"sec-operations-3","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"bil-2801","kind":"requirement","statement":"A tenant at its stored-bytes allowance SHALL have a write that adds data refused with the quota named, and SHALL still be served every read and every deletion.","rationale":"A tenant over its allowance must be able to get under it.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"BIL-2801","area":"02-tenancy","section":"Plans and quotas","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-11","boundaryDetail":"`operation`","traces":["g-157","g-4","d-7801"],"milestone":6,"inSection":"sec-billing-2","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"bil-2802","kind":"requirement","statement":"An owner of a tenant SHALL be able to read the plan of the tenant and, for each quantity the plan bounds, what the tenant has used and what it may.","rationale":"A limit that cannot be seen is met by surprise.","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"BIL-2802","area":"02-tenancy","section":"Plans and quotas","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-3","boundaryDetail":"`tenant plan`","traces":["g-157","d-7801"],"milestone":6,"inSection":"sec-billing-2","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"sch-2700","kind":"requirement","statement":"Each visit of a step in a run SHALL carry an idempotency key derived from the tenant, the automation, the run, the step name, the member of a fan-out and the position of the step in the run, so that a run that goes back to a step applies the effect of each visit once and every attempt of one visit applies it once.","rationale":"A loop through a branch repeats a step: one key for every visit would answer the second visit with the first result, and a key for every attempt would apply a retry twice.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"SCH-2700","area":"04-automation","section":"Retries and effects","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-7","boundaryDetail":"`automation run`","traces":["g-14","d-7700","d-6528"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-automation-4","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"sch-2701","kind":"requirement","statement":"The idempotency entry of the record change of an automation step SHALL be kept for at least the longest the step can retry and the retention of its run record, so that an attempt made after a lost report is answered with the first result however late it is made.","rationale":"A step may retry over days, and a dead-lettered step released later keeps its key: an entry that is gone after a day applies the change twice.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"SCH-2701","area":"04-automation","section":"Retries and effects","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-7","boundaryDetail":"`automation run`","traces":["g-14","d-7701","d-6528"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-automation-4","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"sch-2702","kind":"requirement","statement":"The run record of an accepted invocation of a tenant operation SHALL be kept for seven days from the invocation under the invoker and the operation, so that the same key by the same person for another operation is another key, and a repeat after six days answers the recorded result.","rationale":"The seven days of D-6548 are a retention of the record, and a key belongs to an operation.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"SCH-2702","area":"04-automation","section":"Retries and effects","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-7","boundaryDetail":"`automation run`","traces":["g-603","d-7701","d-6548"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-automation-4","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"sch-2703","kind":"requirement","statement":"The automation worker SHALL remove an ended job thirty days after its outcome, an ended run and its steps ninety days after the run ended, and a declined or held exception record ninety days after it was written; a parked or dead-lettered exception record SHALL be removed only after the tenant owner has settled it and ninety days have passed; and nothing that has not ended SHALL be removed.","rationale":"Work that finished is kept long enough to be looked at and no longer (PRV-357); unfinished work and unsettled exceptions are the tenant owner's to see (OPS-348).","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"SCH-2703","area":"04-automation","section":"Retries and effects","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-7","boundaryDetail":"`automation run`","traces":["g-14","d-7703","d-6530"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-automation-4","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"sch-2704","kind":"requirement","statement":"A job of a paused schedule that falls due SHALL complete without emitting the event of the schedule and SHALL create no next job.","rationale":"Pausing a schedule is the safe way to stop its automation while looking at it, including the job that is already open (SCH-005).","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"SCH-2704","area":"04-automation","section":"Retries and effects","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-7","boundaryDetail":"`automation run`","traces":["g-14","d-7702","d-6531"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-automation-4","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"sch-2705","kind":"requirement","statement":"A start job whose trigger has an earlier event with the same run key whose start job has not ended SHALL be deferred without counting an attempt, and SHALL start its run or write its declined record after the earlier one has ended.","rationale":"The order of the events of a key is the order of the runs, and waiting must not dead-letter the job that waits (SCH-1534).","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"SCH-2705","area":"04-automation","section":"Retries and effects","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-7","boundaryDetail":"`automation run`","traces":["g-14","d-7704","d-6532"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-automation-4","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"sch-2706","kind":"requirement","statement":"A tenant SHALL be able to schedule only a job of the kind start-run through schedule-job, naming one of its automations, with its idempotency key making the job once, and a job of any other kind SHALL be refused with the error invalid.","rationale":"The kinds of a job are the worker's, not free text (D-6520).","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"SCH-2706","area":"04-automation","section":"Retries and effects","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-7","boundaryDetail":"`automation run`","traces":["g-14","d-7706","d-6520"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-automation-4","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"wfl-2680","kind":"requirement","statement":"A run that reaches a request-approval step SHALL stop in the state awaiting-approval with no lease, recording the roles its policy names, its deadline and the person whose action started the run, and SHALL continue only by the decision of a principal who holds workflow-approve and a role that policy names, down the approved step or the refused step that the decision selects, with the comment of the decision recorded.","rationale":"People stay in the loop where the tenant puts them, and a review is an approval step with a named approver, so it can be audited (WFL-006, CMS-156).","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"WFL-2680","area":"04-automation","section":"Definition and activation","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-8","boundaryDetail":"`approval step`","traces":["g-26","d-7680"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-workflows-2","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"wfl-2681","kind":"requirement","statement":"A principal SHALL NOT decide an approval of a run that its own action started, whether it started the run directly or caused the event that a trigger matched; the decision SHALL be refused as forbidden and the run SHALL keep waiting.","rationale":"A person who approves their own work is no check at all, so separation of duties is a rule of the approval (AGS-409).","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"WFL-2681","area":"04-automation","section":"Definition and activation","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-8","boundaryDetail":"`approval step`","traces":["g-26","d-7680"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-workflows-2","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"wfl-2682","kind":"requirement","statement":"An approval that has no decision when its deadline passes SHALL take the refused step of its request-approval step with the decision recorded as timed out, and a decision made after the deadline SHALL be refused as a conflict.","rationale":"A run that waits for a person who never answers ends visibly instead of waiting for ever (D-6535).","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"WFL-2682","area":"04-automation","section":"Definition and activation","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-8","boundaryDetail":"`approval step`","traces":["g-26","d-7680"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-workflows-2","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"wfl-2683","kind":"requirement","statement":"An approval SHALL be decided once: a second decision on the same step SHALL be refused as a conflict and SHALL change neither the step nor the run.","rationale":"Two people deciding the same approval would send one run down two branches.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"WFL-2683","area":"04-automation","section":"Definition and activation","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-8","boundaryDetail":"`approval step`","traces":["g-26","d-7680"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-workflows-2","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"wfl-2684","kind":"requirement","statement":"An automation SHALL start runs only while it is active: a trigger that names a draft SHALL decline with the reason automation-inactive and a direct start of a draft SHALL be refused, and activating SHALL be refused to a principal who is not the tenant's owner holding workflow-activate, when no projection accompanies the request, and when the run-as of the automation names a role the activating principal may not confer.","rationale":"An automation is tried on history before it runs on the present (WFL-002) and never holds more than the person who activated it (WFL-1528).","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"WFL-2684","area":"04-automation","section":"Definition and activation","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-8","boundaryDetail":"`automation definition`","traces":["g-16","g-25","d-7681"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-workflows-2","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"wfl-2685","kind":"requirement","statement":"An automation SHALL be refused when it has an invoke-operation step whose operation does not exist, whose invokers name neither a role of the run-as of the automation nor every signed-in person, or whose inputs name something the operation does not declare, omit a required input or have a shape other than the type of the input, and the step SHALL invoke the operation as the automation principal with its step key as the idempotency key, so that any number of attempts invokes it once.","rationale":"An automation reaches the tenant's own declared operations with the authority of its run-as and no more (D-6547), and a retry must not apply an operation twice (SCH-1524).","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"WFL-2685","area":"04-automation","section":"The step catalogue","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-8","boundaryDetail":"`invoke-operation step`","traces":["g-31","d-7682"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-automation-3","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"wfl-2686","kind":"requirement","statement":"When a step fails for good, the steps of the run that completed and declare a compensating step SHALL be undone by running those compensating steps one at a time from the last completed step to the first, each under a key derived from the run, the compensating step and the step it undoes so that a retry compensates once, and the run SHALL end failed when every compensation is done, and SHALL stay compensating with a dead-lettered exception record that an owner can release to retry when a compensation fails for good.","rationale":"A workflow that cannot finish undoes what it can, and what it cannot undo stays visible to the owner (WFL-005, SCH-1525).","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"WFL-2686","area":"04-automation","section":"Retries and effects","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-8","boundaryDetail":"`compensation`","traces":["g-14","d-7683"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-automation-4","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"wfl-2687","kind":"requirement","statement":"A person who holds jobs-run SHALL be able to start a run of an active automation directly with inputs that are names an automation reads, and starting with the same key and the same inputs SHALL name the same run and start nothing more, while the same key with other inputs SHALL be refused.","rationale":"A person can run an automation on demand without a trigger, as safely as a trigger starts one (D-6523).","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"WFL-2687","area":"04-automation","section":"Runs and exceptions","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-8","boundaryDetail":"`automation run`","traces":["g-13","d-7684"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-automation-6","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"int-2640","kind":"requirement","statement":"A webhook delivery, outbound and inbound, SHALL carry the headers Strata-Event-Id, Strata-Timestamp in whole seconds since 1970 and Strata-Signature, whose entry v1= SHALL be the lower-case hexadecimal HMAC-SHA256, keyed with the bytes of the secret text, of the event identifier, a full stop, the timestamp, a full stop and the raw body; during the overlap after a rotation an outbound delivery SHALL carry one v1 entry for each secret that verifies, separated by spaces.","rationale":"A receiver checks the sender with one stated computation, and the identifier that deduplication keys on cannot be changed on a replay (WFL-010, WFL-255, INT-1577).","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"INT-2640","area":"04-automation","section":"Inbound webhook endpoints","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-150","boundaryDetail":"`webhook signature`","traces":["g-156","g-46","d-7641"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-integrations-1560","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"wfl-2641","kind":"requirement","statement":"The outbound gate SHALL follow at most three redirects of one call, SHALL judge the address of each under the outbound rule after resolving it as it judges the first, and SHALL refuse the call at a fourth redirect or at a redirect whose address the rule does not allow.","rationale":"A chain of redirects is the redirect bypass made longer, and an unbounded chain holds a worker (WFL-251).","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"WFL-2641","area":"04-automation","section":"Outbound calls","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-252","boundaryDetail":"`redirect`","traces":["g-257","d-7640"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-workflows-250","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"wfl-2642","kind":"requirement","statement":"The connector policy of the outbound gate SHALL allow ten seconds to resolve and connect, thirty seconds for the whole call with its redirects, and one mebibyte of response, and an outbound webhook delivery SHALL read at most 64 kibibytes of its response and keep only its status.","rationale":"Numbers stated once are numbers the implementation and the tests agree on (WFL-253).","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"WFL-2642","area":"04-automation","section":"Outbound calls","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-252","boundaryDetail":"`connector policy`","traces":["g-257","g-14"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-workflows-250","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"wfl-2643","kind":"requirement","statement":"An outbound webhook delivery SHALL be attempted at most three times, the second attempt five seconds and the third ten seconds after the previous one failed; it SHALL count as delivered on a 2xx status and SHALL NOT be posted again once delivered; a 5xx, 408 or 429 status, a passed time bound and an address that did not answer SHALL be retried, any other status and a refused address SHALL end it at once, and the attempt that spends the three SHALL dead-letter it.","rationale":"A receiver that is down for a moment still gets the delivery, and one that refuses it is not sent the same delivery again (webhook-delivery-flow, INT-152).","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"WFL-2643","area":"04-automation","section":"Outbound deliveries and the catalogue","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-150","boundaryDetail":"`webhook log`","traces":["g-156","g-13"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-integrations-3","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"fed-2644","kind":"requirement","statement":"In a process started in development mode the outbound gate SHALL allow plain HTTP, any port and any address and SHALL still connect only to the address it resolved; outside development the outbound rule SHALL apply to every address a tenant names, the addresses of identity providers included, without exception.","rationale":"A provider on the developer's own machine can be used in development, and no configuration opens the platform's network in production (FED-261, D-702).","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"FED-2644","area":"03-identity","section":"Binding, provisioning and metadata","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-252","boundaryDetail":"`provider metadata`","traces":["g-257","k-252","d-702"],"milestone":4,"inSection":"sec-federation-252","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"wfl-2645","kind":"requirement","statement":"The outbound rule SHALL refuse the IPv4 blocks 0/8, 10/8, 100.64/10, 127/8, 169.254/16, 172.16/12, 192.0.0/24, 192.0.2/24, 192.88.99/24, 192.168/16, 198.18/15, 198.51.100/24, 203.0.113/24, 224/4 and 240/4, the cloud metadata addresses 169.254.169.254, 169.254.170.2, 100.100.100.200, 192.0.0.192, 168.63.129.16 and fd00:ec2::254, and every IPv6 address outside 2000::/3 or inside 2001::/23, 2001:db8::/32, 2002::/16 or 3fff::/20, judging an IPv4-mapped address and an address under the NAT64 prefix 64:ff9b::/96 as the IPv4 address it carries; a host name SHALL be refused when any address it resolves to is refused.","rationale":"The list is what is refused, so a review and a test can check it entry by entry (WFL-008, WFL-252).","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"WFL-2645","area":"04-automation","section":"The outbound rule","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-7","boundaryDetail":"`outbound rule`","traces":["g-257","d-6570"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-workflows-1560","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"cms-2900","kind":"requirement","statement":"A write that creates or updates a record SHALL be refused with not-found, before it is committed, when a file field of the record newly holds the hash of a file that is not stored for the tenant, is not clean, or was neither uploaded by the acting principal nor readable by that principal through a record that refers to it, and the refusal SHALL be the same for each of those cases.","rationale":"File readability follows the records that refer to a file and a file id is the hash of its content, so a record that could name any hash would let its writer read another principal's unattached upload, and a refusal that differed by case would tell whether a content is stored.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"CMS-2900","area":"07-content","section":"File fields and uploads","lifecycle":"active","realisation":"checked","boundary":"b-9","boundaryDetail":"`file reference field`","traces":["g-33","g-20"],"milestone":7,"inSection":"sec-file-fields"},
    {"id":"prv-2740","kind":"requirement","statement":"The export of one principal SHALL be read in batches of at most 100 records through the declarations that the erasure of that principal reads, SHALL hold every personal field the erasure would clear, no field of another subject and no secret, and SHALL be one deterministic JSON document of the format strata-subject-export/1.","rationale":"An export that could disagree with the erasure about what belongs to a person would either hide data from the person or leave it behind after erasure.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"PRV-2740","area":"09-privacy","section":"Data subject rights","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-350","boundaryDetail":"`strata_kernel::subject_export`","traces":["g-350","k-352"],"milestone":6,"inSection":"sec-privacy-2","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"prv-2741","kind":"requirement","statement":"An export SHALL be delivered only to the principal it concerns or to an owner of the tenant, each after a step-up, SHALL expire seven days after the request, and the request and each fetch SHALL be an audit entry that names the tenant and the export and not the person.","rationale":"The document is the whole of a person's data, so its delivery needs the same care as the erasure.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"PRV-2741","area":"09-privacy","section":"Data subject rights","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-350","boundaryDetail":"`POST /api/subject-rights/export-fetch`","traces":["g-350","k-352"],"milestone":6,"inSection":"sec-privacy-2","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"prv-2742","kind":"requirement","statement":"A restriction placed on a principal SHALL remove the personal fields of that principal from every record a view returns and SHALL keep the records of that principal from the retention sweep until the restriction is lifted, SHALL not block the erasure or the export of that principal, and the erasure receipt SHALL name the restriction.","rationale":"The data stays and its use stops; the effects stated are the ones this tree enforces (D-7741).","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"PRV-2742","area":"09-privacy","section":"Data subject rights","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-350","boundaryDetail":"`POST /api/subject-rights/restrict`","traces":["g-350","k-352"],"milestone":6,"inSection":"sec-privacy-2","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"prv-2743","kind":"requirement","statement":"The erasure of a principal under a legal hold SHALL be refused with conflict naming the hold and SHALL change nothing; the erasure of any other principal SHALL leave unchanged each record of a record type under a hold and list it in the receipt; and the retention sweep SHALL delete no record of a held type or of a held principal until the hold is released.","rationale":"A hold is the tenant's instruction to keep data, and it overrides the schedule and the erasure (PRV-355).","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"PRV-2743","area":"09-privacy","section":"Retention and legal hold","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-350","boundaryDetail":"`POST /api/subject-rights/place-hold`","traces":["g-350","k-352"],"milestone":6,"inSection":"sec-privacy-3","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"prv-2744","kind":"requirement","statement":"A job of each tenant SHALL delete, in batches of at most 100 records and as the system retention principal through the kernel, each record whose retention has ended and that no other record refers to, with an event whose before image holds none of the personal fields of the record, and SHALL create the job of the next batch or of the next sweep in the report that ends it.","rationale":"Removal is scheduled work that survives failure and recurs without a separate schedule (PRV-357).","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"PRV-2744","area":"09-privacy","section":"Retention and legal hold","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-350","boundaryDetail":"`retention sweep`","traces":["g-350","k-352"],"milestone":6,"inSection":"sec-privacy-3","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"prv-2745","kind":"requirement","statement":"A schema SHALL refuse a personal field whose data subject is a field that does not hold text or a list of text, and the erasure of a principal SHALL revoke each pending invitation addressed to the verified address of that principal and clear its address, with the intent, the events and the output of the erasure carrying no address.","rationale":"A principal id is matched as text, and an address left in a pending invitation is personal data the erasure would otherwise leave.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"PRV-2745","area":"09-privacy","section":"Personal data of tenant record types","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-350","boundaryDetail":"`strata_kernel::erasure`","traces":["g-350","k-352"],"milestone":6,"inSection":"sec-tenant-personal-data","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"ctk-2900","kind":"requirement","statement":"The body of a mail template and of a notice template SHALL be a JSON list of template-block, and a template whose body is not, or whose node has a member that its type does not name, SHALL be refused at definition with the place of the fault in the body.","rationale":"The body is what a recipient reads and what the browser builds nodes from, so it has one shape, and a fault is found where it was written.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"CTK-2900","area":"07-content","section":"The blocks of a template","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-451","boundaryDetail":"`mail template`","traces":["d-7900","g-453"],"milestone":7,"inSection":"sec-template-blocks","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"ctk-2901","kind":"requirement","statement":"A template SHALL place a token with an inline node of type token that names it, a template that places a token the tenant does not define SHALL be refused at definition with the name of that token, and a token that a template places SHALL NOT be removed.","rationale":"A misspelt token is found by the author, not by a recipient, and a removal cannot leave a template that names nothing (CTK-004, CTK-005).","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"CTK-2901","area":"07-content","section":"The blocks of a template","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-450","boundaryDetail":"`token reference`","traces":["d-7900","g-450"],"milestone":7,"inSection":"sec-template-blocks","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"ctk-2902","kind":"requirement","statement":"A token expression SHALL read only the fields of a record and the parameters of an event, so that no token names another token and no token refers to itself.","rationale":"CTK-003 holds by construction: the tenant rule language has no way to name a token, so a token that does is refused as an expression that does not parse.","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"CTK-2902","area":"07-content","section":"The blocks of a template","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-450","boundaryDetail":"`token definition`","traces":["d-7900"],"milestone":7,"inSection":"sec-template-blocks","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"eml-2903","kind":"requirement","statement":"A template SHALL declare the type of each value it places, one of str, int, bool and time, where it places it, a name SHALL be placed with one type only, and a template SHALL NOT be rendered with a value missing or of another type.","rationale":"The sender of a message supplies the values, and a template that cannot say what it needs cannot be checked against the sender.","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"EML-2903","area":"04-automation","section":"The blocks of a template","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-451","boundaryDetail":"`template value`","traces":["d-7900","g-453"],"milestone":7,"inSection":"sec-template-blocks","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"cms-2904","kind":"requirement","statement":"A link in a template SHALL carry a web or mail address, a path of the site or a fragment and no space or control character, quotes SHALL nest at most as deep as the Markdown parser keeps them, inline elements SHALL nest at most as deep as it keeps them, and a body SHALL hold at most 5000 nodes.","rationale":"A template is rendered into mail and into the browser, so it is held to the bounds of the one parser that bounds its input (CMS-250, CMS-004).","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"CMS-2904","area":"07-content","section":"The blocks of a template","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-9","boundaryDetail":"`structured blocks`","traces":["d-7900","k-12"],"milestone":7,"inSection":"sec-template-blocks","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"eml-2905","kind":"requirement","statement":"Rendering a template body SHALL be a pure function of the body, the values and the text of each token for the reader, and SHALL give the blocks with each token and value replaced by a text node and the same blocks as plain text, equal for equal inputs.","rationale":"The mail dispatcher and the notice service render with one function, so a recipient reads the same words in the mail and the inbox (EML-016, NTF-1570, CTK-015).","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"EML-2905","area":"04-automation","section":"The blocks of a template","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-451","boundaryDetail":"`strata_kernel::blocks::render`","traces":["d-7900"],"milestone":7,"inSection":"sec-template-blocks","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"set-2900","kind":"requirement","statement":"A setting SHALL be definable with the id of a declared enum, id or scalar type that the kernel holds, a default and an override of it SHALL be refused unless they are text that decodes as that type, a type the kernel does not hold SHALL be refused with the types it holds, and a setting of f64 SHALL be refused because the value algebra holds no float.","rationale":"A setting of a few named values or of an id is typed like any other, and no stored value is ever of another type than its setting (SET-001, SET-004, SET-021).","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"SET-2900","area":"09-administration","section":"Declared types of a setting and settings in views","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-13","boundaryDetail":"`setting definition`","traces":["d-7901","d-5046","g-610"],"milestone":6,"inSection":"sec-setting-types-2900","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"set-2901","kind":"requirement","statement":"An argument of a view section SHALL be able to name a setting, a view that names a setting the tenant does not define SHALL be refused at definition, the argument SHALL take the value of the setting resolved for the reader, and a copy of the view SHALL depend on the platform and tenant revisions of the setting and, when the value comes from the override of a person, SHALL be of that person alone.","rationale":"A page that depends on a setting is declared, and a person's value never reaches another reader (SET-050 to SET-053, SET-1540).","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"SET-2901","area":"09-administration","section":"Declared types of a setting and settings in views","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`view section`","traces":["d-6557","d-5049"],"milestone":6,"inSection":"sec-setting-types-2900","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"int-2900","kind":"requirement","statement":"A schema change that alters or removes an entity that an installed product owns SHALL be refused, naming the entity and the product, unless the same change carries the record of that product at another version or its removal, a change that carries a product record SHALL need the capability bundle-install, and a record at the version already installed SHALL be refused.","rationale":"A product is upgraded or removed as a whole, so what it owns is not edited behind its back, and a schema editor cannot present an edit as an upgrade (INT-1582).","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"INT-2900","area":"04-automation","section":"Guarding what a product owns, and the reference product","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-product-lifecycle","boundaryDetail":"`product change`","traces":["d-7902","d-6582","g-167","g-103"],"milestone":7,"inSection":"sec-product-guard-2900","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"wfl-2901","kind":"requirement","statement":"A trigger on ledger-posted for a unit SHALL start its automation for each entry posted to an account of that unit, with the parameters owner, unit, amount, balance, balance_before, entry_sequence and reason, and with no record in the scopes of its condition.","rationale":"Crossing a threshold needs the balance before and after the entry, which the platform computes (D-6523).","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"WFL-2901","area":"04-automation","section":"Guarding what a product owns, and the reference product","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-7","boundaryDetail":"`trigger`","traces":["d-7903","d-6523","g-13"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-product-guard-2900","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"int-2902","kind":"requirement","statement":"The reference product badge-milestones SHALL install from its bundle into a tenant, award the Silver badge once to a person whose points cross 500 however often they cross, and record at the step that sends mail or a notice the failure that names the step kind when the platform has not built it.","rationale":"The reference product is the proof that a product is built from primitives alone, and its failures say what is missing (WG-5008).","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"INT-2902","area":"04-automation","section":"Guarding what a product owns, and the reference product","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-product-lifecycle","boundaryDetail":"`product module`","traces":["d-6582","g-167","g-103"],"milestone":7,"inSection":"sec-product-guard-2900","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"agt-2940","kind":"requirement","statement":"A change SHALL be applied from an Impact Lab projection only while the tenant is at the revision the projection was taken at, and a tenant at another revision SHALL be refused with a conflict that names its current revision and SHALL be left unchanged.","rationale":"A projection describes one state of the tenant; applying its change to another state would apply a change nobody was shown the effects of (D-7940).","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"AGT-2940","area":"06-agents","section":"Operations over the platform","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-20","boundaryDetail":"`apply-lab-change`","traces":["g-44","g-24","d-7940"],"milestone":7,"inSection":"sec-agents-403","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"cms-2960","kind":"requirement","statement":"The editor of a record type SHALL, before sending a draft, check it with the JavaScript module of the tenant rule language against what the server sent of the type for this reader (each readable field's type, required flag and size limits, the type's constraints as printed rule text, and the guards of the workflow transitions out of the record's current state), and SHALL refuse the draft in the kernel's own wording for every required field, size limit, constraint and workflow guard that the module evaluates to a refusal, without sending a request.","rationale":"A refusal the page can foresee should not cost a round trip; showing it in the kernel's words and rule names keeps the page and the server saying the same thing.","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"CMS-2960","area":"07-content","section":"Arithmetic and time in rules","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`tenant rule language`","traces":["g-20","d-7360"],"milestone":2,"inSection":"sec-composition-2","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"cms-2961","kind":"requirement","statement":"What the server sends the editor of a record type SHALL name no field the reader may not read, SHALL carry no read rule, and SHALL carry no constraint or workflow guard that follows a reference or reads such a field: the kernel's redaction decides which fields those are, and the kernel still enforces what is not sent. A rule the page cannot evaluate, and a verdict the server decides alone, SHALL be left to the server and never shown to the person as valid; the server's answer to a send SHALL always stand, and a send the page passed but the server refused SHALL be logged as a disagreement.","rationale":"Telling the page about a rule over a hidden field would disclose the field; leaving what the page cannot decide to the server keeps one authority.","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"CMS-2961","area":"07-content","section":"Arithmetic and time in rules","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-1","boundaryDetail":"`tenant rule language`","traces":["g-20","d-7360"],"milestone":2,"inSection":"sec-composition-2","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"prv-2720","kind":"requirement","statement":"The store SHALL seal every value of a field that declares personal data under the key of its data subject in the records, the record images of the events, the field values of create-record and update-record intents in the journal and the snapshots, and SHALL return it plain on every read while that key lives.","rationale":"Every copy the platform writes holds the sealed form, so destroying one key reaches all of them (D-7720).","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"PRV-2720","area":"09-privacy","section":"Sealing and audit","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-17","boundaryDetail":"`SealedStore`","traces":["d-7720","d-350","k-352"],"milestone":3,"inSection":"sec-privacy-4","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"prv-2721","kind":"requirement","statement":"A value whose subject key was destroyed SHALL be read as its sealed form, and a read, a query or a replay that meets it SHALL continue.","rationale":"The erased form is explicit and breaks nothing that reads around it (D-7728).","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"PRV-2721","area":"09-privacy","section":"Sealing and audit","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-17","boundaryDetail":"`sealed:v1:`","traces":["d-7728","d-350"],"milestone":3,"inSection":"sec-privacy-4","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"prv-2722","kind":"requirement","statement":"The delta hash and the events hash of a journal entry SHALL be computed over the sealed delta and events, and a replay SHALL reproduce them by sealing its decision again with the live keys.","rationale":"A destroyed key changes no recorded byte and the history still verifies (D-7721).","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"PRV-2722","area":"09-privacy","section":"Sealing and audit","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-2","boundaryDetail":"`journal`","traces":["d-7721","d-350"],"milestone":3,"inSection":"sec-privacy-4","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"prv-2723","kind":"requirement","statement":"The record index SHALL hold of a sealed personal field only the keyed blind hashes of a field declared searchable, and nothing of one that is not, and an exact-match lookup and a unique check of a searchable personal field SHALL be answered through the blind hash.","rationale":"Search and uniqueness keep working without the index holding the value (D-7723, D-6585).","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"PRV-2723","area":"09-privacy","section":"Sealing and audit","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-2","boundaryDetail":"`record_index`","traces":["d-7723","d-6585"],"milestone":3,"inSection":"sec-privacy-4","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"prv-2724","kind":"requirement","statement":"An erasure SHALL destroy every live key of the subject after it has cleared the records of the subject, and its receipt SHALL name the keys destroyed and the copies whose sealed values they reach.","rationale":"The destruction is what reaches the copies the erasure does not rewrite (D-7722).","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"PRV-2724","area":"09-privacy","section":"Sealing and audit","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-350","boundaryDetail":"`erase-subject`","traces":["d-7722","d-350"],"milestone":3,"inSection":"sec-privacy-4","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"prv-2725","kind":"requirement","statement":"The members of an audit line that name a person SHALL be sealed under the key of that person before the line is chained.","rationale":"The chain is over the sealed form, so the erasure of the person breaks no link (D-7725, PRV-360).","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"PRV-2725","area":"09-privacy","section":"Sealing and audit","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-12","boundaryDetail":"`audit entry`","traces":["d-7725","d-350"],"milestone":3,"inSection":"sec-privacy-4","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"prv-2726","kind":"requirement","statement":"The schema history of a tenant SHALL hold no team and no invitation.","rationale":"They name people and nothing reads them from the history (D-7726).","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"PRV-2726","area":"09-privacy","section":"Sealing and audit","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-2","boundaryDetail":"`schema_history`","traces":["d-7726"],"milestone":3,"inSection":"sec-privacy-4","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"prv-2727","kind":"requirement","statement":"A snapshot restored after an erasure SHALL return the sealed fields of the erased person in sealed form.","rationale":"A key destruction is not undone by a restore (D-7727, TEN-1212).","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"PRV-2727","area":"09-privacy","section":"Sealing and audit","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-3","boundaryDetail":"`tenant restore`","traces":["d-7727","d-6206"],"milestone":3,"inSection":"sec-privacy-4","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"sec-2728","kind":"requirement","statement":"A sealed value SHALL open only for the tenant, the key, the object type and the field it was sealed for.","rationale":"A value or a key copied into another tenant or another field opens nothing (D-7722, SEC-001).","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"SEC-2728","area":"08-platform","section":"Keys and credentials","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-17","boundaryDetail":"`data key`","traces":["d-7722","g-40"],"milestone":3,"inSection":"sec-platform-4","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"m-catalogue-refuses-without-capability","kind":"temporal","models":"agt-1209","statement":"An invocation through the catalogue by a caller that lacks a capability of the underlying contract is never applied.","evaluate":{"method":"never","scenarios":["author-invokes-delete-tenant","author-invokes-export-tenant","author-invokes-issue-access-grant"],"occurs":{"event":"ci-applied"},"negatives":[{"scenario":"author-invokes-delete-tenant","faults":["defect-catalogue-skips-contract-auth"]},{"scenario":"author-invokes-export-tenant","faults":["defect-catalogue-skips-contract-auth"]}]},"faultModel":"fault-model-launch","assumptions":["a-model-abstraction"],"faultBasis":"fault"},
    {"id":"run-3060","kind":"requirement","statement":"The platform diagnostics SHALL be served only to a caller that presents both the service credential and the operator credential (STRATA_OPERATOR_TOKEN, in the x-strata-operator header), and the operator credential SHALL NOT be the service credential; a caller that presents the service credential without the operator credential SHALL be refused as unauthenticated and the refusal SHALL be an audit entry, and each call that is served SHALL be an audit entry. A backend with no operator credential configured SHALL answer \"not found\", except in development, where the service credential stands for the operator. The integrity check of the tenant files SHALL be reachable only through the platform diagnostics, and liveness SHALL answer without opening any tenant file.","rationale":"The service credential is shared with the gateway, so it names no operator; the platform diagnostics read every tenant and the integrity check names failing tenants.","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"RUN-3060","area":"01-core","section":"Production safety of the backend","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-19","boundaryDetail":"`x-strata-operator`","traces":["g-11","g-30"],"milestone":2,"inSection":"sec-runtime-1380","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"run-3061","kind":"requirement","statement":"The journal of a tenant SHALL be kept for the life of the tenant and no process SHALL delete one of its entries, because the replay of the impact lab and the audit chain read it from its first entry; an entry SHALL hold the intent as it was stated with its personal fields sealed under the key of their subject (D-350) and SHALL NOT hold a verified mail address, and the events of a tenant SHALL be kept as long as its journal; erasing a subject SHALL destroy that subject's key and SHALL NOT rewrite the journal or the events.","rationale":"Retention of the history is a decision about what a replay can show; stating it keeps a purge from being added that would break every replay and every chain hash.","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"RUN-3061","area":"01-core","section":"Production safety of the backend","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-19","boundaryDetail":"`journal retention`","traces":["g-11","g-30"],"milestone":2,"inSection":"sec-runtime-1380","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"gwy-3062","kind":"requirement","statement":"The source address of a request SHALL be the address of the peer that opened the connection, except that when that peer is one of the addresses in STRATA_TRUSTED_PROXIES it SHALL be the rightmost address in X-Forwarded-For that is not itself a trusted proxy; the gateway SHALL discard any source header a browser sent and SHALL pass its own to the backend in x-strata-source; an IPv6 source address SHALL be counted as its /64 network and an IPv4 address as itself; and outside development a request that carries X-Forwarded-For while no proxy is trusted SHALL be refused naming forwarded_without_trusted_proxies.","rationale":"A quota by source address is only as good as the address: a header a visitor can write, or one address for every visitor behind an untrusted proxy, defeats it.","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"GWY-3062","area":"01-core","section":"Production configuration of the gateway","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-9","boundaryDetail":"`source address`","traces":["g-250"],"milestone":2,"inSection":"sec-runtime-1420","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"gwy-3063","kind":"requirement","statement":"Every served contract that is signed or session-authenticated and starts expensive work SHALL have a quota entry, and the impact lab run, the Lean verification run and the access-token endpoint SHALL each have one: the lab run and the verification run per principal, the token endpoint per source address.","rationale":"Authentication does not bound cost: one signed-in principal or one client secret can otherwise keep the backend busy for everyone.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"GWY-3063","area":"01-core","section":"Production configuration of the gateway","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-9","boundaryDetail":"`quota`","traces":["g-250"],"milestone":2,"inSection":"sec-runtime-1420","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"bil-3064","kind":"requirement","statement":"A write that creates a record SHALL be refused with the error kind QuotaExceeded naming the quota stored-records when the tenant already holds as many records as its stored-records allowance, which is 1,000,000 on the Standard plan, 10,000,000 on the Business plan and no limit on the Enterprise plan until a contract records one; a delete SHALL never be refused for want of room; the operator SHALL NOT set the allowance below the records the tenant holds; and a plan change SHALL be refused while the tenant holds more records than the new plan allows.","rationale":"Stored bytes alone do not bound the number of rows one tenant makes the store index, order and replay (D-508, D-8060).","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"BIL-3064","area":"02-tenancy","section":"Plans","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-3","boundaryDetail":"`stored-records`","traces":["g-157","d-508","d-8060"],"milestone":12,"realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"ntf-3100","kind":"requirement","statement":"The notification service SHALL keep one preference for each person, message category and channel, holding one of on, off and digest and, for digest, the period daily or weekly, and SHALL remove the preferences of a person when the person is erased.","rationale":"A person chooses how each kind of notice reaches them, and the choice ends with the person (NTF-1571).","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"NTF-3100","area":"04-automation","section":"Product notices, preferences and digests","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-154","boundaryDetail":"`notification preference`","traces":["g-155","d-6573","d-8100"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-notifications-1560","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"ntf-3101","kind":"requirement","statement":"A digest SHALL be made when its period has ended, at 09:00 in the zone of the person and on a Monday for a weekly digest; it SHALL list the live notices of its category created before the end of the period that no digest of its channel lists yet; and it SHALL be made once for each person, category, channel and period however often the job that makes it runs.","rationale":"Many small events become one message, and a job that runs twice sends it once (NTF-1572).","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"NTF-3101","area":"04-automation","section":"Product notices, preferences and digests","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-154","boundaryDetail":"`digest`","traces":["g-155","d-6573","d-8100"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-notifications-1560","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"ntf-3102","kind":"requirement","statement":"A digest on the inbox channel SHALL be one inbox item that lists the titles of its notices, pushed to the open pages of the person unless the person is muted or in quiet hours, and a period with no notice SHALL have no digest.","rationale":"The digest is read where the notices are, and an empty period says nothing.","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"NTF-3102","area":"04-automation","section":"Product notices, preferences and digests","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-154","boundaryDetail":"`digest`","traces":["g-155","d-6573","d-8100"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-notifications-1560","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"ntf-3103","kind":"requirement","statement":"An inbox item SHALL end when its recipient removes it, when the record it names is erased, or when its recipient is erased; an ended item SHALL keep its identifier and hold no title, text or value.","rationale":"The item states its own end (ret-inbox-item) and a repeated send does not bring it back (CT-183).","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"NTF-3103","area":"04-automation","section":"Product notices, preferences and digests","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-154","boundaryDetail":"`inbox`","traces":["g-155","d-6573","d-8100"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-notifications-1560","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"ntf-3104","kind":"requirement","statement":"A digest on the mail channel SHALL be one message of the mail template digest_mail_ followed by the category with its hyphens written as underscores, sent by the mail dispatcher under an idempotency key derived from the digest.","rationale":"A digest by mail is mail like any other and is sent once under retry (EML-006).","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"NTF-3104","area":"04-automation","section":"Product notices, preferences and digests","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-154","boundaryDetail":"`digest`","traces":["g-155","d-6573","d-8100"],"milestone":5,"inSection":"sec-notifications-1560","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"ntf-3200","kind":"requirement","statement":"The step send-mail SHALL name exactly one of to, address and segment and the step create-notice exactly one of to and segment, a definition that names none or several SHALL be refused with the error invalid, a segment target SHALL be sent in batches of at most one hundred persons keyed by the step key, and the step send-digest SHALL send one message to each person who holds notices of its category created in its window, listing them, and none to a person who holds none, keyed by the step key and the person so that a replayed step sends once.","rationale":"A workflow can reach a person, an address or a segment with one step each, and a retried run does not send twice (NTF-1572, EML-1560, EML-1561).","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"NTF-3200","area":"04-automation","lifecycle":"active","realisation":"checked","milestone":5,"section":"Product notices, preferences and digests","boundary":"b-154","boundaryDetail":"`send-digest`","traces":["g-155","d-8200"],"inSection":"sec-notifications-1560"},
    {"id":"sch-3202","kind":"requirement","statement":"The trigger catalogue SHALL hold the event declared-event, which names an event kind that a tenant declares, and a trigger on it SHALL bind param.kind beside seq, at and hop.","rationale":"A product reacts to its own events, not only to the platform's (SCH-1576).","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"SCH-3202","area":"04-automation","lifecycle":"active","realisation":"checked","milestone":5,"section":"Time and domain events","boundary":"b-7","boundaryDetail":"`selector`","traces":["g-13","d-8201"],"inSection":"sec-scheduling-1560"},
    {"id":"int-3203","kind":"requirement","statement":"A product file SHALL have a section eventKinds of values of event-kind-decl, specc SHALL refuse a kind that does not begin with app. and a name or that has more than 16 fields with layer.event-kind-invalid and SHALL write the section as the bundle section event-kinds, and the bundle reader SHALL read and check it and refuse to install a bundle that fills it until the kernel holds declared kinds.","rationale":"A product states the events it produces as data, with the same checks the tenant's own declaration has (SCH-1576, D-6700).","evaluate":{"method":"example"},"ref":"INT-3203","area":"04-automation","lifecycle":"active","realisation":"checked","milestone":5,"section":"Product bundles: install, upgrade and remove","boundary":"b-21","boundaryDetail":"`tenant bundle`","traces":["g-167","d-8202"],"inSection":"sec-product-bundles"},
    {"id":"ops-3120","kind":"requirement","statement":"A committed change of the roles of a person, of a team, of an invitation, of a setting or of the schema of a running tenant SHALL append an audit line that holds the previous value, the new value, the acting principal, the revision and the correlation identifier of the request, and a change that is refused SHALL append none.","rationale":"OPS-329 asks it of a configuration change; roles and permissions are configuration too, and a refused change changed nothing to explain (D-8120).","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"OPS-3120","area":"09-operations","section":"Releases and change","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-12","boundaryDetail":"`audit entry`","traces":["g-30"],"milestone":10,"inSection":"sec-operations-8","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"obs-3121","kind":"requirement","statement":"The route of verify-audit-chain SHALL answer a principal that holds the capability audit-read, SHALL refuse anyone else and a tenant other than the one of the request, and SHALL report a chain with an altered or a removed line as broken with the sequence number of the first line that no longer chains.","rationale":"A check that anyone may run reads the trail of every tenant; one that cannot find a changed line proves nothing (OBS-007, CT-128).","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"OBS-3121","area":"06-agents","section":"Audit","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-12","boundaryDetail":"`verify-audit-chain`","traces":["g-30"],"milestone":8,"inSection":"sec-observability-3","realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"prv-3122","kind":"requirement","statement":"The receipt of an erasure SHALL name each backup image the tenant holds with the time it was taken and the time it expires, and each export of the erased subject's data with its own expiry, and the erasure SHALL remove each such export before its expiry.","rationale":"A copy that outlives the erasure for a stated time is named with that time, one by one, so the person can see when each stops existing (PRV-353, D-351, D-7727).","evaluate":{"method":"scenario"},"ref":"PRV-3122","area":"09-privacy","section":"Data subject rights","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-350","boundaryDetail":"`POST /api/subject-rights/erase`","traces":["g-350","k-352"],"milestone":6,"inSection":"sec-privacy-2","realisation":"checked"}
  ],

  // ---- Glossary ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  "terms": [
    {"id":"term-tenant","term":"Tenant","definition":"an organisation's isolated installation: one database, one file namespace, one identity realm, one key."},
    {"id":"term-tenant-database","term":"Tenant database","definition":"the PostgreSQL database that holds everything a tenant owns: schema, records, events, journal, jobs, identity realm and audit log."},
    {"id":"term-control-plane","term":"Control plane","definition":"the component that owns the tenant directory and carries out tenant lifecycle operations."},
    {"id":"term-tenant-directory","term":"Tenant directory","definition":"the control plane's list of tenants with their state, placement and domain bindings."},
    {"id":"term-placement","term":"Placement","definition":"where a tenant's database and files are: cluster, region and database name."},
    {"id":"term-realm","term":"Realm","definition":"The set of principals, credentials and identity provider configurations of one tenant, or of the platform's operators."},
    {"id":"term-principal","term":"Principal","definition":"an identity that can act: a person, a service account or an agent."},
    {"id":"term-sign-in-session","term":"Sign-in session","definition":"the record that says a browser has authenticated as a principal, identified by a secret the browser holds."},
    {"id":"term-assertion","term":"Assertion","definition":"a short-lived statement signed by the identity service saying which principal and session a request belongs to."},
    {"id":"term-access-token","term":"Access token","definition":"a signed, expiring statement of scopes issued to a service account or an agent."},
    {"id":"term-delegation","term":"Delegation","definition":"an agent acting for a person, with a token that names both and grants no more than the person holds."},
    {"id":"term-emailed-link","term":"Emailed link","definition":"a single-use sign-in link sent to an address."},
    {"id":"term-step-up","term":"Step-up","definition":"a fresh authentication asked for before a sensitive operation."},
    {"id":"term-job","term":"Job","definition":"one unit of scheduled work with a due time, a state and a recorded outcome."},
    {"id":"term-schedule","term":"Schedule","definition":"a rule that creates jobs: once at a time, or repeatedly."},
    {"id":"term-trigger","term":"Trigger","definition":"a tenant definition (trigger-def) that starts a run of an automation when a committed domain event of its kind satisfies its condition, creating the run's first job in the transaction of the event."},
    {"id":"term-lease","term":"Lease","definition":"a worker's time-limited claim on a job."},
    {"id":"term-fencing-token","term":"Fencing token","definition":"a number that rises with every lease on a job and is checked when a result is recorded."},
    {"id":"term-idempotency-key","term":"Idempotency key","definition":"a value that lets the receiver of an effect recognise a repeat."},
    {"id":"term-wake-index","term":"Wake index","definition":"the control plane's list of tenants with their next due time."},
    {"id":"term-workflow","term":"Workflow","definition":"a state machine held as tenant metadata whose steps the kernel decides."},
    {"id":"term-connector","term":"Connector","definition":"an adapter that carries out one kind of external effect, such as an HTTP call or a mail."},
    {"id":"term-stored-copy","term":"Stored copy","definition":"A copy of tenant data kept outside the record that owns it, for reads, for backup, for transfer or for a grant: a view copy, an edge copy, a backup image, an export, a move replica or a support view. Each copy declares its owner, key, freshness bound and erasure point."},
    {"id":"term-shared-copy","term":"Shared copy","definition":"a stored copy served as stored to more than one reader."},
    {"id":"term-audience-class","term":"Audience class","definition":"the set of principals that a tenant's policies cannot tell apart for a given read."},
    {"id":"term-freshness-bound","term":"Freshness bound","definition":"the longest time a stored copy may differ from its source."},
    {"id":"term-erasure-point","term":"Erasure point","definition":"the moment by which a deletion has reached a stored copy."},
    {"id":"term-surrogate-key","term":"Surrogate key","definition":"a label on an edge copy by which it can be purged."},
    {"id":"term-edge-copy","term":"Edge copy","definition":"a stored copy held by the content delivery network."},
    {"id":"term-operation","term":"Operation","definition":"a named capability with an input schema, listed in the operation catalogue."},
    {"id":"term-operation-catalogue","term":"Operation catalogue","definition":"the machine-readable list of every operation, generated from platform code and tenant metadata."},
    {"id":"term-proposal","term":"Proposal","definition":"a change submitted for approval together with its projection."},
    {"id":"term-projection","term":"Projection","definition":"the result of replaying recorded or generated activity with and without a proposed change, and comparing."},
    {"id":"term-audit-log","term":"Audit log","definition":"the append-only, hash-chained record of security-relevant actions."},
    {"id":"term-correlation-identifier","term":"Correlation identifier","definition":"the value that ties together every record of one request."},
    {"id":"term-seam","term":"Seam","definition":"a boundary to infrastructure expressed as a contract with a conformance suite and adapters."},
    {"id":"term-adapter","term":"Adapter","definition":"an implementation of a seam for one piece of infrastructure."},
    {"id":"term-sandbox-tenant","term":"Sandbox tenant","definition":"a tenant started from a template by a new organisation, which its owner keeps or lets expire."},
    {"id":"term-staging-tenant","term":"Staging tenant","definition":"a tenant where configuration is prepared before it is promoted to its production tenant. This is a tenant, and it is not the stage environment, which is a platform environment."},
    {"id":"term-environment","term":"Environment","definition":"A platform environment: the local stack, the stage environment or the production environment, each built from the same definitions. A tenant's kind (production, staging or sandbox) is not an environment."},
    {"id":"term-draft","term":"Draft","definition":"a version of a record that is not yet published and that readers do not see."},
    {"id":"term-preview-link","term":"Preview link","definition":"an expiring address that shows one draft version of one record to a reader without an account."},
    {"id":"term-delivery-key","term":"Delivery key","definition":"a service account whose only permission is to read the published content of one site for one audience class."},
    {"id":"term-support-grant","term":"Support grant","definition":"A time-limited permission that a tenant owner issues to a platform operator for work in the tenant. It is called an access grant in the data model, and a break-glass grant is a support grant issued in an emergency, with the same fields."},
    {"id":"term-notice","term":"Notice","definition":"a message about an event, sent by email or placed in an inbox, to a person who subscribed to it."},
    {"id":"term-inbox","term":"Inbox","definition":"the list of tasks and notices shown to one person in the platform."},
    {"id":"term-plan","term":"Plan","definition":"the set of quotas, trial terms and objectives that apply to a tenant."},
    {"id":"term-quota","term":"Quota","definition":"a limit on one metered quantity of a tenant, stated by its plan."},
    {"id":"term-webhook","term":"Webhook","definition":"an HTTP delivery of an event to an address, signed with a shared secret."},
    {"id":"term-redirect","term":"Redirect","definition":"a stored answer that sends a request for a former address to the current address of a page."},
    {"id":"term-submission","term":"Submission","definition":"the data a reader sends through a form on a site, stored as a record of the tenant."},
    {"id":"term-search-index","term":"Search index","definition":"the entries of one tenant from which its search queries are answered."},
    {"id":"term-archive","term":"Archive","definition":"a document with a manifest that holds the records, files or configuration of a tenant for export."},
    {"id":"term-assistant","term":"Assistant","definition":"a program that proposes changes and answers questions in a conversation, acting for one person with that person's delegated token."},
    {"id":"term-conversation","term":"Conversation","definition":"an ordered set of turns between one person and the assistant, kept as tenant data."},
    {"id":"term-turn","term":"Turn","definition":"one message of a conversation, from the person or from the assistant, with the replies and operations it produced."},
    {"id":"term-preview","term":"Preview","definition":"the projection of a proposed change, shown before the change is applied."},
    {"id":"term-confirmation","term":"Confirmation","definition":"the person's explicit answer to a preview, bound to that preview."},
    {"id":"term-pending-action","term":"Pending action","definition":"a proposed change waiting for a preview, a confirmation or an approval."},
    {"id":"term-model-provider","term":"Model provider","definition":"the service that generates a reply from messages and operation descriptions, reached through the model provider contract."},
    {"id":"term-content-token","term":"Content token","definition":"a name that a tenant defines, with an expression that gives its value when content or an email is rendered for a reader. Not an access token."},
    {"id":"term-mail-dispatcher","term":"Mail dispatcher","definition":"the component that renders each message and hands it to the mail provider through the mail contract."},
    {"id":"term-suppression-list","term":"Suppression list","definition":"the addresses of a tenant that bounced for good, complained or unsubscribed, to which no further mail is sent."},
    {"id":"term-sender-domain","term":"Sender domain","definition":"a domain that a tenant has proved control of and sends mail from."},
    {"id":"term-trust-level","term":"Trust level","definition":"the mark on data handed to an agent that says who wrote it: the platform, a principal of the tenant, or a source outside the tenant."},
    {"id":"term-blue","term":"Blue","definition":"One of the two colours of a component in production. Blue and green alternate: each release deploys into the colour that is not live, and a colour switch makes it live."},
    {"id":"term-green","term":"Green","definition":"The other colour of a component in production. A release deploys into green while blue is live, and into blue while green is live."},
    {"id":"term-colour-switch","term":"Colour switch","definition":"The change of the colour that takes public traffic, made at the traffic switch by the release controller, and its reverse, the switch back."},
    {"id":"term-stage-environment","term":"Stage environment","definition":"The platform's pre-production environment, made from the same definitions as production with its own accounts, where each release is verified before it is promoted. It holds synthetic or scrubbed tenants and no personal data of a production tenant. It is not a staging tenant (ADM-157)."},
    {"id":"term-production-environment","term":"Production environment","definition":"The platform's live environment, made from the same definitions as the stage environment and changed only through release records and audited operations. It holds the production tenants and is not one of them."},
    {"id":"term-migration-run","term":"Migration run","definition":"A sequence of kernel decisions that carries one tenant's records from one schema version to another, applied in one transition or in batches, with a cursor and a record of each batch."},
    {"id":"term-kernel","term":"Kernel","definition":"the pure decision functions of the platform: they decide an intent, answer a read and plan the state a decision needs, with no input, output, clock or randomness of their own."},
    {"id":"term-effect","term":"Effect","definition":"an external action that a decision describes as data, such as a call, a mail or a purge, carried out by an adapter after the transaction that decided it commits."},
    {"id":"term-grant","term":"Grant","definition":"a record that gives a principal a permission for a stated purpose, with an expiry and a revocation. A support grant, a delegation and a grant of roles are grants, and a token issued from a grant carries no more than the grant does."},
    {"id":"term-erasure","term":"Erasure","definition":"the removal of one person's personal data from every record and copy that holds it, by deletion or by destroying the subject key that seals it."},
    {"id":"term-retention","term":"Retention","definition":"the period for which a record or copy is kept, set per record type by the tenant policy within the platform's bounds, after which it is removed."},
    {"id":"term-legal-hold","term":"Legal hold","definition":"a tenant's instruction to keep the records it names, which suspends their erasure and expiry until it is lifted."},
    {"id":"term-subject-key","term":"Subject key","definition":"the key under which one person's personal fields are sealed. Destroying it makes those fields unreadable in every copy and backup."},
    {"id":"term-personal-data","term":"Personal data","definition":"a value that identifies a person, or that identifies one together with other values, held in a field that the data model marks as personal."},
    {"id":"term-layout","term":"Layout","definition":"the stored structure of a tenant database or of the control database, its tables, indexes and encodings, which changes from one version to the next."},
    {"id":"term-outbox","term":"Outbox","definition":"the events that a commit leaves for publication, published in commit order by one job per tenant."},
    {"id":"term-intent","term":"Intent","definition":"a request to change a tenant, which the kernel decides. An intent that may be repeated carries an idempotency key."},
    {"id":"term-revision","term":"Revision","definition":"the count of accepted transitions of a tenant. Each accepted transition advances it by one."},
    {"id":"term-journal","term":"Journal","definition":"the ordered record of a tenant's accepted transitions, from which its state is replayed and checked against its state hash."},
    {"id":"term-state-hash","term":"State hash","definition":"the canonical hash of a tenant's state, which a restore, a move, an export and a replay must reproduce."},
    {"id":"term-budget","term":"Budget","definition":"a stated limit on a measured quantity, verified by a recorded measurement that its row in the budget measurement table describes."},
    {"id":"term-halt","term":"Halt","definition":"the stopping of an agent: its requests are refused until a principal other than the agent resumes it. The kill switch is an operator's halt of an agent."},
    {"id":"term-tenant-metadata","term":"Tenant metadata","definition":"the definitions a tenant holds as data, such as its schema, views, workflows, templates, tokens and flags. They are stored under a schema version and changed through audited kernel intents."},
    {"id":"term-template","term":"Template","definition":"a platform-authored bundle of tenant metadata that a tenant installs after reviewing its projection."},
    {"id":"term-request-token","term":"Request token","definition":"the token that the gateway issues to a browser and requires on each state-changing request, against requests forged from another site."},
    {"id":"term-submission-token","term":"Submission token","definition":"the token that a form issues to the browser that loads it, and that the form requires on each submission."},
    {"id":"term-theme-token","term":"Theme token","definition":"a named value of a site's theme, such as a colour or a size, which a tenant selects from the token schema without supplying style."},
    {"id":"term-canary","term":"Canary","definition":"a small share of public requests sent to a new colour for a stated period before the full share (REL-565)."},
    {"id":"term-token","term":"Token","definition":"the bare word names none of the tokens in this glossary. Say access token, content token, fencing token (the lease token of a job), request token, submission token, or theme token."},
    {"id":"term-release-record","term":"Release record","definition":"The data that states what one release deployed: its commit, the digests of its images, the results of its gates, its approvals, its rollback class and the colour it made live."},
    {"id":"term-tick","term":"Tick","definition":"the unit of logical time in a behaviour model. One tick stands for one minute for the bounds that a requirement or decision states in minutes (a-tick); a gap of a few ticks between messages is an order, not a duration."},
    {"id":"term-segment","term":"Segment","definition":"a saved predicate over the people of a tenant, with a name, whose membership the kernel keeps current and whose entries and exits are domain events."},
    {"id":"term-segment-membership","term":"Segment membership","definition":"the fact that one person satisfies the predicate of one segment under a stated version of it, held as a record that carries no field of the person."},
    {"id":"term-refresh-interval","term":"Refresh interval","definition":"the time between two refresh jobs of a segment whose predicate reads the time; the bound by which its membership may lag behind the predicate."},
    {"id":"term-setting","term":"Setting","definition":"A named, typed value with a default, which the platform, the tenant, a team and a person can each override at the levels its definition allows. A read for a principal returns the most specific permitted override (D-5041)."},
    {"id":"term-override","term":"Override","definition":"The value of a setting at one level for one subject: the platform, the tenant, a team or a person. Removing it makes a read fall back to the next level."},
    {"id":"term-aggregate","term":"Aggregate","definition":"A count, sum, minimum, maximum or top list that a named query declares over its declared fields, optionally grouped by one of them, and that is computed over the records the reader may read (D-5060, D-5061)."},
    {"id":"term-automation","term":"Automation","definition":"a workflow of named steps from the published step catalogue, held as tenant metadata and run by the automation worker under the authority of its automation principal."},
    {"id":"term-automation-principal","term":"Automation principal","definition":"the principal automation:<workflow-id> that every step of an automation acts as, holding the roles of its run-as and nothing its definer may not confer."}
  ],

