      "name": "An event committed by another writer is published by the idle sweep (implementation)",
      "description": "The backend calls the commit hook once at start-up and the kick publishes at once; from then on the machine is idle and no commit hook of this runtime runs. The idle sweep fires at 501 ms and again at 1001 ms, so an event another writer committed in between is published within 500 ms. Times are in milliseconds. The same scenario run on the implementation machines.",
      "behaviors": [
