          "type": "timestamp",
          "description": "The earliest time a job of the tenant is due or a lease of it expires."
        },
        {
          "name": "touched",
          "type": "u64",
          "description": "Raised by every write, so that a refresh never overwrites a time another writer lowered after the refresh read it."
        }
      ],
      "retention": "As long as the tenant has an open job: the row is removed when the tenant has none, and with the tenant directory row by cascade.",
      "erasure": {
        "point": "the tenant has no open job, or its directory row is deleted"
      },
      "description": "Table job_wake of the control database: the wake index of the automation worker (SCH-007, SCH-008). It holds a tenant id and a due time per tenant with open jobs and nothing of a job, so that due work is found without opening the file of a tenant that has none."
    },
    {
      "id": "rec-segment-event",
