    {
      "id": "grant-allows",
      "description": "rules.rs holds_policy_power, the part that asks the role permissions: whether a grant is the object grant of the object type and the verb that the action names on the resource (an action that is manage, or a resource that is not an object type, has none).",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "g",
          "type": "grant"
        },
        {
          "name": "act",
          "type": "action"
        },
        {
          "name": "res",
          "type": "resource"
        }
      ],
      "returns": "bool",
      "body": "match g { capability(_) => false, object{object, action} => (match res { object(o) => o == object, _ => false }) && (match act { read => action == object-action.read, create => action == object-action.create, update => action == object-action.update, delete => action == object-action.delete, manage => false }) }",
      "examples": [
        {
          "description": "The grant of the object type and the verb.",
          "args": {
            "g": {
              "object": {
                "object": "note",
                "action": "update"
              }
            },
            "act": "update",
            "res": {
              "object": "note"
            }
          },
          "result": true
        },
        {
          "description": "Another verb is not it.",
          "args": {
            "g": {
              "object": {
                "object": "note",
                "action": "read"
              }
            },
            "act": "update",
            "res": {
              "object": "note"
            }
          },
          "result": false
        },
        {
          "description": "A capability grants no object action.",
          "args": {
            "g": {
              "capability": "content-write"
            },
            "act": "read",
            "res": {
              "object": "note"
            }
          },
          "result": false
        },
        {
          "description": "Read, create and delete are each the verb of the grant of the same name.",
          "args": {
            "g": {
              "object": {
                "object": "note",
                "action": "read"
              }
            },
            "act": "read",
            "res": {
              "object": "note"
            }
          },
          "result": true
        },
        {
          "description": "Create.",
          "args": {
            "g": {
              "object": {
                "object": "note",
                "action": "create"
              }
            },
            "act": "create",
            "res": {
              "object": "note"
            }
          },
          "result": true
        },
        {
          "description": "Delete.",
          "args": {
            "g": {
              "object": {
                "object": "note",
                "action": "delete"
              }
            },
            "act": "delete",
            "res": {
              "object": "note"
            }
          },
          "result": true
        },
        {
          "description": "Manage names no object verb, even on an object type.",
          "args": {
            "g": {
              "object": {
                "object": "note",
                "action": "read"
              }
            },
            "act": "manage",
            "res": {
              "object": "note"
            }
          },
          "result": false
        },
        {
          "description": "Manage names no object verb.",
          "args": {
            "g": {
              "object": {
                "object": "note",
                "action": "read"
              }
            },
            "act": "manage",
            "res": "members"
          },
          "result": false
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "holds-policy-power",
      "description": "rules.rs holds_policy_power: whether a principal holds the power one policy of a role confers, the action on the resource under the condition. The owner holds every power. Otherwise it holds it through a permission of one of its roles on the object type (grant-allows), or through a policy of one of its roles that names the action, reaches the resource (AnyObject covers every Object) and is either unconditional or carries the very same condition: two different conditions cannot be compared, so the wider one is not assumed to include the other.",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "tenant",
          "type": "tenant-state"
        },
        {
          "name": "principal",
          "type": "principal"
        },
        {
          "name": "act",
          "type": "action"
        },
        {
          "name": "res",
          "type": "resource"
        },
        {
          "name": "cond",
          "type": "option<expr>"
        }
      ],
      "returns": "bool",
      "let": [
        {
          "name": "roles",
          "expr": "call roles-of(tenant, principal)"
        }
      ],
      "body": "any(r in roles, r == 'owner') || any(g in call effective-permissions(tenant, principal), call grant-allows(g, act, res)) || any(p in values(tenant.schema.policies), any(r in roles, r == p.role) && any(a in p.actions, a == act) && (match p.resource { any-object => match res { object(_) => true, _ => p.resource == res }, _ => p.resource == res }) && (p.condition == null || p.condition == cond))",
      "examples": [
        {
          "description": "The owner holds every power.",
          "args": {
            "tenant": {
              "fixture": "fx-tenant-state-14"
            },
            "principal": {
              "user": "alpha:owner"
            },
            "act": "delete",
            "res": {
              "object": "note"
            },
            "cond": null
          },
          "result": true
        },
        {
          "description": "A principal holds a power through an unconditional policy of its role that names the action on the object type.",
          "args": {
            "tenant": {
              "fixture": "fx-tenant-state-17"
            },
            "principal": {
              "user": "alpha:writer1"
            },
            "act": "update",
            "res": {
              "object": "note"
            },
            "cond": null
          },
          "result": true
        },
        {
          "description": "A principal that holds no policy and no permission for the action does not hold it.",
          "args": {
            "tenant": {
              "fixture": "fx-tenant-state-17"
            },
            "principal": {
              "user": "alpha:writer1"
            },
            "act": "delete",
            "res": {
              "object": "note"
            },
            "cond": null
          },
          "result": false
        },
        {
          "description": "A policy on every object type covers an object type.",
          "args": {
            "tenant": {
              "fixture": "fx-tenant-state-18"
            },
            "principal": {
              "user": "alpha:writer1"
            },
            "act": "update",
            "res": {
              "object": "note"
            },
            "cond": null
          },
          "result": true
        },
        {
          "description": "A permission on the object type gives the power, with no policy.",
          "args": {
            "tenant": {
              "fixture": "fx-tenant-state-19"
            },
            "principal": {
              "user": "alpha:writer1"
            },
            "act": "update",
            "res": {
              "object": "note"
            },
            "cond": null
          },
          "result": true
        },
        {
          "description": "A conditional policy gives the power only for the very same condition.",
          "args": {
            "tenant": {
              "fixture": "fx-tenant-state-20"
            },
            "principal": {
              "user": "alpha:writer1"
            },
            "act": "update",
            "res": {
              "object": "note"
            },
            "cond": {
              "is-null": {
                "var": {
                  "scope": "new",
                  "field": "published_at"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "result": true
        },
        {
          "description": "A conditional policy does not give the power unconditionally.",
          "args": {
            "tenant": {
              "fixture": "fx-tenant-state-20"
            },
            "principal": {
              "user": "alpha:writer1"
            },
            "act": "update",
            "res": {
              "object": "note"
            },
            "cond": null
          },
          "result": false
        },
        {
          "description": "Manage on the members has no object verb, so only a policy gives it.",
          "args": {
            "tenant": {
              "fixture": "fx-tenant-state-19"
            },
            "principal": {
              "user": "alpha:writer1"
            },
            "act": "manage",
            "res": "members",
            "cond": null
          },
          "result": false
        },
        {
          "description": "A policy on every object type does not cover a resource that is not an object type.",
          "args": {
            "tenant": {
              "fixture": "fx-tenant-state-18"
            },
            "principal": {
              "user": "alpha:writer1"
            },
            "act": "update",
            "res": "schema",
            "cond": null
          },
          "result": false
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "effective-owners",
      "description": "transition.rs effective_owners: the principals who hold owner in effect, directly or through a team: every principal of the table of members or of a team whose assigned-roles include owner.",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "members",
          "type": "map<principal-id, set<role-id>>"
        },
        {
          "name": "schema",
          "type": "tenant-schema"
        }
      ],
      "returns": "list<principal-id>",
      "body": "filter(p in call principal-set-of(concat(keys(members), fold(t in values(call teams-of(schema)), acc = [], concat(acc, t.members)))), any(r in call assigned-roles(members, schema, p), r == 'owner'))",
      "examples": [
        {
          "description": "A direct owner.",
          "args": {
            "members": {
              "alpha:owner": [
                "owner"
              ],
              "alpha:writer1": [
                "writer"
              ]
            },
            "schema": {
              "version": 1,
              "objects": {},
              "roles": {},
              "policies": {},
              "workflows": {},
              "queries": {},
              "views": {}
            }
          },
          "result": [
            "alpha:owner"
          ]
        },
        {
          "description": "A member of a team that holds owner is an owner in effect, with no assignment of its own.",
          "args": {
            "members": {
              "alpha:owner": [
                "owner"
              ]
            },
            "schema": {
              "version": 1,
              "objects": {},
              "roles": {},
              "policies": {},
              "workflows": {},
              "queries": {},
              "views": {},
              "teams": {
                "desk": {
                  "id": "desk",
                  "label": "Desk",
                  "members": [
                    "alpha:guest"
                  ],
                  "roles": [
                    "owner"
                  ]
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "result": [
            "alpha:guest",
            "alpha:owner"
          ]
        },
        {
          "description": "A tenant with no owner has none.",
          "args": {
            "members": {
              "alpha:writer1": [
                "writer"
              ]
            },
            "schema": {
              "version": 1,
              "objects": {},
              "roles": {},
              "policies": {},
              "workflows": {},
              "queries": {},
              "views": {}
            }
          },
          "result": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "owner-lost",
      "description": "transition.rs require_an_owner_remains, as a test: whether a change leaves a tenant with no owner that had one. A tenant that has no owner before the change is not made worse by it, so it is not held to this. The members and the schema are the state before and after the change; counting goes through teams as well as direct assignments (effective-owners).",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "before-members",
          "type": "map<principal-id, set<role-id>>"
        },
        {
          "name": "before-schema",
          "type": "tenant-schema"
        },
        {
          "name": "after-members",
          "type": "map<principal-id, set<role-id>>"
        },
        {
          "name": "after-schema",
          "type": "tenant-schema"
        }
      ],
      "returns": "bool",
      "body": "length(call effective-owners(before-members, before-schema)) > 0 && length(call effective-owners(after-members, after-schema)) == 0",
      "examples": [
        {
          "description": "The last direct owner losing owner leaves no owner.",
