    {
      "id": "limit-count-problem",
      "description": "schema.rs TenantSchema::problems, the first loop: a schema that defines more of something than the maximum (object types 200, policies 500, queries 500) is \"limit: <count> <what> is more than the maximum of <max>\".",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "what",
          "type": "string"
        },
        {
          "name": "count",
          "type": "u64"
        },
        {
          "name": "max",
          "type": "u64"
        }
      ],
      "returns": "list<string>",
      "body": "if count > max then [format('limit: {} {} is more than the maximum of {}', count, what, max)] else []",
      "examples": [
        {
          "args": {
            "what": "policies",
            "count": 3,
            "max": 2
          },
          "result": [
            "limit: 3 policies is more than the maximum of 2"
          ]
        },
        {
          "args": {
            "what": "policies",
            "count": 2,
            "max": 2
          },
          "result": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "schema-limit-problems",
      "description": "schema.rs TenantSchema::problems, the limits (limits.rs): more than 200 object types, 500 policies or 500 queries, in that order, then each query (in id order) whose limit is 0 or more than 200 (the largest page): \"limit: query <id> declares a limit outside 1 to 200\".",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "schema",
          "type": "tenant-schema"
        }
      ],
      "returns": "list<string>",
      "body": "concat(concat(concat(call limit-count-problem('object types', length(keys(schema.objects)), 200), call limit-count-problem('policies', length(keys(schema.policies)), 500)), call limit-count-problem('queries', length(keys(schema.queries)), 500)), fold(q in values(schema.queries), ps = [], concat(ps, match q.limit { Some(n) => if n == 0 || n > 200 then [format('limit: query {} declares a limit outside 1 to 200', q.id)] else [], None => [] })))",
      "examples": [
        {
          "description": "A query limit of 0 or above 200 is a problem; 200 and none are not.",
          "args": {
            "schema": {
              "fixture": "fx-tenant-schema-5",
              "with": {
                "queries.a_zero": {
                  "id": "a_zero",
                  "object": "note",
                  "filter": null,
                  "params": [],
                  "order": [],
                  "limit": 0
                },
                "queries.b_ok": {
                  "id": "b_ok",
                  "object": "note",
                  "filter": null,
                  "params": [],
                  "order": [],
                  "limit": 200
                },
                "queries.c_big": {
                  "id": "c_big",
                  "object": "note",
                  "filter": null,
                  "params": [],
                  "order": [],
                  "limit": 201
                },
                "queries.d_none": {
                  "id": "d_none",
                  "object": "note",
                  "filter": null,
                  "params": [],
                  "order": [],
                  "limit": null
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "result": [
            "limit: query a_zero declares a limit outside 1 to 200",
            "limit: query c_big declares a limit outside 1 to 200"
          ]
        },
        {
          "description": "201 object types, 501 policies and 501 queries are each one more than the maximum (limits.rs MAX_OBJECTS, MAX_POLICIES, MAX_QUERIES).",
